-- Notion scripts into the cards (approved by the owner, Nov 16 2026: "yes ... read all weeks").
--
-- Daryna's weeks were imported on Nov 16 from pasted tables, which carry only the table columns. The script,
-- caption, reference notes, facts and questions live inside each Notion row's page, so every imported card came in
-- with an empty Script. This fills them, read from every row page of Noun Naturals Weeks 1 to 4 and Founder Week 1.
--
-- Only data, no schema change. A card is matched by space, week number and title (the nth row of the same title in
-- a week matches the nth such card by row order). Only a card whose Script is still empty is filled, so nothing the
-- team has typed is overwritten, and running it again changes nothing. A database without these weeks (a fresh test
-- database) is left as it is.

with src (space_slug, week_no, title, ord, sections) as (
  values
  ('noun', 1, 'call-out: that silky feeling might be a coating', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 34K views: greenwashing call-out (quats in a \"natural\" conditioner)"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"site (free from silicones); conditioner page (no silicones, no synthetic quats)."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"That silky feeling from your conditioner might just be a coating. Check the label for ingredients ending in -cone, like dimethicone. Those are silicones. They coat the hair so it feels smooth right away, and that coating can build up over time. We don''t use them. No silicones, no quats. When your hair feels soft after ours, that''s your hair."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Soft hair or coated hair? Check for -cone. #nounnaturals #ingredients"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'comment reply: my scalp is dry and itchy', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 44K views: \"Replying to @Jett thank me later brochacho #hairoiling\" Advice reply."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David on customers with flakes and itchy scalp, Oct 5 call, 7:37; \"we never guarantee anything\", 28:00."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"why is my scalp so dry and itchy  and the flakes are NOT going away  what do i even use??"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"First: we never guarantee results. Every scalp is different, and if it''s bad, see a doctor. What I can tell you is what''s in our shampoo and why: black seed oil and turmeric for the scalp, and no sulfates, so it doesn''t strip. A lot of customers tell us the itch and flakes calmed down after they switched. Try it. If it''s not for you, you get your money back."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Replying to @(user) no promises. Here''s what''s in it and why. #noun #scalpcare"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'ingredient truth: patchouli', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 56K views: \"Thinning hair? Try making this oil at home...\" Oil ingredient breakdown."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"hair oil product page (clinical studies of patchouli extract: 31%, 87%)."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"• Can we quote these numbers on camera as an ingredient study?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"There’s patchouli in our hair oil, and it’s not there for the smell.\nMost people know patchouli as a scent. We use it for your scalp. It’s one of the ingredients in there to help with dryness and flaking, so it works next to black seed, pumpkin seed and batana, not instead of them.\nThat’s not a promise for your head. It’s just why it’s in the bottle. Nothing in our formula is there for decoration. Every ingredient has a job."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Every ingredient has a job. #noun #hairoil"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'myth bust: i''m too young to think about my scalp', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 3.6M views: \"Hair products make the biggest difference\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"longevity message, Oct 5 call, 4:40."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"“I’m literally 15 why would I care about my scalp ”"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"You''re going to have this scalp for the next seventy years. The habits you start now are the ones you keep. You don''t need a ten-step routine. You need to stop putting harsh stuff on your head every day and start reading labels. That''s it. Future you says thanks."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Same scalp for the next 70 years. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'our first shampoo didn''t foam', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@nounnaturals/video/7598746232995073335"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Stop buying natural shampoos that don’t foam. Trust me, you won’t miss them, and this is why.\nSo as many of you know, I started this brand because I was losing my hair. And the first shampoo we ever made? It didn’t foam. At all. You’d rub it into your scalp and nothing happened. It didn’t even feel like you were washing your hair.\nBack then every natural shampoo was like that, and the whole industry acted like it was normal. We didn’t. Making a natural shampoo that actually foams became the thing we had to solve.\nHere’s what changed. One: new ways to extract natural ingredients that didn’t exist when we started. Two: our R&D team gets to test new ingredients a year or two before the rest of the market. Three: two plant-based cleansers, decyl glucoside and lauryl glucoside. That’s where the foam comes from. No sulfates.\nTrust me, you’ll feel it from the very first wash: it foams, it cleans, and your hair doesn’t come out stripped."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Why Natural Shampoo Doesn’t Foam (and How We Fixed It)\nLearn why most natural shampoos don’t lather and which plant-based cleansers make a natural shampoo foam without sulfates. Get a real clean, naturally! #nounnaturals #noun"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'what makes our shampoo foam', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 110K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Please record the new videos in a similar style. Keep the core concept and conversational dynamic the same, but use a hair powder product instead:"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"B\tYo, what are you doing?\nA\tWhat do you mean, what am I doing?\nB\tPowder in your hair? You didn’t even wash it. Come on.\nA\tYou don’t know about this glitch?\nB\tNo.\nA\tDude, I’m about to put you on a real day-two hair glitch, all right? This is the secret to skipping a wash.\nB\tWhat is that?\nA\tEspecially if your hair gets greasy, yo. Two, three pumps at the roots. Dry hair only.\nB \tHe’s pumping it like it’s cologne. Whoa. Wait, what?\nB   Mm. That actually works? Are you kidding me?\nA\tDo you not see this volume on my guy? The clay soaks up the oil.\nB\tOh wait, dude, you just put me on."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Are you looking to skip a wash on day two? Make sure your texture powder is made with natural clays that absorb oil, not aerosols or synthetics. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'regular or natural shampoo?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 273K views"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Regular shampoo versus natural shampoo. Let’s compare.\nStarting off with cleansing. Regular shampoos often rely on sulfates like sodium lauryl sulfate, which can strip your scalp of its natural oils, while our natural shampoo uses plant-based cleansers, decyl glucoside and lauryl glucoside, that clean without over-stripping.\nFoam. People think natural shampoo can’t foam, but the right plant-based cleansers lather just as well, so you still get that real clean feeling.\nScalp. Regular shampoos are made to clean and that’s it, while ours adds black seed oil and turmeric to care for your scalp every time you wash.\nScent. Regular shampoos just list “fragrance”, which can be synthetic, while ours is scented with essential oils, peppermint and eucalyptus.\nEveryday use. Harsh shampoos can leave your hair dry when you wash every day, while ours is gentle enough for daily use and safe for color-treated hair.\nThat’s why people who actually read labels choose high-performing natural products like Noun."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Regular or natural shampoo? Which is better? #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'live', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@nounnaturals/video/7668820334325320973"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Is Noun live tonight? Yes. (TIME). Bring your questions, bring your shampoo bottle, bring the friend who says natural doesn''t work. We read labels, we answer everything, and there''s a flash sale you only get on the live. See you at (TIME)."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Is Noun live tonight? Yes. (TIME) ET. #noun #nounnaturals #tiktoklive"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'there''s glacier in your hair', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 31K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments screenshots"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"“I’ve tried so many texture powders and they all make my hair feel weird and look dusty. been using this one for a bit and my hair actually has volume for once without feeling like I dumped a whole bottle of product on it | . plus it doesn’t make my hair all stiff and greasy looking. lowkey didn’t expect this to work as well as it does”"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Look what this guy said. [Read the whole comment.]\nThat’s exactly why we made it this way. Our texture powder uses super-fine glacial clay for lightweight volume and a matte finish, plus bentonite clay to absorb oil and add hold. No aerosols, no microplastics. Just minerals doing their thing."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Glacial clay + volcanic clay. That''s the formula. #nounnaturals #texturepowder"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'comment reply: do you have anything for curly hair yet?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 104K views: \"New Samples of our 100% natural high performing curl cream and leave in are in\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: no curl styling yet, Oct 5 call, 12:36; shampoo FAQ (works best for types 1a-3b)."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"waittt do y’all have anything for curly hair yet??"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Our shampoo, conditioner and hair oil are about moisture, and curls need a lot of it, so they work for wavy and looser curls today. What we don''t have yet is curl styling: the curl cream and the leave-in. They''re in sampling. If your curls are very tight, wait for those. We''d rather tell you \"not yet\" than sell you something that wasn''t made for your hair."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Replying to @(user) not yet. Soon. #nounnaturals #curlyhair"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'comment reply: is the shampoo good for wavy hair?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 159K views: \"Is the Noun Shampoo Good for wavy hair? Let''s take a barbers opinon\" Talking-head version of their own video."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Noun''s own video; shampoo product page."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"is the Noun shampoo actually good for wavy hair tho??"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Yes. Here''s why. Wavy hair goes flat when it''s weighed down and frizzy when it''s dried out. Our shampoo has no sulfates, so it doesn''t strip the moisture your waves need, and no silicones to weigh them down. Conditioner on the ends and you''re set. We asked a barber the same question. His answer is on our page."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Replying to @(user) waves need moisture, not weight. #noun #wavyhair"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'live', 2, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@nounnaturals/video/7668820334325320973"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"You, us, and all your haircare questions. Today at 9 PM Eastern. See you on live!"},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Is Noun live tonight? Yes. (TIME) ET. #noun #nounnaturals #tiktoklive"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'we didn''t ask barbers to say this', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 133K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"The original video concept was based on a barber sharing an unsolicited video review of the product. Since we don''t have access to those video testimonials, we''re adapting the concept to a customer review"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"Wasn''t expecting much from a natural texture powder, but this stuff actually works. Great volume, strong hold, and my hair doesn''t feel heavy or sticky. Definitely one of the best powders I''ve tried."},{"heading":"Our reaction to it:","text":"We didn''t ask this customer to say this.\nSomeone tried our texture powder and left this review on their own. No script from us. No one telling them what to say. When we say it''s the highest performing natural texture powder, that''s not us hyping ourselves. It''s feedback like this that shows us we''re doing something right.\nAnd you don''t have to take our word for it. Go check out what our customers are saying."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Barbers are getting their hands on Noun Naturals'' Texture Powder! #noun #barber #texturepowder"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'is it safe for colored hair?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 110K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"Is it safe for colored hair or should I avoid it"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Yes. Our shampoo and conditioner have no sulfates and no silicones, which is what you want for color-treated hair. Same for bleached hair. One thing we always say: every head is different, so we never guarantee a result. If you dye your hair, read our full ingredient list first. It''s all on the site. Nothing hidden."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: color safe. Full ingredient list on the site. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'why should i trust a brand talking about itself?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 32K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"ofc you’re gonna say your own product is good lol"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Honestly, fair. You shouldn’t just take our word for it. Scan our products on Yuka, look at the ingredients, and compare them with what you’re using right now. We want you to know what you’re putting in your hair, even if that means deciding we’re not the right fit for you. Do your research first. Always."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: don''t trust us. Check us. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'read a label in 10 seconds', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 116K views"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"How to read a shampoo label in ten seconds.\nOne: ingredients are listed from most to least, so the first five are most of the bottle.\nTwo: find the cleanser. If it ends in sulfate, you know what you''re dealing with.\nThree: find the word fragrance and see if they tell you the source. Three checks. Do it once in the store and you''ll never shop the same way again."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"3 checks before you buy any shampoo: the first 5 ingredients, the cleanser, the fragrance source. Takes 10 seconds. Save this for your next store run. #nounnaturals #hairtok"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'why there''s turmeric in our shampoo', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 37K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments screenshots"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"Love that you actually put turmeric in the formula and not just on the label. So nice to find a brand that actually delivers what it promises!"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"You’ll see a bunch of brands market their products with all these trendy ingredients, turmeric, this, that, and the third, and then you flip the bottle around and, sure as shit, it’s buried at the bottom of the ingredient list. It’s there for the label, not for your scalp. Thankfully, not us, as someone says here: [Read the whole comment.] - hell, you can even smell it!\nExactly."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Turmeric on the front of the bottle means nothing if it’s buried on the back. Always check where the ingredient sits on the list. #nounnaturals #shampoo"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'it says natural, so it''s natural', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 110K views"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"Come on, if it says natural on the label, it’s natural"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"No. In the US there''s no legal definition of natural for cosmetics. A brand can put one plant extract in a synthetic formula and call it natural. That''s why we talk about standards you can check: ISO 16128 and COSMOS. If the only proof is a leaf on the bottle, that''s a design choice. It''s not proof."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"A leaf on the bottle is a design choice. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'pause this and go get your shampoo', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@based, 1.1M views"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"One of the things I always find interesting is how little people actually know about what''s in their shampoo.\nWe use these products every single day, and most of us probably never even think to turn the bottle around and look at the ingredients.\nSo here''s something I''d love for you to do. Go grab the shampoo you''re currently using, turn it around, and take a look at the second and third ingredients on the label.\nDrop those two ingredients in the comments, even if you have no idea how to pronounce them.\nWe''ll pick some of your comments and actually break down what''s in your shampoo, what those ingredients do, and why they''re there.\nAnd we''re happy to do the exact same thing with our own products. Because I think if we''re confident in what we''re making, we should be just as comfortable talking about what''s inside it."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Second and third ingredient. Comments. Go. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'is this for guys or girls?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 110K views: \"Replying to @Alex Cardenas premium ingredients need premium packaging\" Comment-reply format."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: customer base has always been 50/50, Oct 5 call, 8:15; site FAQ (unisex)."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"No questions. This script is ready to film."},{"heading":"Your possible comment:","text":"why do i only see guys using your products? can girls use them too?"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Both. It always has been. Our customers have been fifty-fifty since day one. You see more guys on our TikTok because that''s who found us here first. The products are unisex: shampoo, conditioner, hair oil, texture powder. Hair is hair. Girls, we see you in the comments. We''re putting more of you on camera."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Replying to @(user) 50/50 since day one. #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'ingredient truth: tree bark', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 31K views: \"Texture, Hold, Volume - ...highest performing natural texture powder\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"texture powder product page (aspen bark extract soothes and balances the scalp)."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"There''s tree bark in our texture powder. Aspen bark extract. It''s there for your scalp: it soothes and it balances. Most styling products are built only for how your hair looks. Ours sits on your scalp all day, so we put something in it for your scalp too. That''s the difference between a styling product and a personal care product."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Styling that thinks about your scalp. #nounnaturals #texturepowder"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'myth bust: natural products don''t smell good', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 34K views: \"CEO approves a scent for a product - guess which product?\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David and Steven on scent profiles and fragrance houses, Oct 5 call, 15:05."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"natural products either smell like NOTHING or straight up a salad"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Not ours. We work with fragrance houses to build scents from natural essential oils. No synthetic fragrance. The shampoo is peppermint and eucalyptus. And the scent on the curl line we''re finishing: everyone who has tested it says the same thing. Nothing like it out there. Natural can smell incredible. It just takes more work."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Natural can smell incredible. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'i have sensitive skin. is it safe for me?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@nounnaturals/video/7607579377508846862"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"waittt I have super sensitive skin"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"That''s something we take seriously.\nOne of the things I''m really proud of is that we use natural essential oils to scent our products instead of synthetic fragrances.\nBut I''ll be honest with you. Natural doesn''t mean everyone''s skin will react the same way. So I''d always recommend checking the full ingredient list on our website first. If you know your skin reacts to something in there, skip it.\nAnd at the end of the day, we stand behind what we make. We''re confident in our products, but we also understand that no product is going to be right for absolutely everyone.\nSo if you give Noun a try and you''re not completely satisfied, just reach out to us. We''ll take care of you. That''s our satisfaction guarantee: your money back."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Natural doesn''t mean nobody reacts. Read the ingredient list first. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'scalp or ends?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Your possible comment:","text":"ok but do i put hair oil on my scalp or just the ends??"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Both. They''re different jobs. On your ends: a few drops on damp or dry hair for frizz, shine and protection. On your scalp it''s a treatment: massage it in before you wash. Same bottle, two uses. Most people only know one of them."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Ends for frizz and shine, scalp before you wash. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'it started with his mom''s oils', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 2.5M views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Tell this to the camera the same way as in the reference: straight to the camera, calm and proud, in your own words."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"I turned my own hair loss into a natural hair care brand, and it all started back in 2017.\nBack then, I was using whatever was on the store shelf and never read a label. But then I started looking at what I was actually putting on my head. No one taught me how to take care of my hair, so I went to my mom. She gave me what her family had always used: natural oils. I started blending my own, and it worked for me.\nI wanted to give people more than a home recipe, so I made products that work every single time, made from natural ingredients. Something real. Thank you for being part of the movement. This is just the beginning."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Why I created Noun. It started with hair loss and my mom''s oils. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'what does your shampoo smell like?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Your possible comment:","text":"what does your shampoo actually smell like?"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Like peppermint and eucalyptus. And that''s the whole list. Most shampoos just write \"fragrance\" on the label, and that one word can hide synthetic scent. Ours is scented with essential oils, and we name them. So next time you smell a shampoo you love, flip it over and check if they tell you where the smell comes from."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Peppermint and eucalyptus essential oils. No \"fragrance\" on our label. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'stop buying hair oils with just one ingredient.', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 56K views"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Stop buying hair oils with just one ingredient. Trust me, you won''t miss them, and this is why.\nSo as many of you know, I started this brand because I was losing my hair. And our hair oil has thirteen botanicals in it, because one oil does one job. One of them you''ve probably never heard of: batana.\nHere''s what it is. One: it comes from the American palm in Honduras. Two: the Miskito people there have used it on their hair for generations. Three: in our formula it''s there for softness, shine and dry, damaged ends, next to black seed, pumpkin seed, rosemary and amla.\nTrust me, your ends will feel the difference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Batana is one of 13 botanicals in our hair oil. It''s there for softness, shine and dry ends. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'oil makes your hair greasy', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 44K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Your possible comment:","text":"isn''t hair oil just gonna make my hair greasy tho"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Only if you use it wrong. Greasy hair from oil is a dose problem. People pour it on like conditioner. It''s two to five drops. Warm it between your palms, then mid-lengths and ends. Still greasy? Use fewer drops next time. Fine hair needs less than thick hair. Start with two. Thank me later."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Greasy hair from oil is a dose problem. Start with two drops. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'men''s health picked it', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 77K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We took one of your videos that performed really well, which shows that the format works, and made a few small adjustments to the script.\nPlease record the new video in a similar style: same two-person skit, B throws the bottle to A. You can change the outfits or the location slightly, but keep the core concept the same."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"B\tYo, what are you doing?\nA\tYo, I''m trying to hydrate my hair.\nB\tBro, what do you mean hydrate? Did you use this today or no?\nA\tWhat is that?\nB\tBro, catch. Come on, knucklehead.\nA\tWhat is this?\nB\tBro, it''s the hair oil. Men''s Health voted it the best black seed hair oil.\nA\tNo way.\nB\tHelps with thickness, strength, shine, fights frizz, even hydrates a little bit. Why haven''t you looked at this yet?\nA\tWhat''s the difference between this and water?\nB\tBro, just shut up and use it, all right?\nA\tAll right."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Men''s Health voted it the best black seed hair oil for a reason. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'frizzy ends', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 71K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We took one of your videos that performed really well, which shows that the format works, and made a few small adjustments to the script.\nPlease record it in a similar style: talk to the camera and show every step on your own hair, the same way you did the hot oil treatment."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Men 17 to 25, if you have frizzy, dry ends, this is what you need to do. You need a hair oil with strong oils like black seed, pumpkin seed and batana. This one came out in 2018 and got reformulated back in 2025 with stronger oils. So, as you guys see, I was losing hair back when I was 17. This is how this whole brand started, by the way.\nYou have frizz, you have dry ends, or your hair just looks dull. This is how you do it. Wash, condition, towel dry. Take about two to five drops in your palm. Rub your palms together to warm it up. Then work it into your mid-lengths and ends while your hair is still damp. Not the roots, just the ends. Bang. That''s it. And if you don''t see any results, I could tell you we''ll give you your money back."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Frizzy ends? 2-5 drops of hair oil on damp mid-lengths and ends, right after you condition. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, '“isn’t this the same as every other natural shampoo?”', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 31K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Your possible comment:","text":"what makes this any different from literally every other natural shampoo?"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"We don’t mind inspiring other brands, bro. But most natural shampoos don’t foam, and ours does, because of two plant-based cleansers: decyl glucoside and lauryl glucoside. No sulfates. If yours doesn’t lather, it’s not the same."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Natural shampoo can foam. Ours does. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'guys don''t need conditioner', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 2.4M views"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"I wash my hair every day, yet I don''t struggle with dry, frizzy hair. Why is this the case?\nWell, it''s not just about which shampoo I''m using, because every shampoo takes some of the natural oils out of your hair when it cleans. What actually matters is what you use after: conditioner. Most guys skip it completely.\nAnd most conditioners that do work rely on quats and silicones. What you need is a conditioner that''s both effective and natural. That''s what we focused on with Noun. No quats, no silicones. Amino acids and brassica oil that still detangle and soften your hair.\nThere are definitely other brands that do this right. Ours just happens to work really well."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Shampoo cleans. Conditioner is what keeps your hair from getting dry and frizzy. Don''t skip it. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'comment reply: i went back to my old brand', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 31K views: \"Replying to @basedkaifanaccount we don''t mind inspiring other brands bro\" Reply to a competitor fan."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Steven and David on \"it didn''t work\" reviews and customers who come back, Oct 5 call, 47:00 to 49:27."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"ngl it didn’t work for me  went straight back to my old brand"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"That''s okay. Seriously. We tell everyone to do their own research and make their own call. One question before you go: how did you use it? Most of the time it''s ten pumps instead of three. If you want to give it one more shot the right way, message us. If not, no hard feelings. A lot of people come back later anyway."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Replying to @(user) no hard feelings. One question though. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'my mom buys my shampoo', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 31K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Your possible comment:","text":"how do i convince my mom to buy me your shampoo instead of my usual one?"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Not letting you down, king. Don''t beg. Show her the label. Hand her the bottle she buys now and pull up our ingredient list. Tell her to scan both in Yuka. Parents care about what goes on your head more than you think. And tell her she can use it too. It''s unisex. That usually closes it."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Don''t beg. Show her both labels. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'hair loss is just genetics', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 37K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable. Please record it in a similar style, with the hair oil in your hand."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"finally a hair brand that doesn''t promise some miracle hair regrowth. been using Noun for a while now and my scalp feels so much better. wish more brands were this honest."},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"You''ll see a bunch of companies market their products for hair loss, saying a bunch of different things, regrowth, this, that, and the third, and then you get it, and sure as shit, it doesn''t work as it''s marketed. Thankfully, not us.\nWe''ll tell you straight. Hair loss is a lot of genetics, and some of it you can''t stop. But your scalp is skin, and what you put on it every day for years matters too. You can''t change your genes. You can stop making it harder for your scalp. And actually, one of our customers said something about this that I really liked. Listen to this. [Reads customer review aloud]\nExactly."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"You can''t change your genes. You can change what you put on your scalp every day. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'we were early', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We took one of your videos that performed well and made a few small adjustments to the script. Please record it in a similar style, with the hair oil in your hand."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Did you know we were the first brand to launch a black seed hair oil, back in 2019? Then five years later, Men''s Health named it the best black seed hair oil. And now black seed oil is in everything. That''s what being early looks like. You do it before anyone cares, and then everyone catches up. We''re doing the same thing right now with a quat-free conditioner."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"We launched a black seed hair oil in 2019. Five years later, Men''s Health named it the best one. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'can girls use the texture powder?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 110K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Your possible comment:","text":"is this texture powder just for guys or can girls use it too?"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Yes. Everything we make is unisex. On long hair: two to three pumps at the roots on dry hair, then lift with your fingers. You get volume at the crown without teasing it and without hairspray. And it buys you an extra day between washes."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Everything we make is unisex. 2-3 pumps at the roots for volume. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'aloe vera juice', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 110K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We took one of your videos that performed really well, which shows that the format works, and made a few small adjustments to the script.\nPlease record the new video in a similar style. You can wear a different robe or slightly change the location, but keep the core concept the same."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"B\tYo, what are you doing?\nA\tWhat do you mean, what am I doing?\nB\tYou''re reading a shampoo bottle? Come on.\nA\tYou don''t know about this glitch?\nB\tNo.\nA\tDude, I''m about to put you on a real label glitch, all right? This is the secret to knowing what''s actually in it.\nB\tWhat is that?\nA\tThe top of the list, yo. That''s what the bottle is mostly made of. Look, aloe vera juice, right up there.\nB\tHe''s reading it like it''s a menu. Whoa. Wait, what?\nB\tMm. Aloe? In shampoo? Are you kidding me?\nA\tHydration, bro. And it helps keep your hair at the pH it likes.\nB\tOh wait, dude, you just put me on."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"The top of the ingredient list is what the bottle is mostly made of. On ours, it''s aloe vera juice. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'reading real reviews', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@nounnaturals/video/7607579377508846862"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Your possible comment:","text":"be fr are these reviews actually real or did y''all write them yourselves"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Fair question. So don''t take it from us. Go to Trustpilot, it''s public. Here''s what people wrote. \"I''ve tried so many natural brands, but Noun Naturals is truly on another level.\" \"Twelfth order because family loves Noun Naturals.\" We didn''t write these, and we can''t edit them. Go check for yourself. And to everyone leaving them: thanks for showing love."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Our reviews are public on Trustpilot. Go read them yourself. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'thank you', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@based, 5.8M views"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"To everyone who defended us in the comments when we weren''t even posting: we saw you. There was a stretch where we went quiet and people were making videos saying our products were trash. We didn''t answer. You did. Customers we''ve never met, explaining our ingredients for us. That''s why we''re still here, and it''s why we go live every night. Thank you. Now tell me what you want us to make next."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"We saw every comment. Thank you. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'i can''t read an ingredient list', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 79K views: \"Exposing the misinformation on this app...\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: customers research with AI and the Yuka app, Oct 5 call, 40:21."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"No questions. This script is ready to film."},{"heading":"Your possible comment:","text":"how am i supposed to know if the ingredients in my shampoo are actually good or bad?"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"You don''t have to. Your phone can. Take a photo of the back of the bottle. Ask ChatGPT what each ingredient does and which ones to watch out for. Or scan the barcode in Yuka. Ten seconds. A lot of our customers found us exactly like that: they checked what they were using, and then they checked us."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Photo. Ask. Ten seconds. #noun #yuka"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'scan it', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nickiesshoppingaddiction, 774K views Picks up a product, scans it with an ingredient app on camera and shows the result on the phone screen. Same idea here: hold up our bottle, scan it, show the screen."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"What score do our shampoo and conditioner get on Yuka? Can we show the scan on camera?\nIs a good Yuka score something you check before a formula goes out? If yes, how do you put it in your own words?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"(Hold up the bottle) Don''t ask us if our shampoo is good for you. Scan it.\n(Scan the barcode with the Yuka app on camera and show the result.)\nYuka is an app. You scan the barcode and it breaks down every ingredient in the product. So scan ours. Then go scan the one in your shower and compare. We don''t hide anything. Every ingredient is on the label, and before anything goes into a formula we check it against our own ingredient blacklist. So don''t take our word for it. Scan it."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Don''t ask us. Scan it. #yuka #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'will your oil fix my hairline?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 71K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We took one of your videos that performed really well, which shows that the format works, and made a few small adjustments to the script. Please record it in a similar style: talk to the camera and do the hot oil treatment on your own hair, step by step."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Men 17 to 25, if your hairline is going back, this is what you need to do. First, I''m not going to lie to you. Genetics are real, and no oil is a medical hair-loss treatment. Ours isn''t either. If you''re losing a lot of hair, see a dermatologist. What you can control is your scalp.\nSo, do a hot oil treatment with strong oils like black seed, pumpkin seed, and batana. This one came out in 2018 and got reformulated back in 2025 with stronger oils. As you guys see, I was losing hair back when I was 17. This is how this whole brand started, by the way.\nThis is how you do it. Put the glass in boiling hot water for about two to three minutes. Do this about 15 to 30 minutes before you shower. Take about five drops and put it right into your scalp. Massage it in. Then after 15 to 30 minutes, hop in the shower. Do this treatment three to four times a week. And if you don''t see any results, we''ll give you your money back."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Hairline going back? Be honest about genetics, and take care of what you can control: your scalp. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'wet or dry hair?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Your possible comment:","text":"does my hair have to be dry before using texture powder or does it work on wet hair too?"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Dry. Always dry. On wet hair the powder just turns into paste and you lose all the grip. Dry your hair first. Then two to three pumps at the roots, and work it in with your fingers. That''s where the volume comes from. Wet hair is for conditioner and oil, dry hair is for powder."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Texture powder goes on dry hair, at the roots. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'rosemary oil, the honest version', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 56K views"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Stop buying rosemary oil just because TikTok told you to. Trust me, you won''t miss it, and this is why.\nSo as many of you know, I started this brand because I was losing my hair. And rosemary oil is everywhere right now, so here''s the honest version.\nOne: it''s been studied for its potential to support hair density. Potential. Two: it''s not magic and it''s not overnight. Three: one ingredient is never the whole answer. That''s why in our hair oil, rosemary sits next to twelve other botanicals, like black seed, pumpkin seed and batana.\nTrust me, what matters more than any single oil is doing your scalp treatment consistently."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Rosemary oil has been studied for its potential to support hair density. Potential, not magic. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 1, 'why we make hair products', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 2.5M views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Tell this to the camera the same way as in the reference: straight to the camera, calm and proud, in your own words."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"We make hair products for your hair ten years from now, not just for tonight.\nBack then, most products were made to make your hair look good for a few hours. But we cared about something different: what your hair looks like five, ten years down the road. Nobody was making styling products that also factor in hair health, so we made them ourselves.\nWe wanted to give people more than a good hair day, so we made products that give you the style you want today, plus a healthy scalp and healthy hair for the long run. That''s harder to make, and it takes longer. Thank you for being part of the movement. This is just the beginning."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Good hair tonight. Good hair in ten years. Styling products should factor in hair health too. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'why is your bottle so small for that price?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@nounnaturals/video/7641324415396908302"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"that tiny bottle for that price is crazy"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Small? Let’s do the math.\nOur hair oil is 4 ounces. Most hair oils on the market come in one. And you only need two to five drops at a time, so one bottle lasts you four to six months.\nSame with everything we make. Our sizes are smaller than the rest of the industry on purpose, because high-performing products don’t need a lot. Two to three pumps of texture powder. Not ten.\nSo before you call it small, check how long it actually lasts. Price per month, not price per bottle."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: One bottle lasts you four to six months. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'natural shampoo isn''t supposed to foam', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@nounnaturals/video/7641324415396908302"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"“wait natural shampoo isn’t even supposed to foam ”"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Who told you that? Somebody sold you a natural shampoo that didn''t lather and then told you that''s how it''s supposed to be. It''s not. Ours is 100% natural and it foams. If yours doesn''t, that''s not nature. That''s a lazy formula. Try ours once and come back to this comment."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Someone sold you a natural shampoo that doesn’t lather and said that’s normal. It’s not. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, '“why does texture powder make my hair clump?”', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 155K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"“Does texture powder make anyone else’s hair clump together, or am I doing something wrong?”"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Will texture powder make my hair clump? Let’s find out.\n[Apply the texture powder and show the result.]\nSee? It’s not the powder. It’s how much you use.\nTwo to three pumps on dry hair. Work it in with your fingers. Need more? Add a little.\nThat’s how you get texture and volume without the clumps."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Less is more when the formula works. #noun #hairtips"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'it clumped up my hair', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@nounnaturals/video/7641324415396908302"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"my hair literally clumped together after using this"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"How many pumps did you use? Because every time we ask, the answer is five. Or ten. It''s two to three. This isn''t a powder you have to dump in. Two to three pumps on dry hair, work it in with your fingers. Need more? Add one. Try it like that. And if you still don''t like it, message us and we''ll make it right."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: 2-3 pumps. Not 10. #noun #texturepowder"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'live', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@based, 3.5M views"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"A: David, who’s on the live right now?\nB: Uh, I’m watching the live right now.\nA: No, no, who’s, like, actually on the camera on the live right now?\nB: Yeah, like, I’m actually on, like, watching him give away shampoo.\nA: Okay, so who’s on the live?\nB: Me.\nA: Okay, you’re watching it. Who’s in front of the camera literally giving away Noun to our followers?\nB: Yeah, so when they join the live, I’m on the live.\nA: But you’re in my office, in front of me, and there’s no camera anywhere. So what’s actually going on?"},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Is Noun live tonight? Yes. (TIME) ET. #noun #nounnaturals #tiktoklive"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'live', 2, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 68K views"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Is Noun live tonight? Yes. (TIME). Tonight it''s all about hair oil: how many drops, scalp or ends, how often, and what to do if your hair gets greasy. Bring any bottle of oil you have at home and we''ll read the label together. (LIVE-ONLY DEAL). See you at (TIME)."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Is Noun live tonight? Yes. (TIME) ET. Hair oil Q&A. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'viral format: sea salt spray or texture powder?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 150K views: \"Sea salt spray or texture clay?\" Same this-or-that hook. Also BlackMask \"Just use sea salt spray\" (2.4M)."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"texture powder product page. Sea salt spray usage is general advice."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"You need to record a voice note up to 3 minutes long answering the questions below. Make sure you provide as many details as possible.\nHow do you recommend using the sea salt spray next to the powder?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Sea salt spray or texture powder? Different jobs. Sea salt spray goes in damp hair, before you dry it. It gives you the base. Texture powder goes in dry hair, at the end. It gives you lift and hold. Best result: both. Spray first, powder last. Our spray has taken two years to get right and it''s almost here. Until then: powder on dry hair, two to three pumps."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Spray first. Powder last. #noun #seasaltspray #texturepowder"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'all you do is hate on other brands', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 79K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"\"All you guys do is hate on other brands.\" We don''t hate. We read labels out loud.\nNow, why am I telling you this? Because next time you see us call out a brand, now you know what''s happening. If a brand says something about its product that isn''t true, we say so, with the ingredient list on screen.\nNow, being loyal to another brand is fine. A lot of people are. But at the end of the day, we''ve never lied about anyone. We just call out the facts.\nAnd hold us to the same rule. Read our labels. If we''re wrong about something, call us out."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Not hate. Facts, with the label on screen. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'let’s talk hold', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@blackmask_shop/video/7663259592935181582?is_from_webapp=1&sender_device=pc"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"What actually keeps your hair in place, and what it costs your scalp #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'founder story: bullied for his hairline', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 2.5M views: \"Why I Created My Hair Products\" Founder-story format."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: \"Khaled used to get bullied for having a receding hairline\", Oct 6 call, 6:25."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Our founder got bullied for his hairline. Eighteen years old, hairline going back, and kids are not nice about that. That''s where this company comes from. Not a business plan. He wanted to fix his own problem, and then help the next kid who looks in the mirror and feels the same way. So when you tell us our products made you more confident, that''s not a review to us. That''s the point."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"That''s the point. #nounnaturals #founderstory"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'how to use it: the two-minute scalp treatment', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views: \"how to get the most out of hair oil for hair and scalp - proper hair oil treatment\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"hair oil product page (scalp treatment before washing, two to three times a week)."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"So how do i even use the oil"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"The two-minute scalp treatment. Two to three times a week. Before you shower: a small amount of hair oil on your fingertips. Part your hair and put it on the scalp, not on the hair. Massage in small circles for two minutes. Then wash as normal. That''s it. People skip the massage, and the massage is half of it."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Two minutes. Before you wash. #nounnaturals #scalpcare"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'proof: we answer every review', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views: \"We''re so confident you''ll love noun... satisfaction or your money back\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com ratings (Trio 4.8 from 967 reviews; hair oil 4.9); Steven replies to reviews daily, Oct 5 call, 46:14."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"4.8 stars from more than 900 reviews. On one product. That''s our Hair Care Trio. The hair oil is at 4.9. We read every review and answer them every day, good and bad. If someone used ten pumps instead of three, we message them and fix it. Reviews aren''t a trophy for us. They''re how we find out what to make better."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"We read all of them. #noun #nounnaturals #reviews"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'viral format: it''s 2026', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 37K views: \"It''s 2026, styling products are supposed to also factor in hair health along with performance\" Remake of their own video."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Noun''s own video caption."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"It''s 2026, and somehow we''re still using styling products that only care about how your hair looks.\nYou''ll see a bunch of brands promising crazy volume, strong hold, perfect texture, this, that, and the third.\nBut then you look at what''s actually in the product, and you''re like, damn, does anyone even care about your hair and scalp?\nThankfully, we do.\n[COMMENT APPEARS ON SCREEN, SPEAKER READS IT]\n\"Didn''t think a natural styling product would actually have this much hold lol. The texture is great and my hair doesn''t feel all stiff and gross afterward. Honestly impressed.\"\n[SPEAKER RESPONDS]\nExactly."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Performance + hair and scalp health. That''s the standard. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'drop: what makes our curl line different?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"your drop video C0001 (founder to camera). Intro type: question about the product, then the answer."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Curl Chemistry sub-brand: curl cream, leave-in, gel and mousse; unisex leaning male; pre-orders planned); your own TikTok caption \"New Samples of our ... curl cream and leave in are in\" (104K); Master Client Context Document (natural, high performing, long-term hair and scalp health; science-backed should be the minimum)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this straight to camera with the product in your hand, same energy as your sea salt spray drop videos. Fast, under 30 seconds."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Which product is this drop for? We wrote it for the curl line (curl cream / leave-in). If it''s a different product, we swap the name.\nHow many units go to early access? We put it in the (NUMBER) spots.\nWhere do people sign up for this drop: the website form or the Discord?\nIs there a release date yet, or do we keep it \"coming soon\"?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold the curl line bottle up to the camera.]\nYou know what''s different about our curl line?\nYes, it''s natural. But natural isn''t the whole point.\nIt''s made to style your curls today and to take care of your hair and scalp in the long run.\nMost curl products only care about how your hair looks by lunch.\nWe want you thinking about your hair long term.\nAnd it''s unisex. So guys, this one''s for you too.\nAsk yourself: is my curl cream just styling me, or is it doing something for my hair?\n(PRODUCT NAME). Coming soon."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Natural, made to perform, and built for the long run. Coming soon. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'drop: only (number) before release', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"your drop video C0005 (founder to camera). Intro type: exact number as the hook."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Curl Chemistry sub-brand: curl cream, leave-in, gel and mousse; unisex leaning male; pre-orders planned); your own TikTok caption \"New Samples of our ... curl cream and leave in are in\" (104K); your drop videos C0003 and C0004 (sign up on nounnaturals.com through the pop-up form or the homepage button; list members hear first by email and text; early access before the official release date)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this straight to camera with the product in your hand, same energy as your sea salt spray drop videos. Fast, under 30 seconds."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Which product is this drop for? We wrote it for the curl line (curl cream / leave-in). If it''s a different product, we swap the name.\nHow many units go to early access? We put it in the (NUMBER) spots.\nWhere do people sign up for this drop: the website form or the Discord?\nIs there a release date yet, or do we keep it \"coming soon\"?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"(NUMBER). Not one more, not one less.\nThat''s how many (PRODUCT NAME) go out before the official release.\nAnd they only go to the people on our early access list.\n[Point down at the caption.]\nGo to nounnaturals.com and fill out the form that pops up.\nClosed it too fast? There''s a button right on the homepage.\nEveryone else waits for the release date.\nDon''t be everyone else."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Only (NUMBER) before the official release. Get on the list at nounnaturals.com. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'stop doing this!', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 332K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate a video similar to the reference, including the process."},{"heading":"Hook:","text":"STOP DOING THIS!\nStart by awkwardly brushing your hair to create a messy, unflattering look.\nDemonstrate your hairstyling routine using NOUNNATURALS products, showing each step.\nReveal the final hairstyle.\nHold the products up to the camera to show what you used."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Stop doing this! #hairtutorial #hairstyles #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'one of our competitors had his customers buy our products, return them, and send back boxes full of rocks.', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 79K views"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"One of our competitors had his customers buy our products, return them, and send back boxes full of rocks. Guess what we did about it? (WHAT YOU DID)\nNow, why am I telling you this? Because next time you see a one-star review on our page, posted the day after delivery with no context, now you know where some of them come from.\nNow, being loyal to another brand is fine. A lot of people are. But at the end of the day, don’t buy a product just to fake a return and leave a one-star review.\nIf you actually had a problem with our product, we take care of you. Allergic reaction? We refund you. Used ten pumps instead of three? We message you and fix it. We reply to reviews every single day.\nBut they’re doing it anyway, first, because they’re that loyal to another brand. Second, because they want to make us look bad.\nKeep sending us boxes of rocks. Our customers will keep answering for us. And to the brand behind it: no one’s gonna respond to you, bro."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Not every one-star review is real. Some of them come with a box of rocks. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'how to make sulfate-free shampoo lather?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@rhymeandreason.haircare/video/7276479633132883232"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"How to make sulfate-free shampoo lather?   #nounnaturals #noun"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'call-out: a great barber is not a chemist', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 116K views: \"Stick to being a Tik Tok barber if you''re going to cheap out on formulas\" Remake of their own call-out."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Noun''s own video caption."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Should this stay general, or do you want to answer a specific creator?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"A great barber is not a chemist. Respect to barbers. Cutting hair is a skill. Formulating a product is a different job. So when a barber, or any creator, puts his name on a product, ask one thing: who formulated it, and what''s in it? If the formula is cheap, the name on the front doesn''t fix it. We let barbers do the reviewing. We do the chemistry."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Who formulated it? #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'ingredient truth: the volcano in your texture powder', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 31K views: \"Texture, Hold, Volume - ...highest performing natural texture powder\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"texture powder product page (bentonite, a volcanic clay, for hold, oil absorption, structure, lift)."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"There''s a volcano in your texture powder. Bentonite is a clay that comes from volcanic ash. It does two things in our powder: it absorbs oil, and it gives hair structure so it holds its shape. That''s where the hold comes from. Not a spray. A clay. Paired with glacial clay and silica, it''s why two to three pumps is enough."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Volcanic clay does the holding. #nounnaturals #texturepowder"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'lab update: the curl line', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 60K views: \"The market has never saw something like this... noun natural curl chemistry line\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Noun''s own video; David on the scent, Oct 5 call, 15:05."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"What can we say about the curl cream and the leave-in: names and timing?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"sooo when are y’all finally gonna drop something for curly hair"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"We''ve been working on a curl line for years. The market hasn''t seen anything like it. A curl cream and a leave-in. 100% natural and built to perform. And the scent: everyone who has tested it says the same thing. Nothing like it out there. Samples are in. We''re not giving a date until it''s right. Curly heads, we didn''t forget you."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Curl cream + leave-in. Samples are in. #nounnaturals #curlyhair"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'myth bust: natural products don''t hold', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 135K views: \"Natural is the base line, performance is the differentiator\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"main belief to break, Oct 6 call, 17:11; barber reviews of the powder (133K)."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"Bruh natural products doesn’t hold unc"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"They didn''t use to. That reputation was earned. Old natural styling products were weak. What changed is the ingredients: clays and minerals that grip the hair without synthetics. Our texture powder is 100% natural and it holds all day on two to three pumps. Don''t believe me. Barbers tested it on camera."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"That reputation is out of date. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'proof: 95% of barbers said pump', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 75K views: \"...Over 95% of barbers and stylist we surveyed prefer the pump for a reason\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Noun''s own video caption."},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@blackmask_shop/video/7696983447331458318?is_from_webapp=1&sender_device=pc&web_id=7698338633555920404"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Over 95% of barbers and stylists we surveyed prefer the pump. #texturepowder #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'drop: want the curl line before everyone else?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"your drop video C0004 (founder to camera). Intro type: direct question to the viewer."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Curl Chemistry sub-brand: curl cream, leave-in, gel and mousse; unisex leaning male; pre-orders planned); your own TikTok caption \"New Samples of our ... curl cream and leave in are in\" (104K); your drop videos C0005 and C0007 (early access through the Discord, discord.gg/noun, link in the caption)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this straight to camera with the product in your hand, same energy as your sea salt spray drop videos. Fast, under 30 seconds."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Which product is this drop for? We wrote it for the curl line (curl cream / leave-in). If it''s a different product, we swap the name.\nHow many units go to early access? We put it in the (NUMBER) spots.\nWhere do people sign up for this drop: the website form or the Discord?\nIs there a release date yet, or do we keep it \"coming soon\"?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Want the curl line before anyone else gets it?\nJoin our Discord. discord.gg/noun. The link''s in the caption.\nThat''s where the early access form goes up first.\n(NUMBER) units go out before the official release date. That''s it.\nWhen they''re gone, you wait like everybody else.\nSo join now and be ready."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Early access to the curl line starts in our Discord. discord.gg/noun #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'drop: it''s 2026, your curl cream should do more', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"your drop videos C0002 clips 1 to 3 (founder to camera). Intro type: \"It''s 2026, your X should...\"."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Curl Chemistry sub-brand: curl cream, leave-in, gel and mousse; unisex leaning male; pre-orders planned); your own TikTok caption \"New Samples of our ... curl cream and leave in are in\" (104K); Master Client Context Document (natural, high performing, long-term hair and scalp health; science-backed should be the minimum)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this straight to camera with the product in your hand, same energy as your sea salt spray drop videos. Fast, under 30 seconds."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Which product is this drop for? We wrote it for the curl line (curl cream). If it''s a different product, we swap the name.\nHow many units go to early access? We put it in the (NUMBER) spots.\nWhere do people sign up for this drop: the website form or the Discord?\nIs there a release date yet, or do we keep it \"coming soon\"?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold the curl line bottle up to the camera.]\nIt''s 2026. Your curl cream should do more than hold a curl for a few hours.\nIt should be natural. It should perform.\nAnd it should be good for your hair and scalp in the long run.\nNot a list of trendy ingredients on a pretty label.\nThat''s the bar we built our curl line to.\n(PRODUCT NAME). Coming soon."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"It''s 2026. Your curl cream should do more. Coming soon. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'we''re sampling a hair clay', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 34K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference. No talking or script is needed."},{"heading":"TO-DO LIST","text":"Start with slightly messy, unstyled hair.\nTake the hair powder product and show it to the camera.\nApply a small amount of product to your hair.\nUse one smooth hand movement to distribute the product and style your hair.\nShow the final result, highlighting the transformation from messy hair to a clean, textured style."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Sampling something new #nounnaturals #hairclay"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'my hair is straight and flat, nothing works', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@nounnaturals/video/7641324415396908302"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"i swear my hair just refuses to have volume"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Flat hair needs two things: lift at the root and grip in the strands. Start with completely dry hair. Two to three pumps of texture powder at the roots, then push your hair up with your fingers. The clay absorbs oil and gives your hair texture and lift, so it stays up. No stiffness, no shine. Straight hair isn''t the problem. Product that weighs it down is."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: straight hair isn''t the problem. #nounnaturals #straighthair"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'don’t make homemade hair growth oil!', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@typehairofficial/video/7605065775782563102?is_from_webapp=1&sender_device=pc"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Don’t make homemade hair growth oil!  #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'the wavy hair routine', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 1.3M views: \"Straight to wavy hair tutorial in 5 steps!\" Numbered-steps format."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"product pages; Noun''s wavy hair video (159K)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"The full script will be displayed on screen, so you don’t need to say anything out loud. Just follow the script and demonstrate everything visually, similar to the reference.\nVisual hook: Point your finger at the camera to grab attention.\nShow your starting point: Show your hair before styling, emphasizing that you want to make it look more textured and messy.\nDemonstrate your routine: Go through your entire hair routine, showing each step as you go.\nShow the products: Clearly show each product you’re using alongside the corresponding step.\nFinal result: Reveal your finished hairstyle, highlighting the texture and messy look."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"The wavy hair routine. Three steps. One: sulfate-free shampoo on the scalp. Two: conditioner on the mid-lengths and ends, then rinse. Three: let it dry, and once it''s dry, two pumps of texture powder at the roots if you want volume. That''s it. Waves need moisture and a light product. Nothing heavy."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Wash. Condition. Two pumps. #nounnaturals #wavyhair"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'call-out: best marketing is not best product', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views: \"Consumers picked up on their deceptive marketing schemes...\""},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@blackmask_shop/video/7695824374321941790?is_from_webapp=1&sender_device=pc&web_id=7698338633555920404"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"The ad doesn''t go on your head. The formula does. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'comment reply: 28 dollars for a shampoo?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 110K views: \"Replying to @Alex Cardenas premium ingredients need premium packaging\" Their own price-objection reply."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David on the price objection, Oct 6 call, 12:43; guarantee, Oct 5 call, 29:05."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"28 dollars for a shampoo?"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Yes. Here''s what you''re paying for. Every ingredient is rated 1.0 on the natural scale. The formula comes from an R&D team, and most versions get rejected before you ever see one. And a little goes a long way, so you use less. Cheap shampoo is cheap because of what''s in it. If you try ours and don''t think it''s worth it, you get your money back. The risk is on us."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Replying to @(user) here''s what''s in the 28 dollars. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'comment reply: do i need the conditioner too?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 30K views: \"No conditioner applied after shampoo and this is how the hair looks\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Noun''s own video; duo pricing on the site (55 instead of 60 dollars)."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Can we say the duo is cheaper than buying the two separately?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"wait do i actually need the conditioner too or is the shampoo enough"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"If you can only get one, start with the shampoo. It doesn''t strip, so your hair won''t feel like straw without conditioner. We''ve shown that on camera. The conditioner is what gets you softness and easy detangling, especially if your hair is longer. Getting both? The duo costs less than buying them separately."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Replying to @(user) start with the shampoo. #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'founder story: four products, on purpose', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 45K views: \"Natural Innovation isn''t easy - but I can promise we''re on the forefront of it\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: \"it''s only four SKUs right now\", quality before launch, Oct 5 call, 15:22 and 16:52."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"You need to record a voice note up to 3 minutes long answering the questions below. Make sure you provide as many details as possible.\nWhat can we name as \"coming next\"?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"We only sell four products. On purpose. We could launch twenty tomorrow. Put our logo on formulas that already exist and call it a line. We don''t. Every product goes through our lab and our chemist, and most versions get rejected. So right now it''s four: shampoo, conditioner, hair oil, texture powder. More are coming. Only when they''re ready."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Four products. On purpose. #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'ingredient truth: black seed oil', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views: \"...we were the first brand to launch a black seed hair oil back in 2019\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"shampoo and conditioner product pages (cold-pressed, rich in thymoquinone, scalp benefits)."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Black seed oil is in almost everything we make. Here''s why. It''s cold-pressed from black cumin seeds and naturally rich in a compound called thymoquinone. In our formulas it''s there for your scalp: it nourishes, it soothes, it helps with flaking, and it helps strengthen the hair. This brand started as a hair oil built around it. It''s still the first thing we reach for."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Black seed oil. Where we started. #nounnaturals #blackseedoil"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'proof: money back', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views: \"We''re so confident you''ll love noun and if you don''t, satisfaction or your money back\" Remake of their own video."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Noun''s own video; satisfaction guarantee, Oct 5 call, 29:05."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"You need to record a voice note up to 3 minutes long answering the questions below. Make sure you provide as many details as possible.\nWhat refund terms do you want said on camera? The site says 10-day hassle-free returns.\nThe hair oil is final sale under your return policy. Should we say \"not on the hair oil\" on camera, or keep the terms general?"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We took one of your videos that performed really well and kept the same format: the same two people sitting down, split screen, a quick B-roll of filling bottles when the basement comes up, and the Return Policy page from the website on screen while Khaled talks about trying the product."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"B: Khaled, remember the basement days? We were filling every bottle by hand, and even back then, if someone didn''t love it, they got their money back.\nA: Most people love our products. But not everyone will, and that''s okay. So try it. If it''s not for you, (TERMS).\nB: And all you have to do is message us. A real person answers, usually within a day.\nA: If we didn''t believe in what''s in the bottle, we wouldn''t put our money behind it.\nB: That''s been the rule since day one. If you''re not happy with what you spent, we take care of you.\nA: Every time."}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'viral format: two good products is all it takes', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 2.4M views: \"Two good products is all it takes\" Same hook."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"product pages."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We took a format that performed really well (2.4M views) and wrote the script for your products. Please record it in a similar style: straight to camera, fast pace, with the products in your hand.\nProducts: Shampoo and Glacial Clay Texture Powder. Have the Conditioner nearby for the last line."},{"heading":"Hook:","text":"hold the Shampoo in one hand and the Texture Powder in the other, close to the camera, and say the first line.\n\"A shampoo that cleans without stripping\": lift the Shampoo toward the camera. Optional quick cut: a pump of shampoo into your hand.\n\"A texture powder that holds\": cut to styling on dry hair. 2 to 3 sprays at the roots from about 2 inches away, then work it in with your fingers. Show the finished look.\n\"Add conditioner if your hair is longer\": quickly hold up the Conditioner.\nTips: start with hair fully dry for the styling part, use a clean background, and keep each shot short so the video moves as fast as the reference."},{"heading":"Hook:","text":"hold the Shampoo in one hand and the Texture Powder in the other, close to the camera, and say the first line. - “Stop buying more hair products. Seriously. Two good products is all it takes. You don''t need a shelf of stuff. You need one thing that washes right and one thing that styles right. “"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'drop: now we can finally talk about it', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"your drop video C0003 (founder to camera). Intro type: news / story first, the catch second."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Curl Chemistry sub-brand: curl cream, leave-in, gel and mousse; unisex leaning male; pre-orders planned); your own TikTok caption \"New Samples of our ... curl cream and leave in are in\" (104K); your drop videos C0003 and C0004 (sign up on nounnaturals.com through the pop-up form or the homepage button; list members hear first by email and text; early access before the official release date)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this straight to camera with the product in your hand, same energy as your sea salt spray drop videos. Fast, under 30 seconds."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Which product is this drop for? We wrote it for the curl line (curl cream / leave-in). If it''s a different product, we swap the name.\nHow many units go to early access? We put it in the (NUMBER) spots.\nWhere do people sign up for this drop: the website form or the Discord?\nIs there a release date yet, or do we keep it \"coming soon\"?\nHow long have the curl line samples been in testing? We can add the real time frame to the hook."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold up the curl line sample.]\nWe''ve been sampling this for a while. Now we can finally talk about it.\nOur curl line is coming. (PRODUCT NAME).\nBut there''s a catch. It goes to the early access list first.\nSign up on nounnaturals.com. The form pops up when you open the site.\nNo pop-up? There''s a button on the homepage.\nGet on the list and you''ll hear from us by email and text before we announce the date."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"It''s finally happening. Early access list first. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'drop: steve, when''s the curl line out?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"your drop video C0006 (two-person skit with Steven). Intro type: one person asks, the other explains the drop."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Curl Chemistry sub-brand: curl cream, leave-in, gel and mousse; unisex leaning male; pre-orders planned); your own TikTok caption \"New Samples of our ... curl cream and leave in are in\" (104K); your drop videos C0003 and C0004 (sign up on nounnaturals.com through the pop-up form or the homepage button; list members hear first by email and text; early access before the official release date)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this as a two-person skit with Steven, same setup as C0006: you ask, he answers fast. Keep it under 40 seconds."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Which product is this drop for? We wrote it for the curl line (curl cream / leave-in). If it''s a different product, we swap the name.\nHow many units go to early access? We put it in the (NUMBER) spots.\nWhere do people sign up for this drop: the website form or the Discord?\nIs there a release date yet, or do we keep it \"coming soon\"?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"A: Steve, people keep asking me about the curl line. When''s it out?\nB: Official date? Not yet.\nA: So what do I tell them?\nB: Tell them to get on the early access list.\nA: What list, bro?\nB: The early access list. (NUMBER) units before the official release.\nA: (NUMBER)? That''s it?\nB: That''s it. Not one more.\nA: And how do they get on it?\nB: nounnaturals.com. Fill out the pop-up.\nA: And if they''re sleeping on it?\nB: Then they wait with everybody else."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Steve said it. (NUMBER) units, early access list only. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'call-out: all respect, but he''s wrong', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@typehairofficial/video/7662843199643241759?is_from_webapp=1&sender_device=pc&web_id=7698338633555920404"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Natural is the baseline. Performance is the differentiator. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'comment reply: i struggle with frizz', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views: \"Replying to @hideyokids6967 how to get the most out of hair oil\" Advice reply."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: frizz questions get an ingredient-based answer, no guarantee, Oct 5 call, 28:00."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"guys my hair gets SO frizzy  what do y’all recommend??"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Frizz is usually dry hair looking for moisture. So: a shampoo that doesn''t strip, conditioner on the mid-lengths and ends, and two or three drops of hair oil on the ends once it''s dry. That''s where we''d start. No guarantees, every head is different. And if your hair is curly, the curl cream we''re finishing is made for exactly this."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Replying to @(user) frizz = hair asking for moisture. #nounnaturals #frizz"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'comment reply: why is the sea salt spray taking so long?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 24K views: \"Replying to @Draven why is noun sea salt spray taking so long to release? Here''s the answer\" Remake of their own reply."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David on the two-year delay, Oct 5 call, 16:52."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"You need to record a voice note up to 3 minutes long answering the questions below. Make sure you provide as many details as possible.\nWhat is the current status of the sea salt spray?\nWhat can we say about a date?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"bro why is the sea salt spray taking FOREVERRR"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Because we kept saying no to it. It was supposed to come out two years ago. Every time we thought it was done, our chemist said it wasn''t good enough. So we waited, and yes, that cost us money. The version we have now is not the one we would have sold you two years ago. It''s better. (STATUS OR DATE)."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Replying to @(user) here''s the real answer. #noun #seasaltspray"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'how to use it: where you put the powder', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 179K views: \"Styling the most ignored part of the hair\" Placement how-to."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference. No talking or script is needed. Product to use: Glacial Clay Texture Powder. The focus is on actually showing how the hair looks different when you apply it to different areas.\nStart with clean, fully dry, unstyled hair. Show the \"before\" for a second.\nShow the texture powder bottle to the camera.\nRoots: hold the bottle about 2 inches away and spray 2 to 3 times at the roots. Push it up with your fingers and show the lift and volume.\nMid-lengths: add one more spray through the lengths and scrunch with your fingers. Show the messy, textured look.\nMake the difference between the two results easy to see (same angle and lighting for both).\nEnd with the final look and the bottle in frame so viewers know what you used."},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"Where you put texture powder changes everything"},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Roots for lift. Lengths for texture. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'lab update: head to toe is coming back', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 45K views Khaled talking straight to camera: opens on a montage of comments asking for a product, \"I hear you guys\", explains why it takes time, then asks people to comment."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: Noun sold hair, body and beard care before the rebrand and is relaunching them, Oct 5 call, 3:51. 2025: narrowed to best sellers, reformulated, new manufacturer, re-released (Master Client Context Document)."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"You need to record a voice note up to 3 minutes long answering the questions below. Make sure you provide as many details as possible.\nWhat is coming back in body and beard care, and when?\nArabian Oud Beard Oil is already on the site. Is beard care coming back as a wider line, and which products exactly?"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We took one of your videos that performed well and adapted the script to it. Please record it the same way: straight to camera, same setup. We''ll open the video with a few custom comments asking about body and beard care (made in Canva or CapCut), the same way your sea salt spray video opens."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"I hear you guys. Before the rebrand, Noun was head to toe: hair, body and beard. Last year we narrowed it down to our best sellers, reformulated them with a new manufacturer and a stronger team, and brought them back. Hair came first. Body and beard are next. (TIMING). It takes longer and it costs more, but that’s the only way we do it. Tell me in the comments what you want back first."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Head to toe is coming back. Hair came first. Body and beard are next. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'live promo: unreleased products on the live', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 40K views: \"Just testing the final batch (24 months in the making)\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"sample reveals are among Noun''s top videos (curl cream samples, 104K)."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"You need to record a voice note up to 3 minutes long answering the questions below. Make sure you provide as many details as possible.\nCan you show unreleased samples on tonight''s live? Which ones?\nWhat time is the live (ET)?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"We''re showing unreleased products on the live tonight. (TIME). (WHICH SAMPLES). You''ll see them before anyone else and you can tell us what you think. What we hear on the lives goes straight back to the lab. If you want a say in what we launch next, be there."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"See it before it exists. (TIME) ET. #noun #tiktoklive"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'proof: who leads our innovation', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 77K views Two-person skit: B throws the bottle to A and explains why it''s different."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David, Oct 6 call, 12:57; Master Context: a former L''Oreal VP of Innovation has led formulation strategy since September 2025 (name, exact title and role not confirmed); shampoo INCI (decyl glucoside, lauryl glucoside); conditioner is quat-free."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"You need to record a voice note up to 3 minutes long answering the questions below. Make sure you provide as many details as possible.\nCan we say this on camera and name L''Oreal?\nWhat is his exact title and role: advisor or full-time hire? (We removed \"he''s on our board\" until you confirm.)\nIs it accurate to say we get to test new ingredients a year or two before the rest of the market? If yes, we can add it back to the script."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We took one of your videos that performed really well and adapted the script to it. Please record it in a similar style: same two-person skit, B throws the shampoo bottle to A. You can change the outfits or the location slightly, but keep the core concept the same."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"B\tYo, what are you doing?\nA\tWashing my hair. Bro, this is natural shampoo and it actually foams.\nB      How?\nA\tBro, catch. Read the back.\nB\tDecyl glucoside, lauryl glucoside. What is that?\nA\tPlant-based cleansers. That''s where the foam comes from. No sulfates.\nB\tWho even comes up with this?\nA\tBro, our formulation is led by a former VP of Innovation at L''Oreal.\nB\tNo way.\nA\tAnd the conditioner has no quats. It''s not luck, it''s R&D. Why haven''t you tried this yet?\nB\tAll right, all right."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"A natural shampoo that foams and a conditioner with no quats. It''s not luck. It''s R&D. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'drop: what we''ve been working on besides the powder', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"your drop video C0001 (founder to camera). Intro type: question about the product, then the answer."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Glacial Clay hair clay is a separate product in development, not the texture powder); Oct 5 call, 32:00 (lab samples go to loyal customers); Master Client Context Document (natural, high performing, long-term hair and scalp health; science-backed should be the minimum)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this straight to camera with the product in your hand, same energy as your sea salt spray drop videos. Fast, under 30 seconds."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Which product is this drop for? We wrote it for the hair clay. If it''s a different product, we swap the name.\nHow many units go to early access? We put it in the (NUMBER) spots.\nWhere do people sign up for this drop: the website form or the Discord?\nIs there a release date yet, or do we keep it \"coming soon\"?\nWhat should we say about the clay: hold, finish, who it''s for?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"You know what we''ve been working on besides the texture powder?\n[Hold up the clay sample.]\nA hair clay.\nAnd no, it''s not a new version of the powder. It''s a separate product.\nSame rule as everything we make: natural, and it has to perform.\n(ONE LINE: WHAT THE CLAY DOES OR HOW IT FINISHES).\nWant to know when it''s ready?\nComment \"clay\" and I''ll make sure you hear first."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Not the powder. Something new. Comment \"clay\". #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'drop: remember our website', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"your drop video C0007 (founder to camera). Intro type: the call to action is the first line."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Glacial Clay hair clay is a separate product in development, not the texture powder); Oct 5 call, 32:00 (lab samples go to loyal customers); your drop videos C0003 and C0004 (sign up on nounnaturals.com through the pop-up form or the homepage button; list members hear first by email and text; early access before the official release date)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this straight to camera with the product in your hand, same energy as your sea salt spray drop videos. Fast, under 30 seconds."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Which product is this drop for? We wrote it for the hair clay. If it''s a different product, we swap the name.\nHow many units go to early access? We put it in the (NUMBER) spots.\nWhere do people sign up for this drop: the website form or the Discord?\nIs there a release date yet, or do we keep it \"coming soon\"?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"nounnaturals.com. Remember that.\nBecause that''s where the early access list for our hair clay is.\n(NUMBER) units go out before the official release. Only to people on the list.\nFill out the form that pops up, or hit the button on the homepage.\nList members hear about the drop first, by email and text.\nI don''t think these are going to last long.\nGet on the list."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Hair clay early access. nounnaturals.com. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'is texture powder actually bad?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@dillon.latham/video/7450288429763480878"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Is Texture powder actually bad? #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'comment reply: does it leave white stuff in dark hair?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 8.2M views: \"just gotta work it in really well\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"texture powder product page (zero shine, zero residue, zero buildup)."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"You need to record a voice note up to 3 minutes long answering the questions below. Make sure you provide as many details as possible.\nIs \"if you see white, you used too much in one spot\" correct for dark hair?"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Show how you work it in with your fingers and how you rub the white residue from hair"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"does the powder leave white stuff on dark hair tho"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"No. It''s a matte finish. No shine, no residue. The trick is how you put it in: hold it a couple of inches away, two to three pumps, and work it in with your fingers. If you see white, you used too much in one spot. Rub it through and it''s gone."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Replying to @(user) matte, no residue. #nounnaturals #texturepowder"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'comment reply: highest performing? prove it', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 191K views: \"Does noun have the highest performing texture powder?\" Talking-head answer to their own video."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Noun''s own videos (191K and 31K); barber reviews (133K)."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"“Highest performing texture powder”? Prove it"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Okay. Texture, hold, volume. Those are the three things a powder has to do. Ours does all three on two to three pumps, with no aerosol and nothing synthetic. But don''t take a brand''s word for it, ours included. Barbers tested it on camera. Watch those, then try it. If it doesn''t beat what you use now, you get your money back."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Replying to @(user) texture, hold, volume. #noun #texturepowder"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'founder story: there is no noun without u', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 67K views: \"W friend group, thx boys for showing love\" Community format."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"site tagline (\"Because there is no Noun without U\"); started with one customer, Oct 6 call, 4:30."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"You need to record a voice note up to 3 minutes long answering the questions below. Make sure you provide as many details as possible.\nWhere does the name Noun come from?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"There is no Noun without U. Look at the word. N-O-U-N. Take the U out and it doesn''t work. This brand started with one guy and one customer. Everything since then came from people telling us what they needed and what we got wrong. The lives, the samples, the comment replies. That''s the U."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"No Noun without U. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'ingredient truth: amla', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 56K views: \"Thinning hair? Try making this oil at home...\" Oil ingredient breakdown."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"hair oil product page (amla for strengthening, healthy-looking roots, antioxidant protection)."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Stop sleeping on amla. Trust me, you''ll want it in your hair oil, and this is why.\nSo as many of you know, I started this brand because I was losing my hair. So I got obsessed with what actually goes into a hair oil. And amla is one of the ingredients I''d never leave out.\nOne: amla is Indian gooseberry, and it''s been used on hair for a very long time. Two: in our hair oil it''s there for your roots: strengthening and antioxidant protection. Three: it doesn''t work alone. It sits next to black seed, batana, pumpkin seed and rosemary. Thirteen botanicals, each one with a job.\nTrust me, none of them is there to decorate the label. Massage it into your scalp before you wash, two to three times a week."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Amla. One of 13 botanicals in our hair oil, each one with a job. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'myth bust: natural means no science back', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@blackmask_shop/video/7668859681690881311?is_from_webapp=1&sender_device=pc&web_id=7698338633555920404"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: the team goes deep into the science of each ingredient, Oct 5 call, 28:00."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Is there a specific video or creator saying natural is anti-science that you''d want to react to? Send us the link."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Natural ingredients. Scientific process. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'viral format: choose', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 3.2M views: \"Choose the better product\""},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Your choice. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'drop: (number) units, that''s the whole drop', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"your drop video C0005 (founder to camera). Intro type: exact number as the hook."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Glacial Clay hair clay is a separate product in development, not the texture powder); Oct 5 call, 32:00 (lab samples go to loyal customers); your drop videos C0005 and C0007 (early access through the Discord, discord.gg/noun, link in the caption)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this straight to camera with the product in your hand, same energy as your sea salt spray drop videos. Fast, under 30 seconds."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Which product is this drop for? We wrote it for the hair clay. If it''s a different product, we swap the name.\nHow many units go to early access? We put it in the (NUMBER) spots.\nWhere do people sign up for this drop: the website form or the Discord?\nIs there a release date yet, or do we keep it \"coming soon\"?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"(NUMBER) units of our hair clay. That''s the whole early access drop.\nThey go to the Discord first. discord.gg/noun, link in the caption.\nThe early access form goes up in there before the official release date.\nOnce they''re gone, early access is closed.\nJoin now so you''re ready when it drops."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"(NUMBER) units. Discord first. discord.gg/noun #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'drop: it''s 2026, your clay should be natural and still hold', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"your drop videos C0002 clips 1 to 3 (founder to camera). Intro type: \"It''s 2026, your X should...\"."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Glacial Clay hair clay is a separate product in development, not the texture powder); Oct 5 call, 32:00 (lab samples go to loyal customers); Master Client Context Document (\"natural\" is a standard: ISO 16128 natural vs naturally derived)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this straight to camera with the product in your hand, same energy as your sea salt spray drop videos. Fast, under 30 seconds."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Which product is this drop for? We wrote it for the hair clay. If it''s a different product, we swap the name.\nHow many units go to early access? We put it in the (NUMBER) spots.\nWhere do people sign up for this drop: the website form or the Discord?\nIs there a release date yet, or do we keep it \"coming soon\"?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold up the clay sample.]\nIt''s 2026. Your hair clay should be natural and still hold like a hair clay.\nNot natural on the front of the jar and synthetic on the back.\nFlip it over. Read it.\nThat''s how we''re building ours.\nOur hair clay. Coming soon."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Natural on the front and the back. Coming soon. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'how we condition without quats', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@abbeyyung/video/7345199757452774698"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Can a conditioner without quats or silicones actually work? #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'don’t use texture powder until you know that!', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@075barber/video/7378698483361910024"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Don’t use texture powder until you know that! #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'call-out: whatever''s in your parents'' shower', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 3.6M views: \"Hair products make the biggest difference\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: kids use whatever their parents buy until they find brands on TikTok, Oct 5 call, 32:00; Glacial Clay Texture Powder product page. Same structure as the reference: \"people think it doesn''t matter\", then without vs with, uncut application, final look."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Still using whatever''s in your parents'' shower?  people think it doesn''t matter what you put in your hair. So we''re going to compare my hair without and with texture powder.\n(Fresh out of the shower, hair blow-dried, no product.) I just washed my hair, so there''s nothing in it right now. Watch what happens when I try to style it. (Push it up, let it fall, show it on camera as it is.)\n(Hold up the Noun Glacial Clay Texture Powder.) This is our texture powder. Two to three sprays from about two inches away, on dry hair. I''ll show you uncut. Now take your hands and scrunch. (Keep filming, no cuts, until it''s styled.)\n(Final look, close up.) It''s volcanic silica, Canadian glacial clay and plant-derived powders. No aerosols, no synthetics, no microplastics. And it stays matte all day. You pick your own shoes, your own clothes, your own haircut. Pick what goes in your hair too."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Without vs with. Pick what goes in your hair. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'comment reply: how long until i see a difference?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 31K views: \"Replying to @irockali not letting you down king\" Comment-reply format."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: styling is immediate, wash products are \"not a miracle product\", Oct 5 call, 6:25."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"sooo how long till i actually see a difference tho"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Depends which product. Styling: right away. Texture powder works the second you put it in. Shampoo and conditioner: you feel it from the first wash. Softer, not stripped. The long-term part, scalp and hair health, takes weeks, not days. We''re not a miracle product and we won''t pretend to be. Give it four weeks and judge for yourself."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Replying to @(user) not a miracle. Give it four weeks. #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'founder story: we got sued and lost our name', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 2.5M views: \"Why I Created My Hair Products\" Founder-story format."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Oct 6 call, 4:14 to 5:00 (Habibi Life, trademark infringement lawsuit, long legal battle, gave up the name, more global than one community); Noun Naturals since 2021 (site and Master Context Document); Master Context Document (2025 rebuild: reformulation, new contract manufacturer, former L''Oréal VP of Innovation leading formulation, re-release Sep 2025); nounnaturals.com (Trio 4.8 from 972 reviews; 2025 shampoo bottle has 4 oz more)."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Are you comfortable telling the Habibi Life story on camera?"},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Can we mention the former L''Oréal VP of Innovation on camera (without a name)? What is his exact role: advisor or hire?\nWhat has the feedback been since the September 2025 re-release? Anything customers keep telling you about the new shampoo and conditioner?\nWhat exactly got better in the new formulas, in your words?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"We got sued, and we lost our name. This brand used to be called Habibi Life. The lawsuit was for trademark infringement. The fight went on for a long time, and in the end we gave up the name. So in 2021 we started again as Noun Naturals. New name, bigger vision: not one community, everyone. But the name was only the start. In 2025 we went back to the products. We reformulated our shampoo and conditioner, moved to a new manufacturer, and brought on a former VP of Innovation from L''Oréal to lead formulation. We re-released them in September 2025, and the shampoo bottle got 4 ounces bigger. Today our Trio sits at 4.8 stars from 972 reviews."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"We lost our name. Then we rebuilt the products. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'myth bust: if it foams, it''s full of chemicals', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 135K views: \"Natural is the base line, performance is the differentiator\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"shampoo ingredient list; David on foam in natural shampoos, Oct 5 call, 12:36."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"if it foams that much, it’s gotta be full of chemicals bruh"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Wrong. Foam tells you there''s a cleanser in the bottle. It doesn''t tell you which one. A sulfate foams. A plant-based cleanser foams too. One can strip your scalp. The other is gentle enough for every day. Don''t judge a shampoo by the bubbles. Judge it by the ingredient list."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Don''t judge a shampoo by the bubbles. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'live promo: a dollar off for every ingredient', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 356K views A recorded skit, not a live clip: \"Every juggle is a dollar off on TikTok Live tonight\", he counts the juggles, a second guy walks in (\"You''re supposed to stop at five!\"), \"I''m trying to bless the customers.\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"shampoo ingredient list on nounnaturals.com; nightly lives and flash sales, Oct 5 call."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Are you okay with a dollar off per ingredient on the live? If not, what deal should we use?\nWhat time is the live (ET)?"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We took one of your videos that performed really well and kept the same skit: one person does the challenge and counts, the other walks in and tries to stop him. Same studio setup, same energy. This time it''s the shampoo bottle instead of the ball. Put a counter on screen for every ingredient."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"A: (holding the shampoo bottle up to the camera) Every ingredient I can explain off this bottle is a dollar off on TikTok Live tonight.\nA: (reading the label, fast) Decyl glucoside, a cleanser made from plant sugar. One. Aloe leaf juice. Two. Lauryl glucoside, another sugar cleanser. Three. Citric acid. Four. Xanthan gum, the thickener. Five. Turmeric root oil. Six. Nigella seed oil, that''s black seed. Seven. Sodium phytate. Eight...\nB: (walks in) Yo! What are you doing, bro?\nA: Explaining ingredients for dollars off on the live.\nB: You''re supposed to stop at three! Three!\nA: Bro, they''re all on the bottle. I''m trying to bless the customers.\nB: (walking off) Every time...\nA: (to camera) Tonight, (TIME) Eastern. Come get it."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Every ingredient I can explain is a dollar off on the live tonight. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'call-out: who makes your product?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"a typical Noun expert video @nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dblqcn7CsP0/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&mdxt=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ=="},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Give people the full context. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'how to use it: diy leave-in spray', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 110K views: \"Putting your conditioner in a spray bottle to make at home leave in?\" Remake of their own video. Same two-person skit: one person off camera asks \"what are you doing?\", the other puts them on to the \"glitch\"."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Noun''s own video."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"What conditioner-to-water ratio do you recommend?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"(Kitchen counter. Person 1 in the lab coat pours Noun conditioner into an empty spray bottle. Person 2 films from off camera.)\nPerson 2: Yo, what are you doing?\nPerson 1: What do you mean what am I doing?\nPerson 2: Conditioner. In a spray bottle?\nPerson 1: You don''t know about this glitch?\nPerson 2: No.\nPerson 1: Bro, I''m about to put you on. DIY leave-in. Step one, check your conditioner has no quats. Ours doesn''t. (RATIO) conditioner to water. Then shake.\nPerson 2: You''re shaking it like pre-workout.\n(Person 1 sprays it on damp hair and combs it through.)\nPerson 2: Wait, you''re not rinsing it?\nPerson 1: Nope. You leave it in. That''s a quat-free leave-in until ours comes out.\nPerson 2: Bro, you just put me on."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Conditioner in a spray bottle? DIY leave-in. Check for quats first. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'ingredient truth: pumpkin seed oil', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 56K views: \"Thinning hair? Try making this oil at home...\" Same structure: bold \"do this before your shower\" hook, personal hairline story, how to do it step by step, then why it matters."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"hair oil product page (pumpkin seed oil is omega-rich, supports scalp health, balances natural oils; scalp massage before washing, scalp treatment 2 to 3 times a week); bullied for a receding hairline, Oct 6 call."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Are you OK telling the hairline story in this video?\nBefore washing, how long do you recommend letting the oil sit on the scalp?\nHow many drops do you use for a scalp massage?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Oil your scalp before your shower. Trust me, and this is why. I got bullied for my hairline. So I started paying attention to what I put on my scalp. One of the oils in our hair oil: pumpkin seed oil. It''s rich in omegas, it nourishes your scalp and helps balance its natural oils. Here''s how I use it. Before you wash, put a few drops straight on your scalp. Massage it in with your fingertips. Let it sit (TIME), then shower and wash it out. Two to three times a week. People think hair oil is just for dry ends. Your hair starts at your scalp. Treat it like it."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Oil your scalp before you shower. Pumpkin seed oil is why. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'lab update: how a scent gets approved', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 32K views: \"Replying to @Benedict and noun on the front lines of innovation...\" A reply to a comment, straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"works with fragrance houses, Oct 5 call, 15:20; the fragrance house visit and \"CEO approves a scent\" videos (32K and 34K); fragrance labeled to US and EU rules, no vague \"natural fragrance\" (Master Client Context Document)."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"How does a scent get approved, step by step? How many rounds of samples does it usually take?\nWhich product''s scent is being approved right now, and can we name it?"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable. Record it straight to camera like the reference. We can cut in a few seconds of your fragrance house visit video when you mention it."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"yoo how do you guys pick a scent"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"It takes way longer than people think. We don''t pick a scent off a shelf. We work with fragrance houses, the people whose whole job is building scents. You might have seen the video where we went to one. (HOW IT WORKS: SAMPLES, ROUNDS). And smelling good isn''t enough. It has to work in the formula, and it has to be labeled the right way for the US and the EU. That''s why you won''t see \"natural fragrance\" on our bottles. That phrase tells you nothing. When a scent passes all of that, the final call is mine. Right now we''re approving one for (PRODUCT). Guess which one in the comments."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: How a scent gets approved. Guess which product is next. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'proof: the school presentation', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 67K views: \"W friend group, thx boys for showing love\" Customer-love format. The presentation clip is not in the research sheet."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David, Oct 5 call, 48:47: \"We educate our customers so much. Even, you know, we have a clip of a kid doing a whole school project, and he filmed himself doing the school project in front of his whole class, did a whole presentation about our products.\" David, Oct 5 call, 37:13: when they stopped posting, people made videos saying their products suck, and \"our loyal customer base... they were responding for us\"; \"we go ingredient for ingredient\"; once people do their own research \"they start to realize, hey, these guys actually know what they''re talking about\". David, Oct 6 call, 16:19: \"It goes beyond hair and body products. It really goes down to the personal care aspect of taking care of yourself.\""},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"You need to record a voice note up to 3 minutes long answering the questions below. Make sure you provide as many details as possible.\nCan we mention this story on camera?\nPlease send the clip and confirm you have permission to show it."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Is this story accurate as written? All we have is from the Oct 5 call: a kid presented Noun''s products to his class as a school project.\nDid he do this on his own, or did someone ask him to? How did you find out about it?\nWhat did he actually talk about in the presentation (ingredients, labels, something else)?\nHow old was he, roughly, and is it OK to say that?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"A kid did a whole presentation about our products. In front of his whole class.\n[Cut to a few seconds of his presentation clip, if you have permission to show it.]\nHe filmed himself doing it for a school project. (WHAT HE PRESENTED, from your voice note.)\nAnd he''s not the only one. There was a time we stopped posting, and people were making videos saying our products suck. We didn''t answer. Our customers did. They answered for us.\nWe go through every ingredient, one by one. And when people look into it themselves, they see we actually know what we''re talking about.\nFor us, it was never just shampoo. It''s about taking care of yourself.\nTo everyone who has our back: thank you."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"He did a whole school presentation about Noun. It was never just shampoo. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'viral format: the worst way to style your hair', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 546K views: \"This is the worst way to style your hair in 2025!\" Same hook and structure: combs his hair down into a flat middle part (\"Stop doing this\"), shakes it out, then a quick middle part tutorial step by step (brush back, line up the part with the inside of the eyebrows, product, scrunch), and ends with \"send this to a friend\". Filmed in the bathroom on the front camera, quick cuts between steps."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"texture powder directions on nounnaturals.com (dry hair, 2 to 3 sprays from 2 inches, matte all day); misuse behind negative reviews, Oct 5 call, 47:33."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record it exactly like the reference: front camera, bathroom, start on dry hair, a quick cut for every step. The reference uses two products (sea salt spray and clay). We use the Glacial Clay Texture Powder for both steps. If the sea salt spray is out when you film, you can use it for the first step like the reference does."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Comb your hair down into a flat, stuck-down middle part.]\nStop doing this. This is the worst way to style your hair in 2026.\n[Shake your hair out.]\nI''m going to show you the easiest middle part tutorial to get loads of texture and volume.\n[Brush your hair all the way back, then split it into a middle part, lining it up with the inside of your eyebrows.]\nFirst, brush your hair all the way back. Then split it using the inside of your eyebrows to line up the part.\n[Hold the texture powder up to the camera.]\nNow grab your texture powder. I''m using the Noun Glacial Clay Texture Powder.\n[Hold it about two inches from your head and spray two to three times at the roots.]\nTwo to three sprays at the roots, about two inches away.\n[Show the texture coming in.]\nYou can already see the texture coming in.\n[Scrunch it in with your fingers, then fix the final pieces.]\nTo finish it off for more volume, scrunch it in with your fingers and add your final details.\n[Show the final look, then look at the camera.]\nNow the last step is to send this to a friend who desperately needs this tutorial."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"The easiest middle part tutorial. Send this to a friend who needs it. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'drop: steve, is the balm actually coming back?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"your drop video C0006 (two-person skit with Steven). Intro type: one person asks, the other explains the drop."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Styling Balm: best seller since 2018, in restock); your drop videos C0003 and C0004 (sign up on nounnaturals.com through the pop-up form or the homepage button; list members hear first by email and text; early access before the official release date)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this as a two-person skit with Steven, same setup as C0006: you ask, he answers fast. Keep it under 40 seconds."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Which product is this drop for? We wrote it for the Styling Balm restock. If it''s a different product, we swap the name.\nHow many units go to early access? We put it in the (NUMBER) spots.\nWhere do people sign up for this drop: the website form or the Discord?\nIs there a release date yet, or do we keep it \"coming soon\"?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"A: Steve, is the Styling Balm actually coming back?\nB: It''s coming back.\nA: When?\nB: Early access list first. Then everybody else.\nA: How many?\nB: (NUMBER).\nA: That''s it?\nB: That''s it, bro. Best seller since 2018. You think that''s lasting?\nA: Where do they sign up?\nB: nounnaturals.com. The pop-up on the homepage.\nA: And if they miss it?\nB: Then they wait for the restock like everybody else."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Steve confirmed it. The balm is back, list first. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'drop: still waiting for the styling balm?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"your drop video C0004 (founder to camera). Intro type: direct question to the viewer."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Styling Balm: best seller since 2018, in restock); your drop videos C0003 and C0004 (sign up on nounnaturals.com through the pop-up form or the homepage button; list members hear first by email and text; early access before the official release date)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this straight to camera with the product in your hand, same energy as your sea salt spray drop videos. Fast, under 30 seconds."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Which product is this drop for? We wrote it for the Styling Balm restock. If it''s a different product, we swap the name.\nHow many units go to early access? We put it in the (NUMBER) spots.\nWhere do people sign up for this drop: the website form or the Discord?\nIs there a release date yet, or do we keep it \"coming soon\"?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Still waiting for the Styling Balm?\nGood. Because the restock goes to the early access list first.\n(NUMBER) units before it''s back on the site.\nGet on the list: nounnaturals.com, fill out the form.\nYou''ll hear from us by email and text before anyone else knows the date."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Styling Balm restock. List first, site second. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'drop: our best seller since 2018 is coming back', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"your drop video C0003 (founder to camera). Intro type: news / story first, the catch second."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Styling Balm: best seller since 2018, in restock); your drop videos C0003 and C0004 (sign up on nounnaturals.com through the pop-up form or the homepage button; list members hear first by email and text; early access before the official release date)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this straight to camera with the product in your hand, same energy as your sea salt spray drop videos. Fast, under 30 seconds."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Which product is this drop for? We wrote it for the Styling Balm restock. If it''s a different product, we swap the name.\nHow many units go to early access? We put it in the (NUMBER) spots.\nWhere do people sign up for this drop: the website form or the Discord?\nIs there a release date yet, or do we keep it \"coming soon\"?\nCan we say how many people have bought the balm? Your document has both 100k+ and 300k+."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold up the Styling Balm.]\nOur best seller since 2018 is coming back.\nThe Styling Balm.\nBut before it goes back on the site, it goes to the early access list.\nSign up on nounnaturals.com. The form pops up, or there''s a button on the homepage.\nList members get it first, before the restock date is public."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"The Styling Balm is coming back. Early access list first. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'drop: write down our discord', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"your drop video C0007 (founder to camera). Intro type: the call to action is the first line."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Styling Balm: best seller since 2018, in restock); your drop videos C0005 and C0007 (early access through the Discord, discord.gg/noun, link in the caption)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this straight to camera with the product in your hand, same energy as your sea salt spray drop videos. Fast, under 30 seconds."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Which product is this drop for? We wrote it for the Styling Balm restock. If it''s a different product, we swap the name.\nHow many units go to early access? We put it in the (NUMBER) spots.\nWhere do people sign up for this drop: the website form or the Discord?\nIs there a release date yet, or do we keep it \"coming soon\"?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"discord.gg/noun. Write that down.\nThat''s where the Styling Balm early access goes first.\nOur best seller since 2018, back for (NUMBER) people before the official restock.\nJoin, watch for the form, and be ready.\nWhen it''s gone, it''s gone."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Styling Balm early access starts in the Discord. discord.gg/noun #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'your first brand isn''t your forever brand', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@nathaniel_.harrison/video/7189865547696213290"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Your first hair brand doesn''t have to be your last one. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'customers who use products that don''t exist yet', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@blackmask_shop/video/7675732014217088270"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Studies have shown that a mix of keratin and rice protein can make hair up to 25% stronger by replacing the keratin that is lost when you wash your hair.  #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'the first label he ever read', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 45K views"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Natural innovation isn''t easy. But let me tell you why I do it. When I started losing my hair, I looked up what was happening, and I realized I''d been putting store-bought products on my head for years without reading a single ingredient list. That part was on me. That''s the whole reason this brand exists: ingredients you can actually read, in everything you use. So if you take one thing from me, even if you never buy anything: read the label."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Read the label. That''s the whole reason this brand exists. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'is sulfate shampoo actually good?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@abbeyyung/video/7538174622429089055"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Is sulfate shampoo actually good? #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'sulfates and silicones have their purpose! is this true?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@abbeyyung/video/7221657668673522990"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Sulfates and silicones have their purpose!  Is this true? #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'viral format: stack your products', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 2.3M views: \"You need to stack your products\" Same hook."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: hydrated hair is easier to style, Oct 6 call, 8:00."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"You need to stack your products. One product can''t do everything. Clean base: a shampoo that doesn''t strip. Moisture: conditioner on the ends. Then style on top: texture powder on dry hair. Each one makes the next one work better. Hair that isn''t dried out is easier to style. The styling starts in the shower."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"The styling starts in the shower. #noun #nounnaturals\nOur whole routine, start to finish. Before you wash, two to three times a week: hair oil on the scalp, massage it in. In the shower: shampoo on the scalp, rinse well, then conditioner on the mid-lengths and ends. Dry your hair completely. Style: two to three pumps of texture powder at the roots. Dry ends? Two drops of oil. That''s everything we make, in order. Screenshot it."}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'proof: what cosmos means', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 32K views: \"...noun on the front lines of innovation, we''re not being cheap with you guys, other brands are\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"site FAQ on COSMOS; comment from the reference video (reply format, same structure: read the comment, agree, flip it)."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"You need to record a voice note up to 3 minutes long answering the questions below. Make sure you provide as many details as possible.\nDoes COSMOS apply to all formulas or to specific products? The site says both."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"natural doesn’t automatically mean better bro science has come a long way there’s literally safe AND effective stuff out there yk??"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Yes. Exactly. That''s what we''re saying. The word natural on its own means nothing. Anyone can put it on a bottle. That''s why we formulate with COSMOS-approved ingredients. COSMOS is a standard that checks ingredients are genuinely natural, sustainably sourced, and processed without harmful chemicals. And it''s a standard someone else sets and checks, not a word we made up for the front of the bottle. So you get natural ingredients and the science behind them. This comment actually helps our argument."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: a standard, not a slogan. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'live promo: come tell me natural doesn''t work', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 6.4M views: \"Replying to @J.x JOIN THE LIVE NOW\" Live invitation as a comment reply."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: haters get persuaded once Noun talks to them live, Oct 6 call, 14:31."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"What time is tonight''s live (ET)?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Think natural products don''t work? Come tell me on the live. (TIME). I''ll bring you up. You tell me why, I''ll put the ingredient list on screen, and we go through it together. I''ve had this conversation a hundred times and I like it every time. If you still think I''m wrong at the end, say it on camera."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Come say it to my face. (TIME) ET. #noun #tiktoklive"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'live promo: for viewers outside the us', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 68K views: \"Comeback live tonight at 9pm EST\" Their own live announcement."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: top regions are the UK, UAE and Australia, Oct 5 call, 43:20; site ships worldwide."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"You need to record a voice note up to 3 minutes long answering the questions below. Make sure you provide as many details as possible.\nWhich countries should we name?\nWhat can we say about international shipping? Delivery times are left out on purpose.\nWhat time is tonight''s live (ET)?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"UK, UAE, Australia: this one''s for you. You watch the lives and you ask if we ship to you. We do. Worldwide, and the site shows your own currency. Tonight''s live is at (TIME) Eastern. That''s (LOCAL TIMES) for you. Come say where you''re watching from."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Yes, we ship to you. (TIME) ET tonight. #noun #tiktoklive"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'live promo: two weeks of lives', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@based, 3M views: \"Is BASED live right now?\" Live-promo format."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"most common objections in the calls: foam, price, sea salt spray."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"You need to record a voice note up to 3 minutes long answering the questions below. Make sure you provide as many details as possible.\nWhich three questions did you actually hear most on the lives these two weeks?\nWhat time is tonight''s live (ET)?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Two weeks of lives. Here''s what you asked the most. Does it foam. Is it worth the price. When is the sea salt spray coming. We answered all three on camera and we''ll keep answering. Tonight at (TIME) we do it again. Bring the question we haven''t heard yet."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Ask the one we haven''t heard. (TIME) ET. #noun #tiktoklive"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'ingredient truth: shea butter and olive oil', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals Follow this video''s format."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"conditioner product page (shea butter, olive oil added in 2025, coconut and jojoba oil)."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Why does our conditioner feel this rich? Two ingredients: shea butter and olive oil.\nShea butter locks moisture into the hair. Olive oil is the newest addition to the formula, added in 2025 for an extra boost of conditioning. Coconut and jojoba oil sit right next to them. That''s the nourishing part of the formula. And there are no quats and no silicones in it. The conditioning comes from a plant-derived conditioner instead. That''s how you get 24 hours of weightless hydration. Read the label, it''s all there."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Shea, olive, coconut, jojoba. #nounnaturals #conditioner"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'how to use it: the straight hair routine', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 256K views: \"The only tutorial you''ll ever need to MAX your straight hair!\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"product pages."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference: a step-by-step routine tutorial. No talking or script is needed. Products to use: Shampoo, Conditioner and Glacial Clay Texture Powder. Use someone with straight hair."},{"heading":"TO-DO LIST","text":"Start by showing straight, flat, unstyled hair (the \"before\").\nWash with the shampoo. Show the bottle clearly.\nApply the conditioner to the mid-lengths and ends only, not the scalp. Show the bottle.\nDry the hair completely.\nTexture powder: hold the bottle about 2 inches away, spray 2 to 3 times at the roots and push the hair up with your fingers.\nShow the final result next to the \"before\", and end with all three products in frame."},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"The straight hair routine"},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Less product. Better result. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'how to use it: the whole routine in order', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 13.1M views: \"Fix flat hair after shampoo with this routine\" Full-routine format."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"usage on the product pages."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"You need to record a voice note up to 3 minutes long answering the questions below. Make sure you provide as many details as possible.\nPlease confirm this is the order you recommend."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"No talking in this one. Like the reference, it is a silent BTS of the full routine with text on screen. Film it vertical, one step per shot, short cuts, and keep the product in frame at every step.\nShot 1 (hook): your hair before the shower. Text on screen: \"Fix flat hair after the shower with this routine\".\nShot 2: Hair Oil. 2 to 5 drops, massage into the scalp before washing. Text: \"1. Hair Oil\".\nShot 3: Shampoo in the shower. Text: \"2. Shampoo\".\nShot 4: Conditioner. Text: \"3. Conditioner\".\nShot 5: dry your hair fully (the powder goes on dry hair only).\nShot 6: Glacial Clay Texture Powder. 2 to 3 sprays from about 2 inches, then style with your fingers. Text: \"4. Texture Powder\".\nShot 7: the final look, a slow turn so we see the texture. Show all four products together at the end."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Oil. Shampoo. Conditioner. Powder. In that order. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'comment reply: my hair is oily a day after washing', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 3.4M views: \"How to fix your shampoo day hair\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"shampoo page (turmeric balances oil); texture powder FAQ (absorbs oil between washes)."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"my hair is greasy as hell the day after washing it  what do I do"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Two things. In the shower: our shampoo has turmeric, which helps balance oil, and it cleans without stripping. Between washes: two to three pumps of texture powder at the roots. The clay absorbs the oil and you get another day out of it. No promises, every scalp is different. That''s where we''d start."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Replying to @(user) two things to try. #nounnaturals #oilyhair"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'comment reply: can i use your shampoo with another conditioner?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 34K views: call-out of quats in a \"natural\" conditioner"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Noun''s point about quats and silicones in conditioners."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"wait can i use ur shampoo with the conditioner i already have orrr????"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"You can. Nobody has to buy everything at once. Just check what''s in the one you have. If it has silicones or quats, it''s coating your hair right after you cleaned it. Finish the bottle if you want. When it runs out, try ours and see if you feel the difference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Replying to @(user) you can. Check the label first. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'call-out: brands started checking their facts', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 79K views: \"Exposing the misinformation on this app has other brands thinking before they post now (finally)\" Remake of their own video."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Noun''s own video caption."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Brands on this app have started checking their facts before they post. You''re welcome. For a long time you could say anything about a hair product on here and nobody checked. Then we started putting ingredient lists on screen. Now brands think twice. Good. That''s better for you no matter whose product you buy. Keep asking for the label. It works."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Finally. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'myth bust: a bigger bottle is better value', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 59K views: \"4 ounces that will last you 4-6 months\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: sizes are smaller because you need less, Oct 5 call, 6:25."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"yo lowkey the bigger bottle is the better deal tho"},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Not if you use three times as much. Value is how many uses you get, not how tall the bottle is. Ours are made so you need very little: two to three pumps of powder, a few drops of oil. Smaller bottle, plenty of uses. Divide the price by the uses. That''s the real number."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Price divided by uses. That''s the real number. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'viral format: 1a hair is not cooked', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 1.6M views: \"1A hair is COOKED..\" We flip the hook. Also BlackMask \"1a hair isn''t that bad\" (3.8M)."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"texture powder product page."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"1A hair is not cooked. People on this app act like pin-straight hair is a life sentence. It''s not. Straight hair shows everything, so it needs a product that''s light. Dry hair, two to three pumps of texture powder at the roots, then push it up and mess it with your fingers. That''s texture on 1A hair in ten seconds. You were never cooked. You were using the wrong stuff."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"You were never cooked. #noun #1ahair #straighthair"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'live promo: the cheapest way to buy noun', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 7.4M views: \"It''s not gonna get any lower\" Price-promo format."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: TikTok is always the cheapest source, flash sales on the lives every night, Oct 5 call, 41:59."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"You need to record a voice note up to 3 minutes long answering the questions below. Make sure you provide as many details as possible.\nCan we say the live is always the cheapest way to buy?\nWhat is tonight''s offer, and what time is the live (ET)?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"The cheapest way to buy Noun is not our website. It''s the live. Every night we run flash sales you can''t get anywhere else. (TONIGHT''S OFFER). We know our products aren''t cheap. This is how you get them for less. (TIME) tonight."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Cheapest way to get Noun: the live. (TIME) ET. #noun #tiktoklive #flashsale"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'live promo: last night on the live', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@based, 2.1M views: \"Who is on the BASED live?\" Live-promo format."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Steven''s live conversations with skeptics who switch, Oct 5 call, 20:00."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Last night on the live, (WHAT HAPPENED). Example: \"a guy came on to tell me his brand is better. Twenty minutes later he was asking which product to start with.\" That''s what happens when you put two labels side by side. We''re live again tonight at (TIME). Come be the next one."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"It happens every night. (TIME) ET. #noun #tiktoklive"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'how to use it: make it last twice as long', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 157K views: \"texture clay spoon size amount is goated\" How-much-to-use format."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"customers using 5-10 pumps, Oct 5 call, 47:33; usage amounts from the product pages."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"In the video, you could show what 2–3 pumps actually look like by dispensing it onto the palm, and maybe even demonstrate it on yourself."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"You''re probably using too much of this [show texture powder on screen]. Two to three pumps. Not ten. Hair oil: two to five drops. Not a palm full. Shampoo: on the scalp only. It lathers, so you don''t need more. We make the sizes smaller because you need less. Use them the way they''re meant to be used and one bottle goes a long way."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"You''re using too much. #nounnaturals #hairtips"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'live promo: bring the friend who uses another brand', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 67K views: \"W friend group, thx boys for showing love\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Steven''s live conversations with competitor fans, Oct 5 call, 20:00."},{"heading":"QUESTIONS FOR THE CLIENT","text":"What time is tonight''s live (ET)?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Tag the friend who uses another brand. Then bring him to the live tonight. (TIME). We bring people up, they tell us what they use, and we look at both labels together. No yelling. If his stuff is better, we''ll say it. If it''s not, he''ll know by the end. Either way, it''s a good show."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Tag him. (TIME) ET. #noun #tiktoklive"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'why not both?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 5.8M views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Start with a comb test on camera, the same way the reference opens with a side-by-side: comb through wet hair with our conditioner and show how easily the comb goes through. Screenshot of the comment will be in the video on editing."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Look at how easily this comb goes through. This is insane.\nBut don''t even take it from me, take it from this five-star review. Customer goes, \"I''ve tried so many natural brands, but Noun Naturals is truly on another level.\"\nYeah, so most natural conditioners skip quats and silicones, and they just don''t detangle. And I agree, the synthetic ones do feel super smooth, but quats and silicones build up on your hair. So instead, we put the work into the formula. Our conditioner uses a conditioning system made from amino acids and brassica oil. In lab testing on that ingredient: 66% less force to comb wet hair, and 70% less on dry hair.\nSo if you want a conditioner that''s gonna give you both natural and performance, rather than one over the other, it''s linked below. So lock in."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Natural or high-performing? You don''t have to pick one. No quats, no silicones, and it still detangles. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'what customers said after four weeks', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We took one of your videos that performed well and made a few small adjustments to the script. Please record it in a similar style: the same two-person conversation, sitting together, natural and unscripted in tone."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"A\tAnd Khaled, you know one of the things I love? Even when we were manufacturing and doing everything in your basement, we always wanted to know if it was actually working for people.\nB\tMm.\nA\tSo we asked our customers after four weeks. 94% said their hair felt softer and more manageable. 89% saw less breakage and shedding. And nine out of ten would recommend us to a friend.\nB\tExactly.\nA\tBut we also understand that not everyone''s gonna love our product. So you can try this high-performing product, and if you don''t like it, you get a satisfaction guarantee or your money back.\nB\tExactly.\nA\tSo I think, you know, we''re very confident in what we do, and if we weren''t confident, we wouldn''t offer that.\nB\tMm-hmm. That''s literally one of Noun Naturals'' foundations. If the customer isn''t 100% satisfied with the money they''re spending-\nA\tFacts."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"What our customers said after four weeks: 94% softer hair, 89% less breakage, 9 out of 10 would recommend. And if you don''t love it, satisfaction or your money back. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'this weekend''s lives', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@based, 2.7M views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the reference as a two-person skit: one person at the desk, the other standing in front of him with a phone. One static shot, Noun bottles on the desk."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"A\tDavid, who''s on the live right now?\nB\tUh, I''m watching the live right now.\nA\tNo, no, who''s, like, actually on the camera on the live right now?\nB\tYeah, like, I''m actually on, like, watching him give away shampoo.\nA\tOkay, so who''s on the live?\nB\tMe.\nA\tOkay, you''re watching it. Who''s in front of the camera literally giving away Noun to our followers?\nB\tYeah, so when they join the live, I''m on the live.\nA\tBut you''re in my office, in front of me, and there''s no camera anywhere. So what''s actually going on?"},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN TEXT","text":"We''re live every day. Come find out who''s on camera."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Live every day : (TIMES) ET. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'a natural leave-in', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 30K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate a video similar to the reference: a selfie shot from a low angle, close to your face, with your curls in frame after the leave-in. No talking, just the on-screen text and a trending sound. You can change the location (car, bathroom, office), but keep the concept the same."},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"The healthiest 3c curls on this app"},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Quat-free natural leave-in, by the way. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'you''re putting conditioner in the wrong place', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 13.1M views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate a video similar to the reference, including the process. Show the conditioner going on mid-lengths and ends only, not the scalp:\nStart by showing the result of applying conditioner incorrectly: greasy hair caused by applying it to the roots and scalp.\nThen demonstrate the correct way to use conditioner, applying it only to the mid-lengths and ends, avoiding the scalp.\nThroughout the video, make sure to clearly show the product bottle whenever you use it. At the end, highlight the product you used so viewers can easily identify it."},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"You''re putting conditioner in the wrong place"},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Conditioner goes on your mid-lengths and ends, not your scalp. Your scalp makes its own oil. Your ends don''t. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'this is terrible', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 40K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate a video similar to the reference. Hold the shampoo product up to the camera and demonstrate the results it provides on your hair"},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"Your natural shampoo wasn’t rejected by a chemist twice before launch"},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Our head chemist looked at our formula and said: this is terrible. He sent it back. Then he sent it back again. Nothing ships until he approves it, no matter how many people are waiting or what it costs us to wait. Annoying? Yes. It’s also why it works.  #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'no reason to have flat hair in 2026', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 7.4M views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate a video similar to the reference, including the process:\nRecord the before shot: Wet your hair, stand in front of the camera, and recreate the exact position and head movement shown in the reference. Remember your position so you can repeat it at the end.\nShow the process: Show the hair oil you’re going to use on camera, then show the amount of the product, apply the product, demonstrating each step of your routine.\nReveal the final result: Once your hair is fully styled, return to the same scene and repeat the exact pose and head movement from the beginning to highlight the transformation.\nHighlight the products: Finish by showing the hair oil you used to."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Hey, I totally get it, there''s no need to have flat hair when we''re in 2026! #noun #nounnaturals #flathair"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'dump your shampoo on the live', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 356K views"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Think your shampoo is better than ours? Bring it to the live tonight. (TIME). We''ll put your shampoo''s ingredient list on screen, go through it together, and compare it with ours. No guessing, no bullshit. If yours is better, we''ll say it. If ours is, you''ll see why. So grab your shampoo, join the live, and let''s find out what''s actually in your bottle."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"We''re live every night. Come on camera and show us what you''re using. (TIME) ET. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'can i use conditioner as a leave-in?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 110K views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We took one of your videos that performed really well, which shows that the format works, and made a few small adjustments to the script.\nPlease record the new video in a similar style. You can wear a different robe or slightly change the location, but keep the core concept the same."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"B\tYo, what are you doing?\nA\tWhat do you mean, what am I doing?\nB\tConditioner in a spray bottle? Come on.\nA\tYou don''t know about this glitch?\nB\tNo.\nA\tDude, I''m about to put you on a real leave-in glitch, all right? This is the secret to soft hair all day.\nB\tWhat is that?\nA\tEspecially if your hair gets dry, yo. A little conditioner, fill the rest with water, shake it up.\nB\tHe''s spraying it like it''s cologne. Whoa. Wait, what?\nB\tMm. That actually works? Are you kidding me?\nA\tDo you not see this hair on my guy? Just make sure your conditioner is quat-free, so it doesn''t build up.\nB\tOh wait, dude, you just put me on."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Putting your conditioner in a spray bottle to make a leave-in? Make sure it''s quat-free, so it doesn''t build up on your hair. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'parents, come on the live', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@based, 1.4M views"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Parents, get on the Noun live tonight. (TIME). Your kid asked for a natural shampoo and you want to know why. Fair. Come ask us anything: what''s in it, what''s not, why it costs what it costs. We''ll read the label with you. A lot of parents come in skeptical and end up using it themselves."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Parents, get on the Noun live. (TIME) ET. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'hair won''t hold? easy fix for that', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@blackmask_shop/video/7602980442446384415"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate a video similar to the reference, including the process. Show hair that won''t hold, then two to three pumps of texture powder at the roots on dry hair, work it in with your fingers, and show the result."},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"Hair won''t hold? Easy fix for that"},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Two to three pumps of texture powder at the roots, on dry hair. The clay gives your hair grip, so it holds. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'how to transform your hair', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 6.2M views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate a video similar to the reference, including the process.\nRecord the before shot: Wet your hair, stand in front of the camera, and recreate the exact position and head movement shown in the reference. Remember your position so you can repeat it at the end.\nShow the process: Apply the NOUN NATURALS hair styling products, demonstrating each step of your routine.\nReveal the final result: Once your hair is fully styled, return to the same scene and repeat the exact pose and head movement from the beginning to highlight the transformation.\nHighlight the products: Finish by showing the products you used to achieve the final look."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"How to transform your hair #nounnaturals #texturepowder #hairtutorial"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 2, 'you''re washing your hair wrong', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 3.4M views"},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate a video similar to the reference, including the process:\nWash your hair using a regular mass-market shampoo and show the bad result.\nShow how your hair looks after styling with the regular shampoo.\nRepeat the process using NOUNNATURALS products, showing each cleansing step.\nReveal the final result and highlight the difference.\nEnd with a quick reveal of the products used."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Hey, I totally get it – we all want to know how to make our shampoo-day hair look its best! So, here''s a little guide to help you out. #nounnaturals #hairtips"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'how to spot a good styling product', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"@soldafades on Instagram"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Khaled''s view: build-up in styling products comes from synthetic film-formers; for the sea salt spray he chose a sugar and olive-derived crosspolymer instead, to avoid build-up); Noun''s own sea salt spray video (45K, \"I hear you guys\")."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"A good styling product should wash out as easily as it goes in. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'where can i buy noun?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals Noun''s own video, picked by the team. Reply to the comment straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David on where people buy: discovery on TikTok, Amazon Prime for fast delivery, stopped paying for Amazon ads because of the spillover from TikTok, TikTok is always the cheapest way to buy, flash sales on the lives every night, Oct 5 call, 41:59; nounnaturals.com (ships worldwide with DHL Express, free shipping over 50 dollars)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"bro I SWEAR this isn''t in a SINGLE store near me  where tf am I supposed to get noun??\""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Three places: our site, Amazon, and TikTok Shop. If you want it at your door fast, Amazon Prime. If you want the best price, it''s always TikTok, and catch us on a live, because we run flash sales every single night. Outside the US? Our site ships worldwide, and shipping is free over 50 dollars. Funny thing: we stopped paying for Amazon ads a while ago. People still find us there, because they see us here first."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Our site, Amazon, or TikTok Shop. The best deals are on the live. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'apricot kernel oil is first on our list', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 37K views Founder to camera on what the ingredient list really shows (\"you flip the bottle around and it''s buried at the bottom of the ingredient list\"). Same label-reading talking head as your Week 1 turmeric video."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com hair oil page (full ingredient order starting with apricot kernel oil; absorbs quickly, no greasy residue; 2 to 5 drops on damp or dry mid-lengths and ends)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record it in a similar style to the reference: straight to the camera, with the hair oil in your hand, turning the bottle to show the back label."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Why did you choose apricot kernel oil as the main oil in the formula? If you tell us, we''ll add your reason to the script."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold the hair oil up to the camera, then flip it to the ingredient list.]\nFlip our hair oil over. The first ingredient isn''t black seed. It''s apricot kernel oil.\nIngredients on a label are listed from the biggest amount to the smallest, so that''s the largest part of the formula.\n[Run your finger down the label as you read.]\nAfter it: grape seed, sweet almond, castor, radish seed, argan, amla, black seed, pumpkin seed, batana, rosemary and patchouli. Vitamin E is at the end.\n[Put two drops on your fingertips and work them into your ends.]\nThe oil absorbs quickly and doesn''t leave a greasy residue. Two to five drops on your mid-lengths and ends, on damp or dry hair."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"The first ingredient in our hair oil is apricot kernel oil. Here''s the full list. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'shampoo and conditioner deal on the live', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 697K views: \"$5 shampoo & $5 Conditioner on #tiktoklive\" Your own deal announcement for a TikTok live. Recorded to camera before the live, not a clip from the live."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: flash sales on the lives every single night, TikTok is the cheapest way to get the products, Oct 5 call, 41:59; nounnaturals.com regular prices (shampoo 28 dollars, conditioner 32 dollars)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"This is a remake of your 697K deal video. Record it before the live as a short announcement straight to the camera, with the shampoo in one hand and the conditioner in the other. It''s not a clip from the live itself."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"What price and what time for this live?\nIs the deal limited (number of bottles or a time window)? We''ll say it on camera.\nDid the last 5 dollar deal sell out, and how fast? We want to use the real number. If it didn''t sell out, we''ll cut that line."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold the shampoo and the conditioner up to the camera, one in each hand.]\n(PRICE) shampoo. (PRICE) conditioner. Tonight on the TikTok live.\n[Tap the shampoo bottle.]\nThat''s not a typo. On our site, the shampoo is 28 dollars and the conditioner is 32.\nTonight on the live, (PRICE) each. (TIME) Eastern.\nWe run flash sales on the live every night, and this is tonight''s. (LIMIT: NUMBER OF BOTTLES OR TIME WINDOW.)\n(OPTIONAL, ONLY IF TRUE) Last time it sold out in (MINUTES). Don''t be late."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"(PRICE) shampoo & conditioner tonight on the live. (TIME) ET. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'our first customers grew up with us', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 2.5M views: \"Why I Created My Hair Products\" Founder story told alone, straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"started the brand at 18 in his basement in 2018 (Master Client Context Document); David: \"we were 18 when we first started this company\", the first customers grew with the brand and are now 25 to 35 and still with Noun, Oct 5 call, 10:18; a repeat customer on his twelfth order who buys for his family (Trustpilot review, July 2026, in the Master Client Context Document)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Tell this to the camera the same way as in the reference: on your own, straight to the camera, calm and proud, in your own words. If you have any photos or clips from the basement days, we''ll cut them in as B-roll."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Do you have photos or videos from the basement days (2018) we can use as B-roll?\nCan we show the Trustpilot review from the customer on his twelfth order on screen?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"How old were our first customers?\nMy age. I started this in my basement in 2018. I was eighteen.\n[Cut to basement B-roll.]\nAnd those same people are still ordering.\nThey grew up with us. Now they''re twenty-five, thirty, thirty-five, and they''re still with Noun.\nOne customer on Trustpilot is on his twelfth order. He buys for his whole family.\n[Show the Trustpilot review on screen.]\nIf you''ve been with us since the basement: thank you."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Our first customers were 18, like us. They''re still here. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'if your styling product makes your scalp itch, it''s bad. change my mind.', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals Noun''s own video, picked by the team. Opinion to camera with a \"Change my mind\" hook."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: customers say our styling products, compared to standard synthetic styling products, don''t make their hair feel itchy after using them, and their hair feels good and healthy, Oct 5 call, 7:41."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this the same way as in the reference: straight to the camera, same energy and pace, with the texture powder in your hand."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold the texture powder up to the camera.]\nIf your styling product makes your scalp itch, it''s a bad product. Change my mind.\nI don''t care how good it holds. It sits on your head all day.\n[Scratch your head, then stop and look at the camera.]\nIf you''re scratching your head after you style, your scalp is telling you something.\nWhen people switch from synthetic styling products to ours, this is one of the first things they tell us: it doesn''t make their hair feel itchy, and their hair feels good after.\nHold is half the job. Not irritating the skin it sits on is the other half.\nSo go ahead. Change my mind in the comments."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Hold is half the job. Your scalp is the other half. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'most founders can''t name their own ingredients', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 157K views: \"He forgot to mention Made in China... give the full context buddy\" Your own call-out to camera: you call out what other brands leave out, then give the full context."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: \"all these founders that are promoting their products, they don''t even know half of their ingredients\", while Khaled knows every ingredient, the chemistry of it, and breaks down why it helps, Oct 5 call, 38:23; David: Steven knows every single ingredient down to the chemical compounds, and when people ask for a product they get the ingredient behind it, Oct 5 call, 28:00."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record it in the same call-out style as the reference: straight to the camera, direct and a little bit cheeky, with a Noun bottle in your hand. We don''t name or show any brand."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold a Noun bottle up, turned to the ingredient list.]\nAsk the founder of your favorite hair brand what the third ingredient on the bottle does.\nMost of them can''t tell you.\nA lot of the founders promoting their products on this app don''t even know half of what''s in them.\n[Point at yourself, then off camera.]\nHere, ask me or Steven about any ingredient we use. You''ll get what it is, why it''s in there and what it does for your hair.\n[Tap the label.]\nThat''s not a flex. That should be the bare minimum when you''re putting something on people''s heads. So next time, ask for the full context."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"If the founder can''t explain the formula, who can? #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'i''m allergic to nuts. can i use the hair oil?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 44K views: \"Replying to @Jett thank me later brochacho #hairoiling\" Your own hair oil comment reply, straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com hair oil ingredient list (apricot kernel oil and sweet almond oil, scented with natural essential oils); David: essential oils can cause allergic reactions if you''re sensitive to them, people who react get a refund, Oct 5 call, 45:14."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"I have a nut allergy, is the hair oil safe for me?\""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Good question, and I''m glad you asked before buying. Our hair oil has apricot kernel oil and sweet almond oil in it. Both are on the ingredient list on our site. So if you react to nuts, talk to your doctor before you try it. Don''t guess. And we always say this: we scent with natural essential oils, and some people are sensitive to them. If you ever get a reaction, message us and we''ll refund you."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Apricot kernel and sweet almond oil are in the formula. Check with your doctor first. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'our hair oil won a second award', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 77K views Two-person skit: B asks \"Yo, what are you doing?\", throws the bottle to A and explains why it''s different. Same skit as your Week 1 \"Men''s Health picked it\" card."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com hair oil page (awards: Men''s Health Best Black Seed Hair Oil, original formula, December 2024, and Best Hair Oil for Dry and Damaged Hair; ingredients include argan, sweet almond, castor, batana and pumpkin seed oil; absorbs quickly, no greasy residue; 2 to 5 drops on damp or dry mid-lengths and ends)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"This is a remake of your 77K skit. Keep the same two-person setup: B walks in, throws the hair oil to A, and explains. Show the bottle clearly when it''s caught."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Which publication gave the \"Best Hair Oil for Dry and Damaged Hair\" award, and in what year? We want to say the name on camera.\nThe site says the Men''s Health award was for the original formula. Is it okay to say this bottle is \"the one Men''s Health picked\", and was the second award for the current formula?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[A stands at the mirror, touching his dry ends. B walks in holding the hair oil.]\nB: Yo, what are you doing?\nA: My ends are so dry, bro.\nB: Catch.\n[B throws the hair oil to A. A catches it.]\nA: Wait, isn''t this the one Men''s Health picked?\nB: That''s award number one. It was also named Best Hair Oil for Dry and Damaged Hair by (PUBLICATION).\n[A turns the bottle and reads the back.]\nA: Argan, sweet almond, castor, batana, pumpkin seed...\nB: Two to five drops on your mid-lengths and ends. Damp or dry.\n[A puts a few drops in his hands and works them through his ends.]\nA: It''s not even greasy.\nB: Two awards. One bottle."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Best Hair Oil for Dry and Damaged Hair. Award number two. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'castor oil won''t regrow your hair?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@crownderm/video/7511066934822046998"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com hair oil page (ingredient order: apricot kernel, grape seed, sweet almond, castor, then eight more plant oils and extracts and vitamin E; not a medical hair-loss treatment; see a dermatologist or trichologist)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Castor oil alone won''t regrow hair. Here''s where it sits in our blend. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'what are the 13 botanicals?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals: \"Reply to Benedict''s comment\" Comment-reply format: the comment on screen, then a single continuous selfie shot answering it straight to the camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"hair oil ingredient list (INCI) on nounnaturals.com."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"We counted 12 oils/extracts plus vitamin E (tocopherol) from the ingredient list on your site to make 13. Is that how you count the 13 botanicals?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"13 botanicals in the hair oil? name them then \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Okay. Apricot kernel. Grape seed. Sweet almond. Castor. Radish seed. Argan. Amla. Black seed. Pumpkin seed. Batana. Rosemary. Patchouli. And vitamin E. That''s the full list. Every one of them is on our site, so you don''t have to take my word for it."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: All 13, named. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'your hair shouldn''t feel gross three hours after styling', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop Silent texture powder demo with an on-screen hook (the same reference as your Week 1 card \"Hair won''t hold? Easy fix for that\")."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: people want styling products that don''t make their hair feel gross after three hours, ours is light and made for all-day results, Oct 5 call, 29:12; \"we never guarantee anything\", Oct 5 call, 28:00; texture powder page on nounnaturals.com (dry hair, 2 to 3 sprays from about 2 inches, matte all day)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference. No talking or script is needed.\nProduct: Glacial Clay Texture Powder. Film the morning styling and a check-in later the same day. Wear the same outfit and stand in the same spot for both so the comparison is clear. Show the real time on screen (a phone or clock in frame works)."},{"heading":"TO-DO LIST","text":"Morning: start with clean, dry, unstyled hair. Show the texture powder bottle to the camera.\nHold the bottle about 2 inches from your hair and spray 2 to 3 times at the roots.\nWork it in with your fingers and style. Show the finished look from the front and the side.\nLater in the day: same spot, same angle. Show the time in frame.\nRun your hands through your hair and touch the roots so viewers can see how it looks and moves.\nEnd with the texture powder bottle to the camera."},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"Your hair shouldn''t feel gross three hours after styling"},{"heading":"On-screen text:","text":"Shot 1: \"(TIME) styled with texture powder\"\nLater shot: \"(TIME) still matte\"\nLast shot: \"Glacial Clay Texture Powder\""},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Styled in the morning. Checked it later. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'how long does shipping take?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 31K views: \"Replying to @basedkaifanaccount we don''t mind inspiring other brands bro\" Comment-reply format: the comment on screen, answered straight to the camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"shipping info on nounnaturals.com (US 3 to 6 business days, worldwide DHL Express 2 to 4 business days, free shipping over $50); East Coast warehouse with a 4:00 p.m. ET same-day cutoff (Master Client Context Document, from your Trustpilot review reply)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Is the 4pm Eastern same-day shipping cutoff from your Trustpilot reply still current, and does it apply on weekdays only?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"how long does shipping take, I need it before the weekend \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"In the US, three to six business days. Our warehouse is on the East Coast, and orders placed before 4pm Eastern ship the same day. So if you need it soon, order early in the day. Outside the US, it''s DHL Express, two to four business days. And orders over fifty dollars ship free."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: US 3 to 6 business days, worldwide 2 to 4 with DHL. Free over $50. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'where our products are made', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views Your \"satisfaction guarantee or your money back\" video: Khaled and a second person in a calm, seated back-and-forth conversation, cut as a split screen."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"R&D in-house, manufacturing through contract manufacturers in New Jersey and Illinois (Master Client Context Document); comparison table on nounnaturals.com (US manufacturing, chemists, certified facilities)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this as the same two-person seated conversation as the reference. Calm, natural tone, like you''re just talking to each other. We''ll cut it as a split screen in editing."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Can we name New Jersey and Illinois on camera?\nAre all four products (shampoo, conditioner, hair oil, texture powder) made in the US? Your site says US manufacturing; we want to be sure it covers everything."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"A: Where is Noun actually made? Let''s settle it.\nB: Start with the formulas. Who makes those?\nA: We do. Our R&D is in-house.\nB: And the product itself?\nA: Contract manufacturers here in the US. New Jersey and Illinois.\nB: Certified facilities?\nA: Certified facilities. It''s on our site.\nB: So developed by us, made in the US.\nA: That''s it."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Developed in-house. Made in the US. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'does conditioner do anything after you rinse it out?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 77K views Your Men''s Health two-person \"catch\" skit: B asks what A is doing, throws A the bottle and explains why it''s different."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"conditioner page on nounnaturals.com (\"clinically designed to last up to 24 hours after rinsing\", \"24 hours of weightless hydration\")."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Same two-person \"catch\" skit as your Men''s Health video: B throws the conditioner to A. You can change outfits and location, keep the concept. Make sure the conditioner label faces the camera after the catch."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"B: Yo, what are you doing?\nA: Rinsing out my conditioner. Kind of pointless, it all washes off anyway.\nB: Bro. Catch.\n[B throws the conditioner to A.]\nA: What''s this?\nB: Our conditioner. It''s clinically designed to last up to 24 hours after you rinse it.\nA: After I rinse it?\nB: After you rinse it. 24 hours of weightless hydration.\nA: So rinsing it isn''t the end of it.\nB: Nope."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Designed to last up to 24 hours after you rinse. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'why is there radish in our hair oil?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 59K views: \"4 ounces that will last you 4-6 months\" Comment-reply format used for your Week 1 comment cards: the comment on screen, answered straight to the camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"hair oil ingredient list (INCI) on nounnaturals.com (radish seed oil, argan, batana, black seed); you reply to comments, Oct 5 call, 29:12."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"What does radish seed oil do in the hair oil, in your words? Is it there as a natural alternative to silicones for slip and shine? We won''t say anything about silicones on camera until you confirm."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"why is there RADISH in your hair oil \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Radish seed oil. Not the vegetable on your plate, the oil from the seeds. It sits in the same blend as argan, batana and black seed. (PLACEHOLDER: what radish seed oil does in the formula, from your voice note.) Every ingredient we use is listed on our site. See one you don''t recognize? Drop it in the comments and we''ll explain it."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Radish seed oil, explained. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'squeaky clean isn''t clean', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 2M views: \"shampoo hair is the absolute worst\""},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: people used to over-stripping shampoos feel clean out of the shower but their hair has no moisture; with your shampoo and conditioner their hair looks hydrated out of the shower, which makes it easier to style, Oct 6 call, 8:00."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Squeaky isn''t the same as clean. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'get interviewed on our live', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@based, 2.1M views: \"Who is on the BASED live?\" Live-promo format, recorded to camera (used for your Week 2 live promo \"Last night on the live\")."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Steven runs most of the lives and brings viewers into the live one on one, interview style, Oct 5 call, 20:00; Steven knows every ingredient down to the compounds, Oct 5 call, 28:00."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"This is a short promo recorded straight to the camera before the live, not a clip from a live. Steven is the best person to record it, since he''s the one bringing people on. Same quick energy as the reference."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"What time is tonight''s live (ET)?\nHow do viewers get brought up on camera? Do they request to join, or should they comment something?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Who wants to be on the live tonight? Not watching. On it.\nI bring people up one on one. Interview style. You and me, on camera.\nAsk me about your hair, your routine, or any ingredient on the back of your bottle. I''ll break it down.\n(TIME) Eastern. (HOW TO JOIN)."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Get interviewed on our live tonight. (TIME) ET. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'not every oil clogs your scalp', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@nylah.uk_/video/7283573816666639648"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"hair oil page on nounnaturals.com (absorbs quickly, no greasy residue; scalp massage before washing; scalp treatment 2 to 3 times a week; 2 to 5 drops on mid-lengths and ends)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Not every oil clogs your scalp. It depends on the oil and how you use it. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'the shampoo wars', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 135K views: \"Natural is the base line, performance is the differentiator\" Comment-reply format (used for your Week 2 comment cards): the comment on screen, answered straight to the camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: calling out Based Body Works, the \"shampoo wars\" where people reviewed shampoos and put them against each other, \"Based shampoo versus Noun shampoo\" was the biggest tagline in the space, Oct 6 call, 19:58; \"we never lie, we just call out the facts\", Oct 6 call, 14:31; props to Based for getting kids into haircare, Oct 5 call, 32:00."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this like the reference: answer the comment straight to the camera, with your shampoo in your hand. We''ll add the comment on screen in editing."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Are you okay with naming Based on camera in this video?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"who actually won the shampoo wars? \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"[Hold the shampoo up to the camera.]\nIf you were on this app back then, you remember.\nWe called out Based Body Works, and it turned into the shampoo wars. People reviewing shampoos and putting them up against each other on camera. Based shampoo versus Noun shampoo was everywhere.\nAnd real props to Based for one thing. They got a whole generation of kids into haircare.\nWho won? I''m not picking a winner. We don''t lie. We just call out the facts. So put both bottles next to each other and read the backs yourself."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: The shampoo wars. Read both labels. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'science-backed should be the minimum', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@blackmask_shop/video/7671795506716200206"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document, Oct 14 (beliefs: \"science backed should be on every product, whether it''s synthetic or natural\"; \"a lab, a stability test, a patch test\" is \"just doing your job\"; natural brands work with the same suppliers and labs as synthetic brands; generous to competitors, combative on the claim; shampoo uses decyl and lauryl glucoside, conditioner uses AminoSensyl)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Science-backed isn''t a feature. It''s the minimum. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'stump steven on the live', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 68K views: \"Comeback live tonight at 9pm EST\" Your own live announcement: short, straight to camera, one take, recorded before the live (not a live clip)."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: Steven knows every ingredient in your products down to the chemical compounds, Oct 5 call, 28:00; Steven runs the lives, reads the chat and brings viewers on one-on-one, Oct 5 call, 20:00."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Steven records this straight to camera, the same way as your \"Comeback live tonight at 9pm EST\" announcement: short, direct, one take. Hold up a random bottle (not a Noun product) while you talk."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"What time is the live (ET)?\nIs there a prize if a viewer stumps Steven? If not, we''ll remove that line."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold a random bottle up to the camera, label facing out.]\nRead me one ingredient I can''t explain. Tonight on the live, (TIME) Eastern.\nGrab any bottle in your bathroom. Shampoo, conditioner, body wash, whatever.\nRead me anything off the back.\nI''ll tell you what it is and what it does.\nI''ll bring you on the live one-on-one, so have the bottle ready.\n(ONLY IF THERE''S A PRIZE: If you stump me, (PRIZE).)\nSee you tonight."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Read Steven one ingredient he can''t explain. Live tonight, (TIME) ET. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'we read a 4-star review out loud', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 31K views Your own review-reply format: product in hand, read the customer''s words out loud, then answer them straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document, Oct 14 (Rich, 4-star Trustpilot review, Jul 2026: the texture powder hold was not strong enough; the response direction is a more concentrated formula without added grit; customer names first name only)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this the same way as in the reference: texture powder in your hand, read the review out loud word for word, then answer straight to camera. We''ll put a screenshot of the review on screen in the edit."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"We picked Rich''s 4-star Trustpilot review of the texture powder (he wanted more hold). Are you okay reading it on camera with his first name only? Please send us the exact review text or a screenshot. If you''d rather use a different real review, send that one instead.\nThe next version of the powder is more concentrated without added grit. Can we say that on camera? Is there a timing you want to share (or should we leave timing out)?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold the texture powder up to the camera.]\nThis is a 4-star review. We''re reading it out loud anyway.\n[Read Rich''s review word for word.] \"(REVIEW TEXT)\"\nFair. Rich wanted more hold.\nSo that''s what the next version is about.\nMore concentrated. No extra grit.\n(TIMING, only if you want to share it.)\nThanks, Rich. This is how the next version gets better."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"A 4-star review, read out loud. Here''s what we''re changing. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'duo or trio: which one should i get?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 24K views: \"Replying to @Draven why is noun sea salt spray taking so long to release? Here''s the answer\" Comment-reply format."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com (Duo $55, reg $60: shampoo and conditioner; Trio $99, reg $108: adds the hair oil; hair oil goes on mid-lengths and ends and works as a scalp treatment 2 to 3 times a week; award: Best Hair Oil for Dry and Damaged Hair)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Are the duo ($55) and trio ($99) prices on your site still current for this week?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"duo or trio, which one do i get??\""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Easy.\nThe duo is the shampoo and conditioner. Fifty-five dollars instead of sixty.\nThe trio adds the hair oil. Ninety-nine instead of one-oh-eight.\nIf you just want your wash day sorted, get the duo.\nIf your ends are dry, or you want to start a scalp treatment two to three times a week, get the trio.\nEither way, it''s cheaper than buying them one by one."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Duo for wash day. Trio if you want the oil too. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, '"clinically proven" on the front of the bottle', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@blackmask_shop/video/7675732014217088270 (\"Hydrolyzed keratin and rice protein have been shown to strengthen hair by up to 25%\", 793K views)"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document, Oct 14 (claims must rest on data: test first, then claim; RIPT results support skin tolerance only; no medical claims; no implied certification; talk about the claim, be generous to the people)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"\"Clinically proven\" on what? Always ask. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'did you change the formula?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 31K views: \"Replying to @irockali not letting you down king\" Comment-reply format."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com shampoo page (the 2025 version added 4 oz to the bottle); Master Client Context Document, Oct 14 (2025 rebuild: new contract manufacturer, reformulation with a former L''Oreal VP of Innovation; reformulated shampoo and conditioner re-released in September 2025)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Your shampoo page says the 2025 version added 4 ounces. Did the price stay the same? What is the bottle size now?\nWhat changed in the new formula that you''re happy to name on camera? (One or two things is enough.)\nCan we mention the former L''Oreal VP of Innovation on camera (without his name)? If not, we''ll cut that line."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"did y''all change the formula?? my shampoo bottle looks different \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Yes. Both.\nIn September 2025 we re-released our shampoo and conditioner with new formulas.\nWe moved to a new manufacturer and rebuilt them with a former L''Oreal VP of Innovation.\n(WHAT CHANGED, in one or two lines.)\nAnd the 2025 shampoo bottle has four more ounces in it. (PRICE: same as before?)\nSo if your bottle looks different, that''s why."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: New formula since Sep 2025. Four more ounces in the shampoo. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'why your scalp tingles', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views: \"Replying to @hideyokids6967 how to get the most out of hair oil...\" Comment reply to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com shampoo page (peppermint and eucalyptus blue mallee scent; for daily use); David: you never guarantee results, and customers should reach out if they don''t like a product, Oct 5 call, 28:00."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Is the tingle from the peppermint in the scent? If something else in the formula causes it, tell us what and we''ll change that line.\nIs a light tingle normal for most people, in your experience? We''ll keep your wording."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"why does my scalp feel all tingly after your shampoo \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"That''s the peppermint. (CONFIRM)\nOur shampoo is scented with peppermint and eucalyptus. That''s the fresh smell you get in the shower.\nA light tingle: (YOUR WORDS ON WHETHER THAT''S NORMAL).\nIf it ever burns or itches, rinse it out and message us. Every scalp is different, and we''d rather hear from you."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: That tingle is the peppermint. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'do you actually answer dms?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, \"Who''s been waiting for the noun curl line\" Your own silent clip: one simple action on camera, one line of on-screen text, background music, no talking."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com (support Mon to Fri, 8am to 8:30pm; average reply within 24 hours); Steven catching up on customer emails, Oct 6 call, 0:13; Steven replied to a customer whose friend recommended Noun and who had questions about the shampoo, Oct 6 call, 11:08."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference. No talking or script is needed. Steven at a laptop answering customer messages and emails. Have a shampoo bottle on the desk next to the laptop."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Do the support hours on your site (Mon to Fri, 8am to 8:30pm) cover TikTok and Instagram DMs too, or email only? Which time zone?"},{"heading":"TO-DO LIST","text":"Steven sits down at the laptop with the inbox open (blur or crop customer names and emails).\nClose-up of Steven typing a reply.\nClose-up of the screen as the reply sends (keep customer details hidden).\nSteven picks up the shampoo bottle from the desk, glances at the label, keeps typing.\nEnd on Steven closing the laptop or looking up at the camera."},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"Do you actually answer DMs?"},{"heading":"On-screen text lines (one per shot):","text":"Yes. A real person.\nMonday to Friday, 8am to 8:30pm\nAverage reply: within 24 hours"},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Real people answer. Mon to Fri, 8am to 8:30pm. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'your hair isn''t the problem, it''s build-up', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@actandacre/video/7164532080750136618"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document, Oct 14 (Khaled rejects synthetic film-formers that build up; the sea salt spray uses a sugar- and olive-derived crosspolymer so it does not build up; men''s grooming customers want hold without buildup); nounnaturals.com shampoo page (cleansers: decyl glucoside and lauryl glucoside; for daily use; color-safe); David: hair hydrated out of the shower instead of over-stripped, Oct 6 call, 8:00."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Flat hair might be build-up, not your hair. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'barbers ranked the top haircuts for 2026', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 26K views: \"According to over 50+ barbers these are going to be the most popular men''s haircuts\" Your own video: a ranked list of haircuts, straight to camera, counting down to number one."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"your own video above (survey of over 50 barbers). The top 3 haircuts come from you (see questions)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We took one of your videos that performed really well, which shows that the format works, and made a few small adjustments to the script. Please record it in a similar style. We''ll add a photo of each haircut on screen in the edit."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"This is a remake of your \"50+ barbers\" video. What were the top 3 haircuts in your survey?\nIs that survey still current for 2026, or should we say \"this year\" without a year?\nOptional: which Noun product would you use to style each cut? If you tell us, we''ll add one line per cut."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"According to over fifty barbers, these are going to be the most popular men''s haircuts this year.\nNumber three: (CUT 3).\n[Photo of cut 3 on screen.]\nNumber two: (CUT 2).\n[Photo of cut 2 on screen.]\nAnd number one: (CUT 1).\n[Photo of cut 1 on screen.]\nWhich one are you getting next? Tell us in the comments."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"50+ barbers, top 3 haircuts. Which one''s yours? #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'synthetic texture powder vs ours', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 191K views: \"Does noun have the highest performing texture powder?\" Your own talking-head video that opens with a question about your texture powder and answers it to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com texture powder page (volcanic silica, Canadian glacial clay, plant-derived powders; no aerosols, synthetics or microplastics; 2 to 3 sprays on dry hair from about 2 inches; matte all day); Master Client Context Document (Khaled challenges the belief \"natural means you have to compromise\")."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this the same way as your 191K video: straight to camera, open with the question, texture powder in your hand. Week 2 answered \"prove it\" with texture, hold and volume, so this one is only about what''s inside the bottle."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold the texture powder up to the camera.]\nDoes a texture powder have to be synthetic to actually perform? No.\nA lot of people think natural means you have to compromise. We don''t believe that.\n[Turn the bottle so the label faces the camera.]\nHere''s what''s in ours: volcanic silica, Canadian glacial clay and plant-derived powders.\nHere''s what''s not: no aerosols, no synthetics, no microplastics.\n[Spray two to three times on dry hair, from about two inches away, then work it in.]\nTwo to three sprays on dry hair, from about two inches away. Matte, all day.\nSo next time someone tells you natural can''t hold up, ask them what''s in theirs."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Natural doesn''t mean you have to compromise. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'one shampoo for thinning hair', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@malihaihenacho/video/7628950450745806103"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (shampoo is sulfate-free, cleans with decyl and lauryl glucoside; glucosides mean a clean wash that does not over-strip); nounnaturals.com shampoo page (daily use, color-safe); nounnaturals.com hair oil page (not a medical hair-loss treatment, see a dermatologist or trichologist)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Thin hair? Start with a wash that doesn''t over-strip. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'will conditioner weigh my fine hair down?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 97K views: \"Replying to @aidoku need a few more weeks\" Comment reply to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com conditioner page (\"24 hours of weightless hydration\", quat-free, for every hair type); nounnaturals.com (10-day hassle-free returns, satisfaction guaranteed)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"For fine hair, how much conditioner do you recommend, and where should it go? We''ll add your tip to the answer."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"i have super fine hair, won''t conditioner just make it flat? \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Fair question. Ours is made for every hair type, and that includes fine hair.\nIt''s quat-free, and it''s built for weightless hydration. Twenty-four hours of it.\n(YOUR TIP FOR FINE HAIR: HOW MUCH AND WHERE)\nAnd if it''s not for you, you''ve got our 10-day hassle-free return."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Weightless hydration, made for every hair type. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'where argan oil sits on our label', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 34K views Silent BTS: product shown to camera, applied, then the final look. No talking."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com hair oil page (ingredient list in label order, argan is sixth; 2 to 5 drops on damp or dry mid-lengths and ends)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference. No talking or script is needed. Product: Hair Oil. We''ll add the on-screen text in editing."},{"heading":"TO-DO LIST","text":"Hold the hair oil up to the camera and turn it so the label is visible.\nClose-up of the ingredient list on the bottle.\nDispense 2 to 5 drops into your palm.\nRub your hands together and apply to mid-lengths and ends.\nShow the final result, then the bottle once more."},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"Argan oil: here''s where it actually sits on our label"},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN TEXT","text":"Apricot kernel, grape seed, sweet almond, castor, radish seed..."}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'people who hated us in the comments are customers now', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 31K views: \"Replying to @basedkaifanaccount we don''t mind inspiring other brands bro\" Comment reply to a competitor fan, straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Steven: people join the live saying \"Based is better\", he has a civil conversation with them and they switch over to Noun, Oct 5 call, 20:00; haters in the comments convert after you talk to them, \"we never lie, we just call out the facts\", Oct 6 call, 14:31."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this as a reply to the comment, the same way as the reference: comment sticker on screen, straight to camera, relaxed. Steven, this one is best coming from you, since you run the lives."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Is it okay to show \"Based\" in the comment sticker, or should we keep the brand name out?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"based is better \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Some of our customers started exactly here. In our comments, telling us another brand is better.\nSame thing on our lives. People come in saying \"Based is better.\"\nI don''t argue with that. I just talk to them like a normal person.\nAnd a lot of them end up switching over to Noun.\nWe never lie. We just call out the facts.\nSo if you think we''re not it, come say it on the live. Let''s talk."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Replying to @(user) we''d rather talk than argue. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'giveaway on tonight''s live', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 356K views: \"Every juggle is a dollar off on TikTok Live tonight\" Your own recorded promo skit for a live: one person announces the deal to camera, a second person walks in and argues, the first turns back to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nightly lives on TikTok, Oct 5 call, 20:00 and 41:59. Prize, time and entry rules: (PLACEHOLDERS) until you confirm them."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this as a separate promo, the same way as the reference: white wall, two people, fast and funny. No live clips needed. Hold the prize up to the camera instead of the soccer ball."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"What''s the giveaway prize, what time, and how do people enter?\nHow is the winner picked, and is it announced on the live?\nWho plays A and who plays B?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[A holds the (PRIZE) up close to the camera.]\nA: We''re giving this away on TikTok Live tonight.\n[B walks into frame.]\nB: Yo, what are you doing, bro?\nA: Telling them about the giveaway.\nB: You''re not supposed to tell them yet!\nA: Nah, they need to know.\n[B walks off, shaking his head.]\n[A turns back to the camera.]\nA: (TIME) Eastern. To enter: (HOW TO ENTER). (HOW THE WINNER IS PICKED). See you on the live."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Giveaway tonight on the live. (TIME) ET. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'do you have a subscription?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 31K views: \"Replying to @irockali not letting you down king\" Comment-reply format."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com texture powder page (subscription option); \"we''re hopping back on subscriptions\", Oct 5 call, 41:59; Steven: \"we haven''t fully set it up yet, but that''s something that''s in the works\", Oct 5 call, 43:17."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Your site shows a subscription option for the texture powder. On the Oct 5 call you said subscriptions are coming back. Which products can be subscribed to right now, and is there a discount?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"is there a subscription so i don''t run out? \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"For the texture powder, yes.\nYou can pick the subscription option right on the product page.\nFor everything else, it''s in the works. We''re bringing subscriptions back. (WHICH PRODUCTS AND WHEN, IF YOU CAN SHARE)\nFollow so you see it when it''s live."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Texture powder, yes. The rest is in the works. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'hair oil isn''t a girl thing', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 7.4M views Silent before and after transformation with a hair product, no talking (Week 1 used it for a hair oil BTS)."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com (products are unisex); nounnaturals.com hair oil page (2 to 5 drops on damp or dry mid-lengths and ends; absorbs quickly, no greasy residue; for straight, wavy, curly and coily hair)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference. No talking or script is needed. Product: Hair Oil. A guy should be on camera for this one."},{"heading":"TO-DO LIST","text":"Stand in front of a mirror with the hair oil in hand, hook text on screen.\nDispense 2 to 5 drops into your palm, close enough that we can count them.\nRub your hands together and work the oil through your mid-lengths and ends.\nStyle your hair with your fingers and look up into the mirror.\nEnd on the bottle in frame."},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"Hair oil isn''t a girl thing"},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN TEXT","text":"2 to 5 drops"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'do you have anything for coarse hair?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 24K views: \"Replying to @ThegoatConnor they started listening to daddy\" Comment reply to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"\"we want to make products for all different types of hair types... straight, pin straight hair to curly to wavy to coarse hair\", \"we have no products for very, very coarse hair\", still developing and growing the line, Oct 5 call, 12:36; curl line (Curl Chemistry) pre-orders planned (Master Client Context Document)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Is there anything you can say about coarse hair plans, even \"it''s being worked on\"? If not, we''ll leave it at \"not yet\".\nCan we say the name Curl Chemistry on camera, and is there a pre-order date we can share?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"do y''all have anything for coarse hair or nah\""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Not yet. And I''d rather tell you that than sell you something that isn''t made for you.\nOur goal is products for every hair type. Pin straight, wavy, curly, coarse.\nWe''re still building the line. Next up is our curl line, with pre-orders coming. (PRE-ORDER DATE IF YOU CAN SHARE)\n(WHAT YOU CAN SAY ABOUT COARSE HAIR)\nFollow so you see every drop."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Not yet. Every hair type is the goal. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'girls who use noun: we want to see you', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 45K views: \"Natural Innovation isn''t easy - but I can promise we''re on the forefront of it\" Opens on a montage of comments, then straight to camera: \"I hear you guys\", and ends by asking for comments."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"customer base has always been 50/50 while social presence is mostly male, \"how are we going to get more female faces involved?\", Oct 5 call, 8:15; \"we need a female face\", Oct 6 call, 21:22; nounnaturals.com (shampoo, conditioner, hair oil and texture powder are unisex)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this the same way as the reference: open on a quick montage of comments from girls who use Noun (we''ll make them in Canva or CapCut), then straight to camera. Week 1 answered \"can girls use this?\", so this one is only an invite for girls to film and tag you."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"What happens when a girl tags you: do you repost it, feature her on the page, send product?\nIs there a hashtag or tag you want them to use?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Open on a montage of comments from girls who use Noun.]\nI hear you, girls.\nHalf of the people who buy Noun are women. But look at this page. It''s mostly guys.\nWe need a female face on here. So this is your invite.\n[Hold up the shampoo, conditioner, hair oil and texture powder one by one.]\nIf you use our shampoo, conditioner, hair oil or texture powder, film your routine and tag us. (WHAT YOU OFFER: REPOST, FEATURE OR PRODUCT)\nDrop a comment if you''re in."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Girls who use Noun: film it and tag us. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'all natural doesn''t mean it works?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@jsndeals/video/7681567275807264014"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (claim only what can be backed: test first, then claim; no medical or treatment claims); nounnaturals.com hair oil page (not a medical hair-loss treatment, see a dermatologist or trichologist)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"\"All natural\" tells you what it''s made of, not whether it works. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'can i use the hair oil on curly or coily hair?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 44K views: \"Replying to @Jett thank me later brochacho #hairoiling\" Comment-reply format: hair oil advice, straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com hair oil page (for straight, wavy, curly and coily hair; 2 to 5 drops on damp or dry mid-lengths and ends; absorbs quickly, no greasy residue)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"does the hair oil work on coily hair or is it only for straight hair?\""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"It''s made for all of them. Straight, wavy, curly, coily. Two to five drops on your mid-lengths and ends, damp or dry. It absorbs quickly, so it won''t sit greasy on top of your curls."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Straight, wavy, curly, coily. 2 to 5 drops on mid-lengths and ends. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'vitamin e in a hair oil', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 40K views Silent product BTS with on-screen text (same reference as the Week 1 BTS card \"This is terrible\")."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com hair oil page (INCI: tocopherol (vitamin E); 2 to 5 drops on damp or dry mid-lengths and ends); nounnaturals.com conditioner page (INCI includes tocopherol)."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Why did you put vitamin E (tocopherol) in the hair oil? If you tell us in your own words, we can add one line about it to the on-screen text or caption."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference. No talking or script is needed. Product: Hair Oil (the Conditioner can appear at the end)."},{"heading":"TO-DO LIST","text":"Hold the hair oil bottle up to the camera.\nTurn it around to show the ingredient list and point to \"tocopherol\".\nPut 2 to 5 drops in your palm and work them through damp mid-lengths and ends.\nShow the conditioner bottle next to the hair oil.\nEnd on both bottles next to the finished hair."},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"Tocopherol is on our hair oil label. Here''s what it is."}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'why is there alcohol in your conditioner?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals Comment-reply format, straight to camera (same reference as the Week 1 comment cards \"Natural shampoo isn''t supposed to foam\" and \"Why is your bottle so small for that price?\")."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com conditioner page (INCI: brassica alcohol, cetyl alcohol; quat-free). \"Fatty alcohols soften, they''re not the drying kind\" is general ingredient knowledge, not from your materials: please confirm (question below)."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Is it right to say brassica alcohol and cetyl alcohol are fatty alcohols that soften hair, not the drying kind of alcohol? Please correct the wording if you''d explain it differently."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"why is there ALCOHOL in your conditioner?? doesn''t that dry your hair out\""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Read the full name. Brassica alcohol and cetyl alcohol. Those are fatty alcohols. They''re in there to soften your hair, not dry it out. Same word, different ingredient."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Not every alcohol on a label is the drying kind. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'meet steven', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals Two-person conversation, split screen, plain studio background: Khaled and a team member talk to each other about the brand."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Steven is VP of Operations (Noun video caption 7607246610774510861 and Oct calls); Steven runs most of the lives and brings viewers onto the live 1:1 (Oct 5 call, 20:00); lives are recorded and Steven writes down timestamps while live (Oct 5 call, 21:28); Steven knows every ingredient down to the chemical compounds (Oct 5 call, 28:00); Steven replies to customer emails (Oct 6 call, 0:13 and 11:08)."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Is \"VP of Operations\" the title Steven wants on screen?\nAnything else you want people to know about Steven? We''ll only add what you tell us."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Film this like the reference: the two of you, split screen, talking to each other in a plain studio setup. Khaled is A, Steven is B. Keep it casual and use your own words."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"A: If you''ve been on our lives, you already know this guy. Steven, introduce yourself.\nB: I''m Steven, VP of Operations at Noun.\nA: He runs most of our lives.\nB: Most of them, yeah. I read the chat, and sometimes I bring you onto the live one-on-one.\nA: And while he''s live, he''s writing down timestamps so we can clip the best moments later.\nA: Ask him about any ingredient we use. He knows them down to the chemical compounds.\nB: And if you email us, I''m one of the people replying.\nA: Say hi to Steven in the comments."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"The guy behind the lives. Say hi to Steven. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'trimming won''t make your hair grow faster', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 37K views: \"Replying to @burgool\" Comment reply to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com hair oil page (2 to 5 drops on damp or dry mid-lengths and ends); conditioner on mid-lengths and ends (as in the Week 1 card \"You''re putting conditioner in the wrong place\"). \"Hair grows from the scalp, a trim doesn''t make it grow faster\" is general hair knowledge, not from your materials: confirm with client (question below)."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"The trimming part is general hair knowledge, not from your materials. Are you comfortable saying hair grows from the scalp and a trim doesn''t make it grow faster? Correct anything you''d say differently."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"if i trim my hair every month will it grow faster??\""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"No. Your hair grows from your scalp, not from your ends, so cutting the ends won''t speed it up. If you''re growing it out, take care of the lengths: two to five drops of hair oil on your mid-lengths and ends, conditioner on your mid-lengths and ends, and trim when you need it."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Hair grows from the scalp, not the ends. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'the world''s first all-natural hair styling powder', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop Silent texture powder how-to with an on-screen hook (same reference as the Week 1 BTS card \"Hair won''t hold? Easy fix for that\")."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com texture powder page (\"world''s first all natural hair styling powder\"; volcanic silica, Canadian glacial clay, plant-derived powders; 100% natural, vegan, cruelty-free; no aerosols, synthetics or microplastics; dry hair, 2 to 3 sprays from about 2 inches; matte all day)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference. No talking or script is needed. Product: Glacial Clay Texture Powder."},{"heading":"TO-DO LIST","text":"Start with dry, unstyled hair.\nHold the texture powder up to the camera.\nSpray 2 to 3 times at the roots from about 2 inches away.\nWork it in with your fingers and style.\nShow the matte finish from a few angles.\nEnd on the bottle next to the finished hair."},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"The world''s first all natural hair styling powder"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'can i use the texture powder with gel?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 34K views Silent one-motion styling BTS (same reference as the Week 1 BTS card \"We''re sampling a hair clay\")."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com texture powder page (dry hair, 2 to 3 sprays from about 2 inches, matte all day). Using the powder together with gel is NOT from your materials: it is shown only as a demo until you confirm (question below)."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"IMPORTANT: Do you recommend using the texture powder together with a gel? If yes: powder first or gel first, and how much gel? If no, we''ll change this card to a powder-only demo."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference. No talking or script is needed. Products: Glacial Clay Texture Powder and a small amount of gel (only if you confirm the combination above)."},{"heading":"TO-DO LIST","text":"Start with dry, unstyled hair.\nShow the texture powder to the camera.\nSpray 2 to 3 times at the roots from about 2 inches away.\nUse one smooth hand movement to work it in.\nAdd a small amount of gel on top and shape the style.\nShow the final result."}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'your hair doesn''t get used to your shampoo', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 32K views: \"Replying to @Benedict and noun on the front lines of innovation...\" Reads a comment out loud, then answers it in one continuous take, straight to camera, in the bathroom."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (founder''s view: synthetic film-formers in styling products build up; he prefers natural options that don''t); nounnaturals.com texture powder page (no synthetics; zero residue, zero buildup). \"Hair doesn''t build a tolerance to shampoo\" is general hair knowledge, not from your materials: confirm with client (question below)."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"\"Your hair doesn''t get used to your shampoo\" is general hair knowledge, not from your materials. Do you agree, and would you explain it with build-up the way the script does? Correct anything you''d say differently."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable.\nFilm it like the reference: read the comment out loud, then answer in one take, straight to camera."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"my hair got used to my shampoo so now it doesn''t work anymore \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Your hair didn''t get used to it. Hair doesn''t build a tolerance. What builds up is product. A lot of styling products use synthetic film-formers that stack up wash after wash. That''s why our texture powder has no synthetics and leaves zero buildup."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Your hair didn''t get used to it. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'you just need to know better natural', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@typehairofficial/video/7605038497535233310"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com ingredient lists (hair oil: Nigella sativa (black seed), Emblica (amla); shampoo: decyl glucoside, lauryl glucoside); Master Client Context Document (glucosides mean a clean wash that does not over-strip)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"You just need to know more about natural products. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'sodium phytate and hard water', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 256K views: \"The only tutorial you''ll ever need\" Silent step-by-step tutorial with on-screen text, no talking."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com shampoo page (ingredient list includes sodium phytate)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference. No talking or script is needed.\nProduct: shampoo."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Sodium phytate is near the end of our shampoo list. In one short line, how would you explain what it does in the formula? (Is \"it helps with hard water\" how you would put it?) We''ll use your words for the on-screen text."},{"heading":"TO-DO LIST","text":"Hold the shampoo bottle up to the camera.\nTurn it around and zoom in on the ingredient list on the back.\nPoint to \"sodium phytate\" near the end of the list.\nPump some shampoo into your hand and lather it.\nEnd on the front of the bottle."},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"The ingredient nobody reads at the end of our shampoo list\nOn-screen text (zoom on the ingredient list): Sodium phytate. (ONE-LINE ROLE, FROM YOUR ANSWER)"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'things that will never be in our products', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 332K views Silent BTS: on-screen text hook, then the products shown one by one, ending on all products to camera. No talking."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (sulfate-free; no vague \"natural fragrance\" wording, fragrance listed per US and EU rules); nounnaturals.com conditioner page (quat-free); nounnaturals.com texture powder page (no aerosols, synthetics or microplastics)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference. No talking or script is needed.\nProducts: shampoo, conditioner, hair oil, texture powder."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Please confirm this list: sulfates, quats, aerosols, synthetics, microplastics, vague \"natural fragrance\" wording. Do these apply to all your products, or should we tie each one to a product (for example aerosols and microplastics to the texture powder)? Anything you want to add (for example silicones or parabens)?"},{"heading":"TO-DO LIST","text":"Line up the bottles on a table.\nPick them up one by one and flip each to the back label.\nShampoo: hold it for the \"Sulfates\" line.\nConditioner: hold it for the \"Quats\" line.\nTexture powder: hold it for the \"Aerosols, synthetics, microplastics\" line.\nTurn a bottle to the fragrance line on the ingredient list for the last text line.\nEnd with all the products together in one shot."}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'why we went all-in on 15-year-olds this year', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 104K views: \"New Samples of our 100% natural high performing curl cream and leave in are in\" Casual talking head to camera opening with a shout-out (\"Yo shout out...\"), with clips and photos overlaid while he talks."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: never targeted kids before this year, Oct 5 call, 10:18; Steven: Gen Alpha 15 to 18 are very product-driven and are sold once they feel the performance, Oct 5 call, 17:53; David: a lot of kids have a fear of going bald, Oct 5 call, 35:07; David: products must score green on Yuka, the app blew up with 15 to 18-year-olds who scan products at Target, Oct 5 call, 41:14."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this straight to camera, casual and energetic like the reference. We''ll add the overlays in editing."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Can you send us a screen recording of a Yuka scan of one of your products? We''d use it as the overlay."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Yo, shout out to the fifteen-year-olds in our comments. This year we started making videos for you. Here''s why.\n[Overlay: screen recording of a Yuka scan.]\nYou go to Target and you scan products left and right. Is this good for me or not? That''s why our products have to score green on Yuka.\n[Back to camera.]\nA lot of you are worried about going bald, and you''re already paying attention to what you put on your head.\n[Overlay: shampoo lathering in hands.]\nAnd you''re product-driven. Once you actually feel the difference, you''re sold."}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'betaine in our conditioner', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 6.2M views Silent before and after: the hair before, the product being applied, then the result in the same pose. No talking."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com conditioner page (ingredient list includes betaine)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference. No talking or script is needed.\nProduct: conditioner."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Can we say on screen where your betaine comes from (for example sugar beets)? We didn''t find it on your site, so we left it out for now.\nIn a few words, what does betaine do in the conditioner? We''ll use your words for the on-screen text."},{"heading":"TO-DO LIST","text":"Start in the shower with freshly shampooed, wet hair.\nShow the conditioner bottle to the camera.\nTurn it around and point to \"betaine\" on the ingredient list.\nPump conditioner into your hand.\nApply it to your hair in one smooth movement.\nShow the result, then the bottle one more time."},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"Ever read the back of your conditioner?\nOn-screen text (on the ingredient list): Betaine. (ONE-LINE DESCRIPTION, FROM YOUR ANSWER)"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'natural doesn''t automatically mean safe', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 45K views Khaled to camera in the lab coat: opens on a montage of comments, \"I hear you guys\", explains the problem, then how Noun handles it, and closes asking for comments."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (\"What''s natural can also be very toxic\"; EWG-based ingredient blacklist given to contract manufacturers; 2026 leave-in formula rejected because its PHMB preservative is EU-restricted)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this straight to camera in your lab coat, the same way as the reference. We''ll open the video with on-screen comments, as in the reference."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Opening: on-screen montage of comments saying natural means safe.]\nI hear you guys. But natural doesn''t automatically mean safe. What''s natural can also be very toxic.\nThat''s why we don''t just pick ingredients because they come from a plant. Our manufacturers get a blacklist of ingredients they''re not allowed to use, built on EWG data.\nAnd this year we had a leave-in formula that we didn''t launch. The preservative in it, PHMB, is restricted in the EU. If a formula can''t pass the rules in every market we sell in, it''s out.\nNatural is where we start. It''s not the only test. Leave your questions in the comments."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Natural is where we start. It''s not the only test. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'what a scalp-health dermatologist would tell you', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@aamnaadel/video/7675065639383600406"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: the focus is long-term hair and scalp benefit, not just styling, Oct 5 call, 35:07; Oct 6 call (hydrated out of the shower vs over-stripped \"feel clean\"); nounnaturals.com hair oil page (not a medical hair-loss treatment, see a dermatologist or trichologist)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"What a scalp-health dermatologist would tell you. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'our live from the other side', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 60K views: \"Who''s been waiting for the noun curl line\" Short silent clip with one on-screen text line over music, no talking."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Steven runs the lives, reads and interacts with the chat, and brings viewers on one on one, Oct 5 call, 20:00; Steven writes timestamps of good moments on a notepad while he''s live, Oct 5 call, 21:28."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference. No talking or script is needed.\nWe don''t have clips from your lives yet, so this needs to be filmed fresh during one of your next lives: someone stands behind Steven with a second phone and films the live from your side."},{"heading":"TO-DO LIST","text":"Film the phone being set up for the live, from behind.\nSteven reading the chat.\nSteven bringing a viewer on camera.\nSteven writing a timestamp on his notepad while live.\nClose-up of the notepad.\nEnd on a wide shot of the setup."},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"What our live looks like from the other side"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'can i use the hair oil every day?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 32K views: \"Replying to @LUCA Happy to say this is releasing really, REALLY, soon\" Comment reply to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com hair oil page (FAQ: a small amount can be used daily; 2 to 5 drops on damp or dry mid-lengths and ends; scalp massage before washing; scalp treatment 2 to 3 times a week)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"can i use the hair oil every day or is that too much \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"[Hold the hair oil up to the camera.]\nEvery day? Yes. Just keep it small.\nTwo to five drops on your mid-lengths and ends, damp or dry.\nUsing it on your scalp is a different job. Massage it in before you wash, two to three times a week.\nSo: a few drops on the ends every day, scalp treatment two to three times a week."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: A few drops daily on the ends, scalp treatment 2 to 3 times a week. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'do you guys sell gift cards?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 129K views: \"Replying to @. At least we fill the whole bottle\" Comment reply to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com (gift card is available on the site)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"do you guys have gift cards? my brother''s birthday is next week\""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"We do. Noun gift cards are on our website. Get him one and let him pick what he wants: shampoo, conditioner, hair oil or texture powder. Happy birthday to your brother."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Yes, gift cards are on our site. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'halloween live', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@based, 2.1M views: \"Who is on the BASED live?\" Short live-promo talking head to camera, opening with a question about who''s on the live."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Saturday, Oct 31 is Halloween; Steven runs the lives and brings viewers on one on one, Oct 5 call, 20:00; nightly flash sales on the lives, Oct 5 call."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this as a short promo straight to camera before the live, the same way as the reference. We don''t have live clips, so this is filmed separately."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Saturday is Halloween. Are you going live? What time, and is there a special deal or prize?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Who''s pulling up to the Halloween live tonight?\n(TIME) Eastern, right here on TikTok.\nCome in costume and show us your Halloween hair. Steven''s bringing people on camera.\n(HALLOWEEN DEAL).\nBest costume on camera gets (PRIZE). See you tonight."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Halloween live tonight. (TIME) ET. Come in costume. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'can a shampoo bring your hairline back?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcXgnsXqTt8/"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: \"we never guarantee anything\", every scalp is different, Oct 5 call, 28:00; nounnaturals.com hair oil page (not a medical hair-loss treatment, see a dermatologist or trichologist); Master Client Context Document (no medical or cure claims; glucosides mean a clean wash that does not over-strip)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"No shampoo should promise your hairline back. Here''s what it can do. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'glucosides: the cleanser in our shampoo', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 40K views: \"Just testing the final batch (24 months in the making)\" Silent product BTS with on-screen text (same format as the Week 1 card \"This is terrible\")."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com shampoo ingredient list (decyl glucoside, lauryl glucoside); Master Client Context Document (glucoside-based, sulfate-free washing; \"glucosides mean a clean wash that does not over-strip\"); David: the shampoo foams very well and is still 100% natural, Oct 5 call, 12:36."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Can we say on screen that glucosides are made from plant sugar? We left it out until you confirm."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference. No talking or script is needed. Product: the shampoo."},{"heading":"TO-DO LIST","text":"Hold the shampoo bottle up to the camera.\nTurn it around and show the ingredient list, close enough to read.\nPump the shampoo into your hand.\nWork it into wet hair and show the lather building.\nEnd on the bottle next to the lather."},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"The cleanser in our shampoo: glucosides"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'is texture powder all the same?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@edwinthebarber/video/7330499319478504747"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com texture powder page (plant-derived powders; 100% natural, vegan, cruelty-free; 2 to 3 sprays from about 2 inches on dry hair; matte all day)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Not all texture powders are made the same. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'live: ask us about your scalp', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@based, 3M views: \"Is BASED live right now?\" Recorded live promo, straight to camera (used for the Week 2 card \"Live promo: Two weeks of lives\")."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"customers deal with flakes and itchy scalp, scalp less itchy after using the shampoo, conditioner and oil, Oct 5 call, 6:25 and 7:41; people ask about frizz and dry scalp on the lives and in comments, \"we never guarantee anything\", every scalp is different, we explain which ingredients are in the product, Oct 5 call, 28:00; Steven runs the lives, Oct 5 call."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this as a short promo straight to the camera, the same way as in the reference. No live clips needed. Steven is the best fit since he runs the lives."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"What time is Sunday''s live (ET)?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Straight to the camera.]\nSunday live: everything scalp.\nFlakes, itch, dry scalp, oily by noon. Bring the question you''ve been too embarrassed to comment.\n(TIME) Eastern.\nWe''ll tell you which ingredients do what, so you know what to try.\nWe never guarantee results. Every scalp is different. But we''ll be honest with you."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Sunday scalp Q&A on the live. (TIME) ET. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'why natural products still need preservatives', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 110K views: \"Replying to @Alex Cardenas premium ingredients need premium packaging\" Comment reply to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com shampoo and conditioner ingredient lists (sodium benzoate, potassium sorbate); Master Client Context Document (COSMOS-approved sodium benzoate and potassium sorbate preservation; \"natural\" is a standard, not a vibe)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"In your own words: why does a shampoo or conditioner need a preservative? We left a placeholder in the script.\nSodium benzoate and potassium sorbate are also used in food. That''s general knowledge, not from your materials. Do you want to say it on camera?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"if it''s natural why does it have preservatives \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Good question. Natural doesn''t mean nothing is protecting the formula.\n[Hold up the shampoo and conditioner.]\nOur shampoo and conditioner use sodium benzoate and potassium sorbate. Both are COSMOS-approved preservatives.\n(WHY A SHAMPOO NEEDS A PRESERVATIVE, IN YOUR WORDS.)\nNatural isn''t about leaving things out. It''s about choosing the right ones."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: natural still needs a preservative. Ours are COSMOS-approved. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'ph: the part of shampoo nobody talks about', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views: \"Did you know we were the first brand to launch a black seed hair oil back in 2019...\" \"Did you know\" talking head, product in hand, straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com shampoo ingredient list (citric acid, gluconolactone). The role of pH in hair care is general chemistry, so we kept it to one line and added questions for you to confirm in your words."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this the same way as in the reference: straight to the camera, same pace. Have the shampoo bottle in your hand."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"In your own words: what do citric acid and gluconolactone do for the shampoo''s pH? We left a placeholder in the script.\nDo you know the shampoo''s pH, and can we say the number on camera?\nIs it OK to say \"your scalp is naturally slightly acidic\"? That''s general chemistry, not from your materials."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold the shampoo bottle up to the camera.]\nDid you know your shampoo has a pH? Nobody talks about it. We do.\nYour scalp is naturally slightly acidic.\n[Turn the bottle and point to the ingredient list.]\nThat''s why there are two ingredients on our label most people skip: citric acid and gluconolactone.\n(WHAT THEY DO FOR THE SHAMPOO''S pH, IN YOUR WORDS.)\n(OPTIONAL: OUR SHAMPOO''S pH NUMBER.)\nSmall ingredients. They''re on the label for a reason.\nDrop your ingredient questions in the comments."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"The part of shampoo nobody talks about: pH. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'cold weather is coming for your scalp', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 13.1M views: \"Fix flat hair after shampoo with this routine\" Silent step-by-step routine with numbered on-screen text (same format as the Week 2 card \"How to use it: The whole routine in order\")."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com hair oil page (scalp massage before washing; scalp treatment 2 to 3 times a week); conditioner on mid-lengths and ends (Week 1 card \"You''re putting conditioner in the wrong place\")."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Do you want an on-screen line that cold air and indoor heating can dry out the scalp? That''s general knowledge, not from your materials, so we left it out."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference. No talking or script is needed. Products: hair oil, shampoo, conditioner. Show each bottle clearly when you use it."},{"heading":"TO-DO LIST","text":"Show the hair oil to the camera.\nPut a small amount on your fingertips and massage it into your scalp, before washing.\nIn the shower: shampoo.\nConditioner on mid-lengths and ends only, not the scalp.\nEnd with all three products lined up to the camera."},{"heading":"ON-SCREEN HOOK","text":"It''s getting cold. Here''s my scalp routine."}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'pump or sifter? let’s talk about it', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@blackmask_shop/video/7591186356118867231"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com hair oil page (not a medical hair-loss treatment; see a dermatologist or trichologist); David: \"we never guarantee anything\", every scalp is different, Oct 5 call, 28:00."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Pump or sifter? Here’s why our texture powder uses a pump #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'how to wash out halloween hair', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@blackmask_shop, 3.4M views Silent before and after wash video (same format as the Week 1 card \"You''re washing your hair wrong\")."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com hair oil page (2 to 5 drops on damp or dry mid-lengths and ends); conditioner on mid-lengths and ends (Week 1 card \"You''re putting conditioner in the wrong place\")."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Any tip you give for getting colored spray or glitter out (for example, rinse longer or shampoo twice)? We kept the steps simple until you confirm."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Recreate the same format as the reference. No talking or script is needed. Products: shampoo, conditioner, hair oil. Show each bottle clearly when you use it."},{"heading":"TO-DO LIST","text":"Start with Halloween hair: colored hair spray, glitter or gel still in it.\nRinse with warm water.\nShampoo.\nConditioner on mid-lengths and ends.\nAfter the shower, a few drops of hair oil on damp mid-lengths and ends.\nShow the final result, then the three products to the camera."}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 3, 'hair confidence starts in the shower', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 2.5M views: \"Why I Created My Hair Products\" Founder talking straight to camera, calm and proud (same format as the Week 1 cards \"It started with his mom''s oils\" and \"Why we make hair products\")."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: hair that comes out of the shower hydrated instead of over-stripped is easier to style, and that is where confidence comes from, Oct 6 call, 8:00."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Tell this to the camera the same way as in the reference: straight to the camera, calm and proud, in your own words, with the shampoo in your hand."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Who should record this, Khaled or David?\nIs there a real moment when your hair started making you feel more confident? One or two sentences is enough. We left a placeholder in the script."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Straight to the camera, shampoo in your hand.]\nHair confidence doesn''t start with styling. It starts the second you step out of the shower.\nWhen your hair comes out hydrated, it''s easier to style.\nWhen it''s easier to style, you stop fighting it in the mirror.\nAnd when you stop fighting it, you walk out the door feeling good.\n(YOUR OWN MOMENT, IN ONE OR TWO SENTENCES.)\nThat''s what we think about when we make a shampoo. Not just clean. How you feel when you walk out the door."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Hair confidence starts in the shower. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'dry hair? don''t just blame your shampoo', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@blackmask_shop/video/7604525570478705950"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from the react video (washing every day without dry, frizzy hair is not only about which shampoo you use)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Washing every day and still dry? It''s not only about your shampoo. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'does hair oil make hair greasy?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 97K views Comment-reply format: a comment on screen, answered straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com hair oil page (2 to 5 drops on damp or dry mid-lengths and ends; scalp massage before washing; scalp treatment 2 to 3 times a week; absorbs quickly, no greasy residue)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"every hair oil i try makes me look like i skipped a shower for a week \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"[Hold the hair oil up to the camera.]\nThen the oil isn''t the problem. The timing is.\nThere are two ways to use our hair oil, and they''re not the same thing.\nOn your lengths: two to five drops on your mid-lengths and ends. Damp hair or dry hair, both work. It absorbs quickly and leaves no greasy residue.\nOn your scalp: that''s a massage before you wash. Two to three times a week. Then you shampoo it out.\nSo if you''ve been rubbing oil into dry roots and walking out the door, that''s not how it''s meant to be used.\nLengths after the shower, scalp before it. Try it this way and tell me how it goes."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: lengths after the shower, scalp before it. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'simple wash day order tips', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 56K views: \"Thinning hair? Try making this oil at home...\" Founder talking head: bold advice hook with a big on-screen headline, a quick personal line about his thin hair, then a step-by-step method with hand demos, then what to expect."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Khaled in the reference video, 0:11 (\"my hair was really thin, you could see my bald spots\"); nounnaturals.com hair oil page (scalp massage before washing, scalp treatment 2 to 3 times a week, 2 to 5 drops on damp or dry mid-lengths and ends); nounnaturals.com shampoo page (daily use); nounnaturals.com conditioner page (quat-free, for every hair type); nounnaturals.com texture powder page (dry hair, 2 to 3 sprays from about 2 inches); David, Oct 5 call, 6:25 (shampoo and conditioner don''t show results immediately, they''re about longevity)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record it like the reference: straight to camera, same studio setup, with a bold headline on screen for the first line. Keep all four products on the table and pick each one up as you name it. Show the scalp massage with your hands."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Your products aren''t the problem. The order you use them in is.\nHere''s the wash day order, and why it works.\nMy hair used to be so thin you could see my bald spots. So trust me, I take wash day seriously.\n[Pick up the hair oil.]\nStep one happens before you even get in the shower: hair oil on your scalp.\n[Massage your scalp with your fingertips.]\nMassage it in, then wash. Two to three times a week, not every single wash day.\n[Pick up the shampoo.]\nStep two: shampoo. It takes that oil out with everything else. Ours is gentle enough to use every day.\n[Pick up the conditioner.]\nStep three: conditioner. Ours is quat-free and made for every hair type.\n[Pick up the hair oil again.]\nStep four: same bottle, way less. Two to five drops on your mid-lengths and ends. Damp or dry, both work.\n[Pick up the texture powder.]\nStep five: dry your hair first, then texture powder. It only goes on dry hair.\n[Spray the powder two to three times from about two inches away.]\nTwo to three sprays from about two inches away. Done.\nWill your shampoo and conditioner change your hair overnight? No. They''re built for the long run. Keep the order, keep it consistent.\nSave this for your next wash day."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Oil, shampoo, conditioner, oil, powder. In that order. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'is noun cruelty-free?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals Comment-reply format: a comment on screen, answered straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com texture powder page (100% natural, vegan, cruelty-free); nounnaturals.com support info (Monday to Friday, average reply within 24 hours)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Are the shampoo, conditioner and hair oil cruelty-free? Are any of your products or ingredients tested on animals?\nAre the shampoo, conditioner and hair oil vegan too, or only the texture powder?\nDo you hold any cruelty-free certification (for example Leaping Bunny), or should we only say \"cruelty-free\"?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"is noun cruelty free or nah? i need to know before i buy \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Good. You should ask that before you buy anything.\nStart with Our Glacial Clay Texture Powder is vegan and cruelty-free. It says it right on the product page.\nFor the shampoo, the conditioner and the hair oil: (PLACEHOLDER: cruelty-free and vegan status of each, from questions 1 to 3.)\nAnd if there''s anything else you want to check before you order, message our support team. They answer Monday to Friday, usually within 24 hours."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: here''s where Noun stands on cruelty-free. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'why we went quiet in 2025', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views Our own \"Did you know\" talking head: a surprising fact as the hook, product in hand, straight to camera, short story, then what''s next."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (2025 build year: no paid ads and no social content January to August 2025; consolidated from 15 products, new contract manufacturer, reformulation; demand outran supply from day one and is the reason content was never consistent, Khaled: \"The reason why we were never consistent with our content was always because of the supply chain\"; started 2018 at 18 hand-making products; shampoo and conditioner re-released September 2025; now media-first with nightly lives; Khaled calls the media-first chapter \"the part I''m most excited about\")."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record it like the reference: straight to camera, one of the products in your hand, calm and direct."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Are you OK saying on camera that you posted nothing from January to August 2025?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold the shampoo up to the camera.]\nDid you know we didn''t post a single video from January to August 2025? No ads either. Nothing.\nHere''s why.\nWhen I started this brand in 2018, I was 18 and making everything by hand. From day one, people wanted our products faster than we could make them.\nThe reason we were never consistent with our content was always the supply chain.\nSo in 2025 we stopped and fixed it. New manufacturer. Fewer products. Reformulated our best sellers. And in September, the new shampoo and conditioner came back.\n[Put the shampoo down.]\nNow the supply side is handled, so we''re going media-first. That''s why you''re seeing us every day now, and why we''re live every night.\nHonestly, this is the part I''m most excited about.\nIf you''re new here, welcome. Come say hi on tonight''s live."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"We went quiet in 2025 for a reason. Here it is. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, '14 texture powders, ranked', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@mpgdiazd/video/7675471938344602893"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from the react video (14 texture powders ranked from worst to best)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"14 texture powders, ranked worst to best. Here''s my take. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'testing viral tiktok hair products', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@typehairofficial/video/7488420707576204575"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from the react video (testing viral TikTok hair products)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Viral on TikTok doesn''t always mean worth it. My honest take. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'should you quit shampoo?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@drdrayzday/video/7432078647428746527"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from nounnaturals.com shampoo page (made for daily use)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"A dermatologist on going \"no poo\". Our shampoo is made for daily use. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'our best seller since 2018 is the styling balm', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views Our own \"Did you know\" proof talking head: a surprising fact as the hook, product in hand, straight to camera, then what''s next."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Styling Balm: best seller since 2018, \"100k+ customers\" as stated and OK to share as stated, currently in restock; live core products are shampoo, conditioner, hair oil and texture powder)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record it like the reference: straight to camera with the Styling Balm in your hand. If you don''t have a jar on hand right now, hold up an empty one or a photo of it."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"When is the Styling Balm back in stock? (Date or rough timing.)\nIn one or two sentences: what does the balm do (hold, finish, hair types) and how do you use it?\nThe context document mentions both \"100k+ Styling Balm customers\" and \"300k+ customers\". Can we say \"over 100,000 people\" have bought the balm?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold the Styling Balm up to the camera.]\nDid you know our best seller isn''t the shampoo, and it isn''t the hair oil? It''s this.\nOur Styling Balm. It''s been our best seller since 2018, the year this brand started.\nOver 100,000 people have bought it.\n(PLACEHOLDER: what the balm does and how you use it, from question 2.)\nRight now it''s in restock. (PLACEHOLDER: when it''s back, from question 1.)\nIf you''ve been waiting for it, turn on notifications so you catch it the second it drops."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Our best seller since 2018. And it''s coming back. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'what does noun even mean?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals Comment-reply format: a comment on screen, answered straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (started 2018; trademark infringement lawsuit at 20 forced the 2021 rebrand to Noun Naturals; origin of the name \"Noun\" is listed as an open question for Khaled)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Where does the name \"Noun\" come from? Who picked it and why?\nIs the site tagline \"Because there is no Noun without U\" part of the real meaning? (We used that line in Week 2, so we''d rather not repeat it unless it''s the actual origin.)"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"ok wait what does noun even mean  like person place or thing??\""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Person, place or thing. Honestly? Not a bad guess.\nBut here''s the real story.\nWe didn''t start out as Noun. We started in 2018 under a different name, and after a trademark lawsuit, we rebranded in 2021.\nWe picked Noun because (PLACEHOLDER: where the name comes from and why you chose it, from question 1).\nSo now you know. Next time somebody asks you what Noun means, you''ve got the answer."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: the real story behind the name. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'does texture powder cause hair loss?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 110K views: \"Replying to @Alex Cardenas premium ingredients need premium packaging\" Comment-reply format: the comment on screen, answered straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Khaled was bullied for a receding hairline (Oct 6 call, 6:25); texture powder ingredients and directions (nounnaturals.com texture powder page: volcanic silica, Canadian glacial clay, plant-derived powders, 100% natural, no aerosols, synthetics or microplastics, 2 to 3 sprays from about 2 inches on dry hair); \"not a medical hair-loss treatment, see a dermatologist or trichologist\" (nounnaturals.com hair oil page); no medical or cure claims (Master Client Context Document)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Are you OK mentioning on camera that you got bullied for a receding hairline? If not, we will cut the first line."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"bro does texture powder actually make your hair fall out or is that just a myth \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"I got bullied for a receding hairline. So I get why you''re asking.\nI''m not going to make medical claims in a comment section. What I can do is tell you exactly what''s in our texture powder.\nVolcanic silica. Canadian glacial clay. Plant-derived powders. A hundred percent natural.\nNo aerosols. No synthetics. No microplastics.\nAnd you use it on dry hair. Two to three sprays from about two inches away. That''s it.\nNow, if you''re actually losing hair, a styling product isn''t the answer, and neither is TikTok. Go see a dermatologist or a trichologist. They can tell you what''s really going on with your scalp.\nGot a question about any ingredient in it? Ask me below."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: here''s what''s in our texture powder, and who to see if you''re losing hair. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'we heard you on hold', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 45K views: \"I hear you guys\" Opens with a montage of viewer comments asking for one thing, then Khaled in the lab coat, straight to camera: \"I hear you guys,\" explains what the brand is doing about it and closes by asking for comments."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"texture powder hold is the one product complaint on record, raised by a customer (Rich, 4 stars); the response direction is a more concentrated formula without added grit; hold feedback is driving that iteration (Master Client Context Document, TP1); directions: dry hair, 2 to 3 sprays from about 2 inches, matte all day (nounnaturals.com texture powder page)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record it like the reference. We will open with a quick montage of on-screen comments asking for more hold (we create them in Canva or CapCut). Then Khaled, in the lab coat against a plain background, says it straight to camera, calm and direct. This is a different video from the 4-star review one: no review is read here, it answers the comments."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Are you OK saying publicly that a more concentrated texture powder is coming?\nDo you have a rough timing for it? If yes, we will add one line at the end."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[On-screen comment montage: \"can it hold longer tho?\", \"love the matte look but I need more hold\", \"stronger version when??\"]\n[Cut to Khaled in the lab coat, straight to camera.]\nI hear you guys. You want more hold.\nOut of everything people tell us about our texture powder, hold is the one thing they''ve asked us to improve.\nSome people think the answer is more grit. We''re going a different way.\nThe next version of our texture powder is a more concentrated formula, built for more hold, and we''re not adding grit to get there.\nUntil then, here''s how to get the most out of the one you have: dry hair, two to three sprays from about two inches away. Matte all day.\nKeep the comments coming. This version exists because you asked for it."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"You asked for more hold. The next texture powder is more concentrated. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'why we don''t launch with a discount', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views: satisfaction guarantee conversation Two people seated, split-screen, talking to each other: one asks and reacts, Khaled answers in short, confident lines."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"\"Hype before discount. Launch with pre-orders and hype-building email and SMS rather than discount-led sends\" and Curl Chemistry pre-orders planned (Master Client Context Document, MC); flash sales on the lives every single night (Oct 5 call, 41:59); curl products coming very soon (Oct 5 call, 12:36)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record it like the reference: two people seated, split-screen, a natural back-and-forth. A = Steven or a team member asking. B = Khaled answering. Keep it relaxed, like you''re explaining it to a friend."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Are you OK talking publicly about launching with pre-orders instead of a discount?\nIs the curl line confirmed to open with pre-orders? Do you have a date?\nIs the email and text list live? Where do people sign up (so we can add it to the caption)?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"A: Khaled, real question. Why don''t our new launches ever come with a discount?\nB: Because our rule is hype before discount.\nA: Meaning what?\nB: Meaning when something new is coming, we open pre-orders first. Not a sale.\nA: Like the curl line.\nB: Exactly like the curl line. Pre-orders.\nA: So how do people hear about it before it drops?\nB: Email and text. That''s where we build it up before launch day.\nA: But people know we do deals on the live.\nB: Flash sales on the live, every night. That doesn''t change. A launch is different.\nA: So if you want the new stuff first?\nB: Pre-order it. Don''t sit around waiting for a discount.\nA: Follow so you know the second pre-orders open."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Hype before discount. That''s how we launch. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'drugstore clay vs natural clay vs pro clay', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@typehairofficial/video/7689517263531068703"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from nounnaturals.com texture powder page (Canadian glacial clay)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Which clay would you put in your hair? Ours is Canadian glacial clay. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'will the conditioner work on curly hair?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 44K views: \"Replying to @Jett thank me later brochacho #hairoiling\" Comment-reply format: the comment on screen, answered straight to camera with practical advice."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com conditioner page (for every hair type; quat-free; INCI incl. aloe, olive, shea, coconut, jojoba, brassicyl valinate esylate); quat-free with a plant-derived conditioning agent, AminoSensyl HC (Master Client Context Document); curly hair goes to more hydrating products (Master Client Context Document, HS); curl products like curl cream and leave-in coming very soon (Oct 5 call, 12:36). No detangling claim."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Is brassicyl valinate esylate on the label the plant-derived conditioning agent (AminoSensyl HC) that replaces quats? If not, we will drop that line."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"i have thick curly hair, is the conditioner even gonna do anything for me or is it just for straight hair \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"It''s not a straight-hair conditioner. It''s made for every hair type, and that includes yours.\nCurly hair wants hydration. That''s the first thing I look at.\nSo flip the bottle. Aloe. Olive. Shea butter. Coconut. Jojoba.\nAnd no quats. The conditioning comes from a plant-derived ingredient instead. On the label it''s called brassicyl valinate esylate. Big name, plant-derived.\nCurl styling, like curl cream and leave-in, is on the way. For conditioning, you don''t have to wait.\nTry it and show me your curls in the comments."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: every hair type means curls too. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'is the new hair oil different from the old one?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 44K views: \"Replying to @Jett thank me later brochacho #hairoiling\" Comment-reply format: the comment on screen, answered straight to camera with practical advice."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com hair oil page (\"Upgraded With Batana, Pumpkin Seed Oil, Patchouli, Amla, and Radish Seed Oil\"; batana from Honduras; black seed (Nigella sativa) in the INCI; Men''s Health Best Black Seed Hair Oil award was for the original formula, Dec 2024; 2 to 5 drops on damp or dry mid-lengths and ends; scalp massage before washing)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"When did the upgraded formula launch?\nWas anything removed or changed besides the five added oils? If yes, we will add one line."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"wait is the new hair oil different from the old one?? \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Yes. We upgraded it. Here''s exactly what changed.\nWe added five oils. Batana, from Honduras. Pumpkin seed oil. Patchouli. Amla. And radish seed oil.\nBlack seed is still in there.\nAnd if you''re thinking about the Men''s Health award for Best Black Seed Hair Oil: that one went to the original formula, back in December 2024. We''re not going to pretend otherwise.\nHow you use it stays the same. Two to five drops on your mid-lengths and ends, damp or dry. Or massage it into your scalp before you wash.\nUsed the old one? Try the new one and tell me the difference in the comments."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: yes, the hair oil got an upgrade. Here''s what we added. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'is sulfate-free just a buzzword?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@labmuffinbeautyscience/video/7233223539610897682"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from nounnaturals.com shampoo page (INCI: decyl glucoside, lauryl glucoside)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Sulfate-free tells you what got taken out. Ours cleans with decyl and lauryl glucoside. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, '$48 for a hair oil?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 110K views: \"Replying to @Alex Cardenas premium ingredients need premium packaging\" Their own price-objection comment reply, answered straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: \"our products are on the pricier end... we like to categorize ourselves in the more premium aspect\" (Oct 5 call, 12:21) and \"we go ingredient for ingredient... we go based off facts\" (Oct 5 call, 12:36); nounnaturals.com hair oil page ($48, 4.9 from 254 reviews, INCI incl. batana from Honduras, black seed, argan, amla, pumpkin seed, rosemary, patchouli; 2 to 5 drops)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"$48 for a hair oil?? \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Forty-eight dollars. Yes. Look at what''s in the bottle before you scroll.\nWe''re on the premium side, on purpose. And we back it up ingredient by ingredient.\nBatana oil from Honduras. Black seed. Argan. Amla. Pumpkin seed. Rosemary. Patchouli. Every one of them is right there on the label.\nYou only use two to five drops at a time. This isn''t an oil you pour on.\nAnd it sits at 4.9 stars from 254 reviews.\nDon''t take my word for it. Read the reviews, then decide."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: $48, 4.9 stars from 254 reviews. Read them, then decide. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'are consistent formulas better?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@blackmask_shop/video/7669093316092300575"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from the Master Client Context Document (2025 reformulation and re-release of shampoo and conditioner) and nounnaturals.com hair oil page (upgraded formula)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Consistency matters. So does upgrading a formula when you can make it better. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'pick your product by hair type', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 45K views: \"I hear you guys\" Opens with a montage of viewer comments asking the same question, then Khaled in the lab coat, straight to camera: \"I hear you guys,\" answers it and closes by asking for comments."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Khaled routes by hair type: \"If it''s curly hair, it''s more hydrating products. If it''s wavy hair... straight hair products like clays and powders\"; curly to hydration, wavy to moisture plus hold, straight and thick to texture (Master Client Context Document, HS); curl products coming very soon (Oct 5 call, 12:36); nounnaturals.com: shampoo for 1a to 3b, daily use; conditioner for every hair type; hair oil for straight, wavy, curly, coily, 2 to 5 drops on mid-lengths and ends; texture powder 2 to 3 sprays from about 2 inches on dry hair; texture powder gives texture, hold, volume (Noun''s own caption on video 7563863893148290359)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record it like the reference. We will open with a quick montage of on-screen comments asking which product fits their hair (we create them in Canva or CapCut). Then Khaled, in the lab coat against a plain background, straight to camera. Hold up each product as you mention it."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[On-screen comment montage: \"what do I use for wavy hair?\", \"curly hair here, which one do I get\", \"straight thick hair, help\"]\n[Cut to Khaled in the lab coat, straight to camera.]\nI hear you guys. \"Which one is for MY hair?\" Here''s how I''d pick.\n[Hold up the conditioner and the hair oil.]\nCurly hair: go more hydrating. The conditioner is made for every hair type. The hair oil, two to five drops on your mid-lengths and ends. And curl styling products are on the way.\n[Hold up the shampoo and conditioner, then the texture powder.]\nWavy hair: moisture first, then hold. Shampoo and conditioner for the moisture. Texture powder for the hold.\n[Hold up the texture powder.]\nStraight hair, especially thick: you want texture. That''s what clays and powders are for. Dry hair, two to three sprays from about two inches away.\nAnd the shampoo covers types 1a to 3b. Gentle enough for every day.\nComment straight, wavy or curly, and I''ll reply with where to start."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Curly, wavy or straight? Here''s where to start. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'taking care of your hair is discipline', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 2.5M views: \"Why I Created My Hair Products\" Founder talking straight to camera, calm and sure, one continuous message."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: \"It goes beyond hair and body products. It really goes down to the personal care aspect of taking care of yourself, taking care of your health... you want to be successful, you have to be disciplined, you have to take care of yourself\", Oct 6 call, 16:19; Master Client Context Document (Noun''s role is the daily routine: wash, condition, style)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Tell this to the camera the same way as in the reference: straight to the camera, calm and sure, in your own words. Hold a product in your hand."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Everybody wants to be successful. Nobody wants to do the boring stuff.\nThis was never just about hair for us. It''s about taking care of yourself. Your health. How you show up.\nIf you want to be successful, you have to be disciplined. And discipline isn''t only the big things. It''s the small things you do every day when nobody''s watching.\nWash. Condition. Style. Every day.\nYou don''t need a shelf full of products. You need to do the basics, and do them every single day.\nTake care of yourself. That''s where it starts."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Discipline shows up in the small stuff too. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'texture, hold, volume', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 37K views: \"It''s 2026, styling products are supposed to also factor in hair health along with performance\" Your own label call-out rant to camera: \"you''ll see a bunch of brands promise this, that, and the third\", then flip the bottle and show what''s really in it."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"your original draft line on this card (\"texture, hold and volume, without turning your hair into a helmet\"); Glacial Clay Texture Powder product page on nounnaturals.com (volcanic silica, Canadian glacial clay, plant-derived powders; 100% natural, vegan, cruelty-free; dry hair, 2 to 3 sprays from about 2 inches; matte all day)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record it like your 37K video: straight to camera, same rant energy, texture powder in your hand. Show the spray and the finished style on camera."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold the texture powder up to the camera.]\nYou''ll see a bunch of styling products promise texture, hold, volume, this, that, and the third. Then you put it in and your hair turns into a helmet.\nThat''s not hold. That''s your hair not moving.\n[Turn the bottle so the label faces the camera.]\nTexture powder is supposed to give you all three and still look like hair. Here''s what''s in ours. Volcanic silica. Canadian glacial clay. Plant-derived powders. A hundred percent natural.\n[Spray two to three times on dry hair, about two inches away.]\nDry hair. Two to three sprays. That''s it.\n[Work it through with your fingers and show the finished style from the front and the side.]\nTexture. Hold. Volume. Matte all day.\nNot a helmet. Hair."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Texture, hold, volume. Not a helmet. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'ingredients that strengthen hair?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@blackmask_shop/video/7671162988191141151"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; the caption states no product facts."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Which ingredients actually strengthen hair? Here''s my take. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'two ways to wash your hair: which one is wrong?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dbi-XkbBid0/"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; the caption states no product facts."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Two ways to wash your hair. Which one are you? #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'do you have anything for beards?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 31K views: \"Replying to @irockali not letting you down king\" Comment-reply format: the comment on screen, you answer straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Arabian Oud Beard Oil is listed; GCC hero product; final sale; GCC oud and halal grooming buyers are a named segment)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"What''s in the Arabian Oud Beard Oil, and how would you describe the scent in one line?\nHow should people use it (how many drops, when)?\nWhere can people buy it right now (our site, which countries), and what does it cost?\nIs it okay to say on camera that it''s our hero product in the Gulf?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"do y''all have anything for beards or is it just hair \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"We do. Arabian Oud Beard Oil.\nIn the Gulf, this is our hero product.\n(ONE LINE: WHAT''S IN IT AND WHAT IT SMELLS LIKE.)\nHow to use it: (HOW MANY DROPS, WHEN).\nWhere to get it: (WHERE IT''S AVAILABLE).\nOne thing to know before you order: it''s final sale. So if you have a question about it, ask us first. We''ll answer."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Yes, we have something for your beard. Arabian Oud Beard Oil. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'black seed oil for hair loss?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@dr.farzan/video/7372689130620341510"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from the nounnaturals.com hair oil page (black seed oil, Nigella sativa, is in the hair oil; the hair oil is not a medical hair-loss treatment)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Black seed oil is in our hair oil. It''s not a hair-loss treatment, and we don''t sell it as one. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'where do you get your ingredients from?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 32K views: \"Replying to @Benedict and noun on the front lines of innovation, we''re not being cheap with you guys, other brands are\" Comment-reply format: the comment on screen, one continuous take straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (started at 18 in 2018, hand-making products in the basement; ISO 16128-aligned formulas with COSMOS-approved inputs, verifiable through supplier documentation; a formula that fails EU rules is out, even if it works in the US; named suppliers: only name suppliers actually used); nounnaturals.com hair oil page (batana oil from Honduras)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Which ingredient suppliers can we name on camera? Your Master Context Document lists Colonial Chemical, Givaudan and Inolex (AminoSensyl HC in the conditioner). Please confirm which ones you actively use today. We will only name the ones you confirm.\nIs there one more ingredient whose origin you''d like to mention (for example, where your black seed oil comes from)?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"where do y''all even get your ingredients from \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"We started out hand-making everything in a basement. Today every ingredient has to pass a standard before it gets anywhere near a bottle.\nOur formulas are aligned with ISO 16128, and we use COSMOS-approved ingredients. Every one of those comes with supplier documents behind it.\nAnd it has to pass EU rules, not just US rules. If a formula fails in Europe, it''s out. Even if it would be fine here.\nSome of it comes from pretty far. The batana oil in our hair oil? Honduras.\nWe work with suppliers like (CONFIRMED SUPPLIER NAMES).\nWant to know where one specific ingredient comes from? Name it in the comments and I''ll tell you."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Every ingredient has to pass a standard first. Even EU rules. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'why the curl line bottle has a dark pump', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 2.5M views: \"Why I Created My Hair Products\" Founder talking straight to camera, calm and sure, explaining why he made something the way he did."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Jul 2026 Curl Chemistry bottle review: chose a darker pump to drop a beauty-aisle signal while keeping the gradient; pump hardware color can make a bottle feel feminine; Curl Chemistry is unisex leaning male, targets curly-haired men first, women welcome; pre-orders planned)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Tell this to the camera the same way as in the reference: straight to the camera, calm and sure, in your own words. If you can show a Curl Chemistry bottle or sample, hold it up when you talk about the pump."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Can we show the Curl Chemistry bottle on camera yet? If not, we''ll keep it off camera and you just tell the story.\nIs the darker pump final on the bottle that will ship?\nAnything we can say about pre-order timing?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"One tiny part of our new curl bottle took more thought than you''d think. The pump.\n[Hold up the Curl Chemistry bottle with the pump facing the camera.]\nThis is Curl Chemistry, our new curl line. It''s made for guys with curly hair first. Women, you''re welcome too. It''s unisex.\nThe bottle has a gradient. We kept it. We like it.\nBut one small thing can change how a whole bottle reads. The color of the pump. The wrong one, and the bottle looks like it belongs in the beauty aisle.\n[Tap the pump.]\nSo we went darker on the pump. Same gradient. Darker pump.\nWe want a guy with curls to pick this up and feel like it was made for him. Because it was.\nPre-orders are coming (TIMING). Follow so you don''t miss it."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Why our curl line bottle has a dark pump. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'why our label never says just ''natural fragrance''', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 37K views: \"It''s 2026, styling products are supposed to also factor in hair health along with performance\" Your own label call-out rant to camera: \"you''ll see a bunch of brands... this, that, and the third\", then flip the bottle and read what''s really on it."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (rejects vague \"natural fragrance\" wording; fragrance INCI per US and EU rules); nounnaturals.com hair oil page (ingredient list ends with fragrance from natural essential oils); David: some people can react to essential oils and Noun always puts that out there, Oct 5 call, 45:14."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record it like your 37K video: straight to camera, same rant energy. Have the hair oil in your hand and turn the label to the camera when you read it."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold the hair oil up to the camera.]\nYou''ll see a bunch of brands put \"natural fragrance\" on the label, like that''s supposed to tell you something.\nNatural fragrance. Two words. Which oils? How many? It doesn''t say.\n[Turn the hair oil label to the camera.]\nFlip ours. The ingredient list on our hair oil ends with fragrance from natural essential oils. It''s labeled the way US and EU rules ask for. Not two vague words.\nWhy does that matter? Because some people react to certain essential oils. We say that out loud. If you''re one of them, you should be able to see it on the label before you buy, not after.\nSo next time you flip a bottle and it just says \"natural fragrance\", ask what''s in it."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"\"Natural fragrance\" doesn''t tell you much. Ask what''s in it. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'did you go to school for this?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 31K views: \"Replying to @irockali not letting you down king\" Comment-reply format: the comment on screen, you answer straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (dropped out of law school; started in 2018 at 18 in his basement, hand-making products; R&D in-house; he is not the formulating chemist and directs formulation with chemists and contract manufacturer partners; he checks INCI spellings and technical claims with the formulator or supplier documents; a formula that fails EU rules is out, even if it works in the US)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Are you comfortable saying \"I''m not the chemist\" on camera? If you''d say it differently, tell us how.\nDo you want to add which law school it was, or why you left? Only if you want to share it."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"wait did you actually go to school for this or nah \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Honestly? No. I went to law school. And I dropped out.\nI started this at eighteen, in my basement, making everything by hand.\nAnd I''m not the chemist. I''ll never pretend to be. Our formulas are made with chemists and our manufacturing partners, and the R&D stays in-house.\nMy job is the ingredients. I choose them. I check every name on the label with our formulator. And if a formula doesn''t pass EU rules, it''s out, even if it would pass here.\nSo no chemistry degree. Just doing this every day since 2018.\nGot a question about an ingredient? Ask me. That part I can answer."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: No chemistry degree. Law school dropout. Here''s who actually makes our formulas. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'is the texture powder actually vegan?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 25K views: \"Replying to @hideyokids6967 how to get the most out of hair oil\" Comment-reply format: the comment on screen, then a straight-to-camera answer."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com Glacial Clay Texture Powder page (100% natural, vegan, cruelty-free; volcanic silica, Canadian glacial clay, plant-derived powders); Oct 5 call, 28:00 and 38:23 (the team knows every ingredient in their products)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"vegan texture powder? sure \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Sure. And it''s not just me saying it.\nGo to the texture powder page on our site. It''s written right there: 100% natural, vegan, cruelty-free.\n[Hold the texture powder up to the camera.]\nWhat''s inside: volcanic silica, Canadian glacial clay and plant-derived powders. Minerals and plants.\nStill not convinced about one of the ingredients? Name it in the comments. We know every single one of them, and we''ll tell you exactly what it is."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Vegan and cruelty-free. It says so right on the product page. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'barber breaks down wash day', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@2fresh.au/video/7598819300333407544"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from nounnaturals.com shampoo page (made for daily use)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"A barber breaks down wash day. Our take: pick a shampoo that''s made for daily use. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'derived from natural does not mean natural', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@typehairofficial, 273K views Comparison-list talking head: \"X versus Y, let''s compare\", then one bold category at a time, each comparing both sides in one or two lines, closing line on the brand."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (ISO 16128 natural vs naturally derived; a quaternized guar derivative is chemically modified, so \"natural\" is inaccurate; calling chemically modified ingredients natural hurts the reputation of natural products); nounnaturals.com (ISO 16128 aligned, COSMOS-approved ingredients)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record it like the reference: straight to the camera, say each bold category out loud, then compare the two sides in one or two lines. Keep a steady pace. Don''t name any brand."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Is this simple definition OK with you: natural = used the way it comes from the plant or mineral; naturally derived = started there, then chemically modified?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Natural versus naturally derived. Not the same thing. Let''s compare.\nStarting off with what it means. A natural ingredient is used the way it comes from the plant or the mineral, while a naturally derived ingredient started there and was then chemically modified.\nAn example. Guar comes from a plant, while quaternized guar is guar that has been chemically modified, so calling it natural isn''t accurate under ISO 16128.\nThe label. Some brands sell naturally derived as natural on the front of the bottle, while the honest way is to call each ingredient what it is.\nWhy it matters. Every time a chemically modified ingredient gets called natural, it hurts the reputation of the products that actually are natural.\nOurs. Our formulas are aligned with ISO 16128 and use COSMOS-approved ingredients, so when we say natural, there''s a standard behind the word.\nNext time a bottle says natural, ask: natural, or did it just start that way?"},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Natural vs naturally derived. Same word on the front, not the same thing. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'what''s arrowroot doing in a texture powder?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 37K views Comment-reply format: the comment on screen, then a straight-to-camera answer."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Glacial Clay Texture Powder direction: glacial clay, bentonite, arrowroot); nounnaturals.com texture powder page (plant-derived powders; 2 to 3 sprays from about 2 inches on dry hair)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Is arrowroot in the texture powder that''s on sale right now? (Your doc lists glacial clay, bentonite and arrowroot as the direction; the site lists volcanic silica, Canadian glacial clay and plant-derived powders.)\nWhat does arrowroot do in the formula? One or two sentences in your own words is perfect. It goes where the placeholder is."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"why is there ARROWROOT in a texture powder \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Arrowroot. A plant. In a styling powder. On purpose.\n[Hold the texture powder up to the camera.]\nOur texture powder is built on clays and plant-derived powders, and arrowroot is one of them.\n(PLACEHOLDER: what arrowroot does in the formula, in one or two sentences.)\nHow to use it: dry hair, two to three sprays from about two inches away, then style.\nGot another ingredient on our labels that sounds like it belongs in a kitchen? Comment it and we''ll answer it."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Yes, arrowroot. Here''s why it''s in our texture powder. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'is oiling making your dandruff worse?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@angela.onuoha/video/7348908693003521313?is_from_webapp=1&sender_device=pc&web_id=7700970576471377429"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from nounnaturals.com hair oil page (scalp massage before washing; not a medical treatment, see a dermatologist or trichologist)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Oil or a water-based serum for a flaky scalp? Here''s my take. Our hair oil is a scalp massage before you wash, then it washes out. Flakes that won''t go away? See a dermatologist. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'i tried to build an ai hair scanner', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 157K views Call-out talking head: one bold, provocative opening line straight to camera, short punchy lines, closes on a firm one-liner."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Jun 2026: Khaled tried building an AI hair and scalp scanner himself and concluded AI is not precise enough yet; approved quote \"Misdiagnose someone''s hair once and you lose them\"; nightly lives); Oct 5 call, 28:00 (Steven knows every ingredient; comment and live questions get ingredient-based answers); Oct 5 call, 38:23 (the founders know their ingredients)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record it like the reference: straight to the camera, one take, calm but direct, like you''re calling something out. Short lines, small pauses between them."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Are you OK sharing on camera that you tried to build the scanner and didn''t launch it?\nIs \"this year\" right (your doc dates it to June 2026)?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Look straight into the camera.]\nI tried to build an AI that tells you what your hair needs. Then I shelved it.\nThis year I tried building an AI hair and scalp scanner myself.\nAnd it''s not out there.\nBecause AI isn''t precise enough yet. Not for hair.\nMisdiagnose someone''s hair once and you lose them.\nSo I''m not putting something in front of you that guesses.\nIf you want to know what to use, ask us. Comment your hair type, or come on the live.\nSteven and I know every ingredient in every bottle, and we''ll tell you which one we''d pick for you and why.\nThat''s slower than an app. But it''s a real answer."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"I tried to build an AI hair scanner. Here''s why it never launched. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'thickening product on thinning hair', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@lifeaszeph/video/7692552594241113374"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from Master Client Context Document (belief: \"natural, high performing, long term hair and scalp health\"); Oct 5 call, 6:25 (David: not a miracle product, built for longevity)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"A thickening product on thinning hair: our honest take. We build for long-term hair and scalp health, not miracles. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'is black seed oil the same as black cumin?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 37K views Comment-reply format: the comment on screen, then a straight-to-camera answer."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com hair oil page, ingredient list (Nigella sativa (black cumin) seed oil); nounnaturals.com shampoo and conditioner ingredient lists (nigella seed oil)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Optional: can we add one line saying black cumin is a different plant from the cumin spice in your kitchen? We left it out of the script until you confirm."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"wait is black seed oil the same thing as black cumin oil?? \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Same plant. Three names.\nBlack seed. Black cumin. Nigella sativa.\n[Turn the hair oil around and point to the ingredient list.]\nThat''s how it''s written on our hair oil: Nigella sativa, black cumin, seed oil.\n[Pick up the shampoo and the conditioner.]\nAnd it''s not only in the oil. It''s on our shampoo and our conditioner labels too, written as nigella seed oil.\nSo if you see any of those names on a label, it''s the same ingredient. Now you know what to look for."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Black seed, black cumin, Nigella sativa. Same plant. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'so how much shampoo do i need?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@blowoutprofessor/video/7047272211186502917?is_from_webapp=1&sender_device=pc&web_id=7700970576471377429"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from Oct 5 call, 6:25 (David: with high-performing products you don''t need to use a lot)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"How much shampoo do you actually need? Less than you think. A good formula doesn''t need a handful. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'two ingredients we left out of our shampoo', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 157K views Call-out talking head: one bold, provocative opening line straight to camera, short punchy lines, closes on a firm one-liner."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (shampoo: decyl and lauryl glucoside, aloe vera juice base, deliberately no sodium cocoyl glutamate and no cocamidopropyl hydroxysultaine; sulfate-free); nounnaturals.com shampoo page (ingredient list: decyl glucoside, aloe leaf juice, lauryl glucoside; daily use, color-safe)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record it like the reference: straight to the camera, one take, calm but direct, like you''re calling something out. Short lines, small pauses between them. Hold the shampoo bottle the whole time."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Why did you leave out sodium cocoyl glutamate and cocamidopropyl hydroxysultaine? One or two sentences in your own words. It goes where the placeholder is.\nAre you OK naming these two ingredients on camera? (We don''t say anything negative about them, only that you chose not to use them.)"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold the shampoo bottle up to the camera.]\nTwo cleansers you will never find in this bottle.\nSodium cocoyl glutamate.\nCocamidopropyl hydroxysultaine.\nWe left both out on purpose.\n(PLACEHOLDER: why you left them out, one or two sentences in your own words.)\n[Turn the bottle around and point to the ingredient list.]\nWhat cleans your hair instead: decyl glucoside and lauryl glucoside, with aloe leaf juice.\nNo sulfates. Made for daily use. Color-safe.\nIf it''s on our label, we chose it. If it''s not on our label, we chose that too."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Two cleansers we left out of our shampoo, on purpose. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'powder, clay or balm?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 24K views Comment-reply format: a viewer comment on screen, answered straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com texture powder page (Canadian glacial clay in the powder; 2 to 3 sprays from about 2 inches on dry hair; matte all day); Master Client Context Document (Glacial Clay hair clay is a separate product in development; Styling Balm is the best seller since 2018 and is in restock)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"When is the Styling Balm back in stock? We left (RESTOCK DATE) in the script.\nIn one line each: who is the balm for, and who will the clay be for (finish, hold, hair type)? We did not want to guess, so the script only says what is confirmed."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"soo... powder, clay or balm?  which one do i get\""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Right now? Powder. And that''s not me dodging the question.\nIt''s the only one of the three you can buy today.\n[Hold up the texture powder.]\nThe texture powder already has Canadian glacial clay in it. Two to three sprays from about two inches, on dry hair, and it stays matte all day.\nThe balm has been our best seller since 2018. It''s in restock, and it''s back (RESTOCK DATE).\nThe clay is its own product, separate from the powder, and it''s still in development.\nSo: powder today, balm when it''s back, clay when it''s ready. Follow so you don''t miss either one."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Powder today. Balm and clay are on the way. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'hair oil mistakes', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 77K views Two-person skit: one person is doing it wrong, the other takes over, explains, and throws the bottle (\"Catch\")."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"nounnaturals.com hair oil page (2 to 5 drops on damp or dry mid-lengths and ends; scalp massage before washing; scalp treatment 2 to 3 times a week)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Same two-person catch skit as your Men''s Health video (77K). A is the one getting it wrong, B takes the bottle, explains, and throws it back at the end. You can change outfits and location, keep the concept. Show the hair oil bottle clearly in every shot."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[A is standing at the mirror, dressed to go out, tipping the hair oil bottle over the top of his head.]\nB: Why are you pouring hair oil on your scalp right before you leave the house?\nA: Getting ready.\nB: Give me that.\n[B takes the bottle.]\nB: Mistake one. The scalp part is a massage before you wash. Not something you walk around in all day.\nB: Two to three times a week, massage it into your scalp, then shampoo.\nA: Before the shower?\nB: Before the shower. Mistake two. The everyday spot isn''t your scalp. It''s your mid-lengths and ends.\nA: So I have to wait till my hair''s dry?\nB: Mistake three. Damp or dry, both work. You don''t have to wait.\nA: How much?\nB: Two to five drops. Catch.\n[B throws the bottle back to A. A puts a few drops in his palm and works them through his ends.]\nA: That''s actually it?\nB: That''s it."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Three hair oil mistakes. Which one were you making? #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'is silicone bad for hair?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@aliialshami/video/7703017675575938318?_r=1&_t=ZT-9B2KxDUOeTd"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from nounnaturals.com shampoo and conditioner ingredient lists (no silicones listed)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Silicones: bad for your hair or just misunderstood? Here''s my take. Flip our shampoo and conditioner, you won''t find one on the label. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'we ran meta ads from a basement', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 110K views: \"Putting your conditioner in a spray bottle to make at home leave in?\" Two-person skit: A in a lab coat behind the kitchen counter does something unexpected, B asks from off camera (\"what is bro doing\" on screen), A explains, B ends up convinced."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (started in 2018 at 18 in his basement, hand-making products; pushed products on YouTube and social; ran Meta ads from the basement in 2018; demand from YouTube and social outran supply)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Same setup as your conditioner spray bottle video (110K): Khaled in the lab coat behind the kitchen counter, the other person films and asks from off camera. Keep \"what is bro doing\" on screen for the first two seconds. This time Khaled has his phone propped against the counter and is filming a Noun bottle."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Did your very first orders come from YouTube and social first, then the Meta ads? That is the order we took from the Master Context. Correct?\nWhich product were you making by hand in the basement? If you tell us, we can name it on camera."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Khaled, in the lab coat behind the counter, has his phone propped up and is filming a Noun bottle. B films from off camera.]\nB: Bro. Why are you filming a bottle on the kitchen counter?\nA: What do you mean? This is how we got our first customers.\nB: With a phone?\nA: 2018. I''m eighteen. Making the products by hand in my basement.\nA: Then I put them on YouTube. Then on social.\nB: And people bought it?\nA: Then I ran Meta ads. From the basement.\nB: From the basement?\nA: From the basement. Orders came in faster than I could make the product.\nB: So the first Noun customers found you on YouTube?\nA: YouTube, social, and ads I ran from my basement.\n[A turns to the camera.]\nA: If you found us back then, tell me where in the comments.\nB: Bro, you just put me on."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"2018: YouTube, social, and Meta ads from my basement. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'where did the other products go?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 77K views Two-person skit: one person asks what''s going on, the other explains and throws the bottle (\"Catch\")."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (15 SKUs consolidated to 2, now 4 live; best sellers reformulated with a new contract manufacturer and re-released; shampoo and conditioner re-released in September 2025; products brought back slowly; to be told as reformulation and re-release); nounnaturals.com (current lineup: shampoo, conditioner, hair oil, Glacial Clay Texture Powder)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Same two-person catch skit as your Men''s Health video (77K). This time A explains and throws the hair oil to B at the end. You can change outfits and location, keep the concept. Different from the Week 2 \"Four products, on purpose\" video: that one was about not launching more, this one is about what happened to the old products and how they come back."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Shampoo, conditioner, hair oil and texture powder in a row on the counter. A is lining them up.]\nB: Wait. Why are there only four bottles on this table?\nA: That''s the whole lineup right now.\nB: Didn''t Noun used to have way more than four?\nA: Fifteen.\nB: Fifteen? So where did they go?\nA: We took the best sellers, reformulated them with a new manufacturer, and re-released them.\n[A taps the shampoo and the conditioner.]\nA: These two came back first. September 2025.\n[A picks up the hair oil and the texture powder.]\nA: Then these.\nB: And the rest?\nA: They come back slowly. One at a time. Reformulated first, then back on the site.\nB: So nothing comes back the same as before.\nA: Nothing. Catch.\n[A throws the hair oil to B, then turns to the camera.]\nA: Which old Noun product do you want back next? Comment it."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Fifteen products, then four. The rest come back one at a time. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'just sea salt spray?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@tk.essentials/video/7697645749890190614?is_from_webapp=1&sender_device=pc&web_id=7700970576471377429"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from: none (the caption makes no product claims)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Is sea salt spray really all you need? #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'fake vs real texture powder', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@blackmask_shop/video/7563316081612377375"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from: none (the caption makes no product claims)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Real or fake? The ingredient list tells you. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'why is the hair oil final sale?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 24K views: \"Replying to @Draven why is noun sea salt spray taking so long to release? Here''s the answer\" Comment-reply format: a viewer comment on screen, answered straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Hair Oil and Arabian Oud Beard Oil are final sale under the return policy, with exceptions); nounnaturals.com (10-day hassle-free returns; full hair oil ingredient list on the product page; support Mon to Fri 8am to 8:30pm, average reply within 24h); Oct 5 call, 45:14 (allergic reactions to essential oils: \"we take care of that, we give them the refund\"; warning for people sensitive to essential oils)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Why are the oils final sale? One or two sentences in your words. We left (REASON) in the script.\nWhat are the exceptions (for example damaged on arrival, wrong item, a reaction)? We left (EXCEPTIONS). Can we say on camera that a reaction gets taken care of, as David said on the Oct 5 call?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"why is the hair oil final sale but everything else can be returned?? \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Fair question. Yes, our oils are final sale. Here''s the honest answer.\nThe hair oil and the Arabian Oud Beard Oil are final sale. (REASON)\nEverything else has a 10-day hassle-free return.\nThere are exceptions on the oils: (EXCEPTIONS). And if you have a reaction, message us. We take care of that.\nSo before you buy, read the full ingredient list on our site. Every oil is on there. If you''re sensitive to essential oils, check it first.\nStill not sure? Message us. Monday to Friday, 8am to 8:30pm, and we usually reply within 24 hours."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Why our oils are final sale, and what to check before you buy. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'how long does one bottle of hair oil last?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 24K views Comment-reply format: a viewer comment on screen, answered straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"your own caption on @nounnaturals 7641324415396908302 (\"4 ounces that will last you 4-6 months\"); nounnaturals.com hair oil page (2 to 5 drops on damp or dry mid-lengths and ends; scalp treatment 2 to 3 times a week, before washing)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Your caption says 4 ounces lasts 4 to 6 months. Is that based on daily use on the ends? Is that still true for the new formula?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"ok but how long does ONE bottle of the hair oil actually last \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Four to six months. From one bottle.\nIt''s four ounces, and you only use two to five drops at a time on your mid-lengths and ends.\n[Tip two or three drops into your palm and show it to the camera.]\nThat''s one use. That''s it.\nDoing the scalp treatment too, two to three times a week before you wash? Then it goes faster. That''s just math.\nStill on your first bottle? Tell me how many months in."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: One 4 oz bottle, 4 to 6 months. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'how do i become a noun creator?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 24K views: \"Replying to @Draven why is noun sea salt spray taking so long to release? Here''s the answer\" Comment-reply format: a viewer comment on screen, answered straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (affiliates since 2018; buyers are men and women); Oct 5 call, 44:01 (when you worked with one big creator, Australia became your top country, and those customers still buy today); Oct 5 call (customers are 50/50 men and women); Oct 5 call, 28:00 (very interactive in the comments)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"How does someone become a Noun creator right now: TikTok Shop affiliate, a form on the site, a DM, an email? We left (HOW TO APPLY) in the script.\nAre there any requirements (minimum age, followers, country)? A lot of your commenters are teens, so an age rule matters. We left (REQUIREMENTS).\nCan we mention that one creator partnership made Australia your top country for a while? We did not name the creator."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"how do i become a noun creator?? i''d post every day fr \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"You want to make videos with us? Say less. We''ve worked with creators since 2018.\nHere''s how it works right now: (HOW TO APPLY).\nWhat you need: (REQUIREMENTS).\nAnd creators really move things for us. When we worked with one big creator, Australia became our top country for a while. People there still order from us today.\nGuys and girls. Our customers are half men, half women, so we want both on camera.\nDrop your handle below. You know we''re in the comments."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Want to make videos with Noun? Here''s how. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'we stand by what we say', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 135K views: \"Natural is the base line, performance is the differentiator\" Your own founder statement straight to the camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"being unapologetic, \"we stick by it, we die by it\", not apologizing because you believe it, busting brands that lie about their product (David, Oct 6 call, 19:58); being controversial for calling out brands, haters in the comments who end up trying the products (David, Oct 6 call, 14:31); \"do your own research\", \"we''re not going to force you\" (David, Oct 6 call, 18:31)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We took one of your videos that performed really well, which shows that the format works, and wrote a new script for it. Say it straight to the camera, same setup and same calm, confident energy as the reference."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Anything we say on this app, we stick by it. We die by it.\nPeople call us controversial. We''ve called out other brands, and our comments get loud for it.\nWe''re not going to apologize for that. We only say what we actually believe.\nIf a brand tells you something about their product that isn''t true, we''re going to bust it. Every time.\nBut here''s the part people miss.\nWe don''t want you to just take our word for it either. Read the label. Look the ingredients up. Do your own research.\nAnd if after all that you decide we''re not for you? So be it. We''re not going to beg you to buy.\nThat''s the deal. We say it, we stand behind it, and you make the call."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"We say it, we stand behind it. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'matte finish clay samples', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 356K views Two-person skit: A says something to the camera, B storms in (\"Yo! What are you doing, bro?\"), they argue, B walks off, A shrugs back to the camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Glacial Clay hair clay is a separate product from the texture powder and is in development (Master Client Context Document, product table); loyal customers get raw samples straight from the lab before a launch decision (David, Oct 5 call, 32:00); \"matte finish\" from this card''s original title and your clay-sample video (please confirm, see questions)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this the same way as your juggling video: white or plain background, one static shot, two people. Person A holds a clay sample jar close to the camera, person B walks in and interrupts. Keep it fast and natural, the argument is the joke."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Is \"matte finish\" the right way to describe the clay? If not, what finish should we say?\nIs it OK to show the clay sample jar on camera? If the jar has no label yet, that is fine."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[A holds a small clay sample jar right up to the camera.]\nA: This is our hair clay. Matte finish. And it''s not out yet.\n[A opens the jar and tilts it toward the camera.]\nA: Raw sample, straight from the lab. And no, it''s not the texture powder. It''s a whole separate product.\n[B walks into frame.]\nB: Yo! What are you doing, bro?\nA: Showing them the clay.\nB: It''s still in development! Close the jar!\nA: Nah, nah, they should know it''s coming.\nB: How many times do we tell you? It''s not out yet!\n[B walks off, shaking his head.]\nA: Bro, I''m just trying to show the customers.\n[A turns back to the camera and shrugs.]\nA: Comment \"clay\" if you want to see it on hair next."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Not the texture powder. Something new.  #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'do you make a gel?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 31K views: \"Replying to @basedkaifanaccount we don''t mind inspiring other brands bro\" Comment-reply format: the comment on screen, you answer straight to the camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Curl Chemistry sub-brand of 7 to 9 products including leave-in, curl cream, curl gel and mousse, unisex leaning male, pre-orders planned (Master Client Context Document, product table); curly line not fully released yet (Steven, Oct 5 call, 31:42)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"What is the current status of Curl Chemistry and the curl gel? Can we say anything about pre-orders (how and where), without a date?\nIs there one thing about the gel you want people to know now (hold, feel, scent)? If yes, we will add one line."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"do y''all make a gel or nah?? i need something for my curls \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"A gel? It''s not on the site yet. But it''s not coming alone.\nIt''s part of Curl Chemistry. That''s our curl line.\nSeven to nine products. A leave-in, a curl cream, a curl gel, a mousse, and more.\nMade unisex, like everything else we make.\n(PRE-ORDER / LAUNCH STATUS, NO DATE)\nUntil then, drop \"gel\" in the comments so we know how many of you are waiting."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: the gel is part of our curl line, Curl Chemistry. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'my order is late, now what?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 32K views Comment-reply format: the comment on screen, you answer straight to the camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (real objection on record: a customer reported a long delivery delay and asked about the refund path; the team offered store credit in early July 2026); nounnaturals.com (US shipping 3 to 6 business days; support Mon to Fri 8am to 8:30pm, average reply within 24 hours; satisfaction guaranteed)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"When an order is late, what do you offer: a refund, store credit, or a reship? We''ll put your exact answer in the (WHAT WE OFFER) spot.\nIs the best way to reach you email, DMs, or the site chat?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"ordered 2 weeks ago and still nothing  do I just get my money back or what\""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"If your order is late, I want to hear about it. Here''s exactly what to do.\n[Point at the comment.]\nIn the US, shipping is 3 to 6 business days.\nIf it''s been longer than that, something went wrong. And that''s on us to fix, not on you to chase.\n[Count on your fingers.]\nOne. Message us with your order number.\nTwo. We reply Monday to Friday, 8am to 8:30pm, usually within 24 hours.\nThree. (WHAT WE OFFER).\nDon''t sit there waiting. Message us."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: late order? Message us with your order number. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'what''s actually in the sea salt spray?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 31K views: \"Replying to @basedkaifanaccount we don''t mind inspiring other brands bro\" Comment-reply format: the comment on screen, you answer straight to the camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Dead Sea and Himalayan salts, sea silt mineral water, sorbitan olivate decyl glucoside crosspolymer chosen over synthetic film-formers (Master Client Context Document, product table and domain expertise); salt gives texture, not hold, hold comes from a polymer, yours is olive and sugar derived (your own video \"I hear you guys\", 7675851037894364429)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Is the sea salt spray out now? If yes, where can people buy it (site, TikTok Shop, Amazon)? If not, what can we say about timing without giving a date?\nIs this ingredient list final, and is \"sea silt mineral water\" the wording you want on camera?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"ok but what''s actually IN the sea salt spray  just salt and water??\""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"[Hold the sea salt spray bottle up to the camera.]\nSalt and water? Close. But not even half of it.\nTwo salts: Dead Sea salt and Himalayan salt.\nThen sea silt mineral water.\nBut here''s the thing. Salt gives you texture. It doesn''t give you hold.\nThe hold comes from a polymer. Ours is called sorbitan olivate decyl glucoside crosspolymer.\nLong name. It''s made from olive and sugar.\nWe picked it over synthetic film-formers on purpose, so your styler isn''t sitting in your hair wash after wash.\n(LAUNCH STATUS: for example \"It''s live on our site now\" or \"Comment ''salt'' and we''ll let you know when it''s out\")"},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: two salts, sea silt mineral water and an olive and sugar polymer. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'you need to stop using texture powder?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@_cutzbymc/video/7440532397789154591"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from nounnaturals.com Glacial Clay Texture Powder page (dry hair, 2 to 3 sprays from about 2 inches)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Before you quit texture powder, check how you use it. dry hair, 2 to 3 sprays from about 2 inches. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'why our formulas skip film-formers', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 34K views Your own short call-out talking head about what is really behind a feeling on your hair (greenwashing call-out on a \"natural\" conditioner)."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"salt gives texture, not hold; brands add a polymer to hold the style; you chose an olive and sugar derived one (your own video \"I hear you guys\", 7675851037894364429); you reject synthetic film-formers that build up and chose sorbitan olivate decyl glucoside crosspolymer for the sea salt spray (Master Client Context Document, industry practice and domain expertise)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Say this straight to the camera like the reference: short, direct, with a styling spray in your hand. Turn the bottle around when you get to the label part."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Do you want to name one or two synthetic film-formers people will see on labels? If yes, which ones?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"[Hold a styling spray up to the camera.]\nThe salt in your sea salt spray is not what''s holding your hair.\nSalt gives you texture. It doesn''t give you hold.\nThe hold comes from a polymer. An ingredient that coats your hair and keeps the style in place. That''s a film-former.\nA lot of the ones out there are synthetic. And some of them stay in your hair wash after wash.\nThat''s the part we didn''t want.\nSo for our sea salt spray, we went with sorbitan olivate decyl glucoside crosspolymer. It comes from olive and sugar.\n[Turn the bottle around and point at the ingredient list.]\nNext time you buy a styler, flip it over and find the ingredient doing the holding. Drop it in the comments and we''ll tell you what it is."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"The salt isn''t what holds your hair. Here''s what does. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'natural doesn''t work? not anymore', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@pyrosso/video/7558152996270443790"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from David, Oct 6 call, 17:11 (natural products do work now; new extraction methods that were not available when Noun started)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Natural products don''t work? That was the old story. Extraction has changed. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'what happens before a product launches', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 116K views: \"Stick to being a Tik Tok barber if you''re going to cheap out on formulas\" Your own quick, confident talking head to the camera (used in Week 1 as a numbered tip: \"One... two... three\")."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"\"a lab, a stability test, a patch test\" for every formula; RIPT supports skin tolerance only; claim only what can be backed, test first then claim; a formula that fails EU rules is out even if it works in the US; R&D in-house, formulation with chemists and contract manufacturer partners (Master Client Context Document, professional philosophy and operating principles); loyal customers get raw samples straight from the lab before you decide whether to launch (David, Oct 5 call, 32:00)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Talk straight to the camera like the reference: quick, confident, one step at a time. Hold up a finger for each number."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Can we say that every Noun formula goes through a stability test and a patch test (RIPT)? If only some do, which ones?\nIs it OK to mention on camera that loyal customers get lab samples before launch?"},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Here''s everything a Noun formula has to get through before you can buy it.\n[Hold up one finger.]\nOne. The lab. We develop it in-house with our chemists and manufacturing partners.\n[Hold up two fingers.]\nTwo. A stability test.\n[Hold up three fingers.]\nThree. A patch test. That tells us how skin tolerates it. That''s all it tells us, so that''s all we''ll ever say about it.\n[Hold up four fingers.]\nFour. The rules. If a formula fails EU rules, it''s out. Even if it would pass in the US.\n[Hold up five fingers.]\nFive. Real people. Some of our loyal customers get raw samples straight from the lab before we even decide to launch.\nAnd anything we claim on the bottle? We test it first. Then we say it. Never the other way around.\nSo when a drop takes longer than you want, this is where the time goes."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Five things every formula has to get through before it reaches you. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, '3 things i never do to my hair', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcjbNp_hfYn/"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; the caption states no product facts."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Three things to never do to your hair. What would you add? #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'we talk like you in the comments on purpose', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 67K views: \"W friend group, thx boys for showing love\" Your own community video, straight to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Steven: the audience comes through TikTok content and comments, you use the humor and slang of middle school and high school kids because you still understand how they talk, they see you in your content and on lives, Oct 5 call, 20:00."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Who should record this one, Khaled or Steven? Steven described how you talk to followers in the comments on the Oct 5 call."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We took one of your videos that performed really well, which shows that the format works, and wrote a new script in the same style. Record it straight to the camera, relaxed, the way you talk on your lives."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"Why does a hair brand reply in the comments like it''s in high school? Because a lot of you are.\nA lot of you found us through our TikToks. And a lot of you are in middle school or high school.\nSo when we answer you in the comments, we talk the way you talk. Your jokes. Your slang.\nIt''s not an act. We still get how you talk.\nAnd it doesn''t stop in the comments. You see us the same way in our videos and on our lives.\nSo keep the comments coming. Ask us anything about your hair, in your own words. We''ll answer."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Ask us anything. We''ll answer in your language. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'are you over-oiling your scalp?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@afsennah/video/7388405776911502624"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from nounnaturals.com hair oil page (2 to 5 drops on mid-lengths and ends)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"2 to 5 drops on your mid-lengths and ends. That''s enough. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'do you ship to the uk?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, comment reply Your own comment-reply format: comment on screen, answer to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (DTC orders ship to the UK, EU and GCC through Shopify Markets Pro; Canada is in the active market list); nounnaturals.com shipping info (worldwide DHL Express, 2 to 4 business days)."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Does free shipping over $50 also apply to orders from the UK, Europe, the Gulf and Canada? If yes, we will add one line about it."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"do y''all ship to the UK?? or Dubai  you keep coming up on my fyp\""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Yes. You don''t have to live in the US to get Noun.\nOur website ships to the UK, to Europe and to the Gulf. Canada too.\nOutside the US, your order goes out with DHL Express. Two to four business days.\nOrder on nounnaturals.com and it comes straight to you.\nNow tell me in the comments: where are you watching from?"},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: UK, Europe, the Gulf, Canada. Yes, we ship to you. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'does hair oiling make your hair grow?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@sofiahairhealth/video/7428670158438157601"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from nounnaturals.com hair oil page (not a medical hair-loss treatment; scalp massage before washing; scalp treatment 2 to 3 times a week)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Hair oil is not a hair-loss treatment. For your scalp: massage it in before you wash, 2 to 3 times a week. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'natural in 2018 vs natural now', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 79K views: \"Exposing the misinformation on this app has other brands thinking before they post now (finally)\" Your own founder video to camera: bold opening statement, short story, then the turn \"Now, why am I telling you this?\" and the point."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document: in 2018 natural brands \"had to compromise on performance\" and natural innovation is now \"overwhelming\" (section 5.1); started in 2018 at 18, hand-making products in his basement; belief \"natural, high performing, long term hair and scalp health\"; conditioner uses a plant-derived conditioning ingredient (AminoSensyl HC); nounnaturals.com conditioner page (quat-free)."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Do you want to add one example of a natural ingredient or method you can use now that natural brands didn''t have in 2018? We can add it as one line after \"overwhelming\"."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this straight to the camera, the same way as in the reference: open with the bold statement, tell the short story, then turn to the viewer with \"Now, why am I telling you this?\" Hold up the conditioner when you talk about it."},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"When I started Noun in 2018, natural hair care came with a catch. It didn''t perform as well.\nNatural brands back then had to compromise on performance. That was the deal.\nI was eighteen, making products by hand in my basement.\nNow, why am I telling you this?\nBecause a lot of you still think natural means weaker. That''s 2018 thinking.\nNatural innovation right now is overwhelming.\n[Hold the conditioner up to the camera.]\nOur conditioner is quat-free. It conditions with a plant-derived ingredient instead.\nNatural and high performing. That''s the standard now."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Natural in 2018 vs natural now. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'does the conditioner detangle?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 59K views: \"4 ounces that will last you 4-6 months\" Your own comment-reply format: comment on screen, answer to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document (Jul 2026: a repeat customer on his twelfth order praised detangling; \"detangling found us\"; detangling moved into consumer testing and is not yet a claim; quat-free conditioner with AminoSensyl HC; claims follow evidence); nounnaturals.com conditioner page (quat-free, for every hair type)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Is the detangling consumer test still running? If it''s done, what can we say now?\nOK to mention the twelfth-order customer (no name)?"},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"does the conditioner detangle?? my brush gets stuck every single time \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"Honest answer? We''re not allowed to say yes yet.\n[Hold the conditioner up to the camera.]\nA customer on his twelfth order told us the detangling is the best part.\nWe didn''t put it on the label.\nWe put it into consumer testing.\nBecause here, a claim comes after the proof. Not before.\nWhat I can tell you today: it''s quat-free, and it''s made for every hair type.\nThe test results decide what we say next.\nTry it and tell me in the comments what you notice."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Proof first, claims second. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'i build our own software', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 79K views: \"Exposing the misinformation on this app has other brands thinking before they post now (finally)\" Your own founder video to camera: bold opening statement, short story, then the turn \"Now, why am I telling you this?\" and the point."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"Master Client Context Document: Khaled built an ops platform, a PLM and an ERP with Claude Code and Replit; builds internal software to own the data; hands-on across formulation, packaging, finance, legal and software."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"OK to share this on camera?\nOK to name Claude Code and Replit, or should we just say \"AI coding tools\"?\nWould you show a screen from one of the tools in a follow-up video? If not, we''ll change the last line."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record this straight to the camera, the same way as in the reference: open with the bold statement, list what you built, then turn to the viewer with \"Now, why am I telling you this?\""},{"heading":"SCRIPT","text":"I run a hair care brand. And I build our software myself.\nOur ops platform. Our ERP. A PLM for our products.\nI built them with Claude Code and Replit.\nNow, why am I telling you this?\nBecause at Noun I''m hands-on with everything. Formulation. Packaging. Finance. Legal. And software.\nWhen we build our own tools, we own our data.\nWant to see what I built? Tell me in the comments."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"Hair care founder. Also building our own software. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'how to put texture powder on', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@choppedbystev0/video/7676669473587285278"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from nounnaturals.com texture powder page (dry hair, 2 to 3 sprays from about 2 inches, matte all day)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"On dry hair, about 2 inches away, 2 to 3 sprays. Matte all day. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'best and worst shampoos at walmart', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 62K views"},{"heading":"React to this video:","text":"https://www.tiktok.com/@greyfro4u/video/7683586100404800781"},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"the react video itself; caption facts from nounnaturals.com shampoo page (INCI: decyl glucoside, lauryl glucoside)."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"Record your thoughts on this video as shown in the reference."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"What''s in yours? Ours cleans with decyl glucoside and lauryl glucoside. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('noun', 4, 'are you making deodorant?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"@nounnaturals, 59K views: \"4 ounces that will last you 4-6 months\" Your own comment-reply format: comment on screen, answer to camera."},{"heading":"Facts from:","text":"David: before the rebrand Noun sold hair, body and beard care and is relaunching those categories, Oct 5 call, 3:51; rebrand to Noun Naturals in 2021 (Master Client Context Document); new deodorant, balm and texture lines target 95% natural content, minimum 70% naturally derived (Master Client Context Document)."},{"heading":"Questions for you (a short voice note is perfect):","text":"Can we say on camera that a deodorant is in development?\nIs it OK to share the target (95% natural content, at least 70% naturally derived) publicly?\nIs there anything else in body care we can name? No dates needed."},{"heading":"NOTES FOR THE CLIENT","text":"We can create custom TikTok-style comments with any questions we want using Canva or CapCut, then add them to videos so you can respond to them. These will look like real comments but won''t be clickable."},{"heading":"Possible comment:","text":"\"y''all ever gonna make deodorant or body stuff?? i want natural for more than just my hair \""},{"heading":"Your answer:","text":"We''re working on it. And it has a standard to hit first.\nNoun didn''t start as only hair care. Before our rebrand in 2021, we sold body care and beard care too. Now we''re bringing those categories back.\nA new deodorant is one of them.\nHere''s the bar it has to clear: 95% natural content, and at least 70% naturally derived. Same standard as our new balm and texture products.\nNo date yet. Follow us so you catch it when it drops."},{"heading":"CAPTION","text":"In reply to your comment: Body care is coming back. Deodorant included. #noun #nounnaturals"}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, 'why i started noun', 1, '[{"heading":"Goal:","text":"show people you had the problem yourself before you built the solution."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"So I started a hair brand because I was losing my own hair. Kind of ironic, right?"},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"I was 17 and my hair was thinning.\nNothing in the market worked, so I went back to what my family has used for generations."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"What you tried from the market and why nothing helped.\nWhat those brands were really selling: a nice smell and a quick fix, nothing for the scalp."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"What you grew up with: olive oil, black seed oil.\nHot oil treatments three times a week.\nYou posted it on YouTube in 2017, it blew up, people kept asking what you were using.\nYou bottled it and called it Habibi Oil."},{"heading":"PAYOFF","text":"Why Noun is still about long-term hair and scalp health, while most brands still sell quick fixes."},{"heading":"CTA","text":"Follow for the rest of the story of how Noun was built, I''ll break it down in the following videos."}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, 'real or slop?', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"Watch the reference"},{"heading":"Goal:","text":"rate industry practices fast. For each one, answer \"real\" or \"slop\" and say why in one sentence."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"Alright, I own a hair care brand, so let''s do this. Real or slop? Go."},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"Some of these are why I built my brand the way I did.\nOthers are why you can''t trust what you see on TikTok."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"The industry is full of slop and most people can''t tell the difference anymore."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"Celebrity hair brands\nBefore and after videos on TikTok\n\"Dermatologist recommended\" on the bottle\nClean and non-toxic labels\nFounders posting their $1M month\nBrands that show the % of their ingredients\nSalon-only products"}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, 'the 0.5% label trick', 1, '[{"heading":"Goal:","text":"expose how brands put an ingredient on the label without enough of it to work."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"Your shampoo label is lying to you"},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"There''s a trick a lot of brands use, and you''d never notice it.\nOnce you see it, you''ll start seeing it everywhere."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"An ingredient needs a certain % to actually work.\nBrands put in a fraction of it so they can print it on the label."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"Why they do it: cost and marketing.\nWhat you do instead: whatever is on your label is in the product at the dose it needs, even if the ingredient costs $2,000 and has to go in at 10%.\nHow a regular person can tell if a product is doing this."},{"heading":"PAYOFF","text":"You''d rather lose margin than lie on a label."},{"heading":"CTA","text":"Comment a product you want us to look into."}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, 'hair care scams you''re still paying for', 1, '[{"heading":"Goal:","text":"list the biggest scams in hair care one by one, with one reason each from your experience."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"Let''s talk about the hair care scams you''re probably still paying for"},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"Some of these are so normal now that people don''t even notice them.\nI built my brand by refusing to do them."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"Why these work on people: good packaging, influencers, big promises."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"Hero ingredients at a fraction of the dose they need\nBefore and afters from paid affiliates who never used the product\nNatural on the front, a different story on the back\nGrow your hair in 30 days promises\nWhite label products sold as a founder''s own formula"},{"heading":"PAYOFF","text":"If a brand needs a trick to sell it, the product isn''t doing the work."}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, '$350, my parents'' basement and my sisters shipping orders', 1, '[{"heading":"Goal:","text":"show how you started from nothing, with your family behind you."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"If a hair brand needs millions in ads to sell, the product probably sucks. I started mine with $350 in my parents'' basement."},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"I was a college freshman.\nNo investors, no factory, just my parents'' basement."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"What your life looked like then: college, sales job at AT&T, no money to start a brand."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"The flask, the measuring cup and the oils you bought on Amazon.\nYour dad''s credit card paid for Shopify. Website went live in February 2018.\nEvery weekend you came home to make product in the basement. Your sisters shipped orders during the week.\nYour dad was one of your first investors."},{"heading":"PAYOFF","text":"Today brands launch with a white-label formula and an ad budget. You started by making every bottle yourself, and that''s still how you think about the product."}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, 'do not trust most hair oils on the shelf', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"Watch the reference"},{"heading":"Goal:","text":"de-influence the hair oils people buy on autopilot and show what a real hair oil should be."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"Don''t trust most of the hair oils on the shelf. I genuinely don''t want you to waste your money."},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"My brand started with one hair oil I made in my parents'' basement.\nI''m on a mission to clean up this industry, and today we need to talk about what''s really in the oil you''re using."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"Why hair oils blew up: everyone''s oiling now, and brands jumped on it."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"What a lot of shelf oils are actually made of.\nWhat the word \"oil\" on the label can hide.\nHow to tell a good hair oil from a bad one."},{"heading":"PAYOFF","text":"An oil should feed your scalp, not just make your hair shine for a day."}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, 'why we went quiet for a year', 1, '[{"heading":"Goal:","text":"show the decision that cost you growth but protected the product."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"Most brands would''ve cheapened the formula. I went quiet for a year instead to make it perfect."},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"We slowed our content down for about a year.\nCompetitors took market share, and I let them."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"The supply chain broke, you couldn''t get certain ingredients on time.\nThe easy option: swap in cheaper ingredients and keep shipping 5,000 orders.\nWhat a lot of brands do when this happens: quietly change the formula and keep the same label."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"What you chose: fix the supply chain and the product first.\nWhat it cost: competitors with the same supply problems kept selling a worse product and grabbed market share.\nWhat you rebuilt so it never breaks again."},{"heading":"PAYOFF","text":"Most brands would have cheapened it. Customers buy because of the formula, and you won''t trade it to win a quarter."},{"heading":"CTA","text":"Follow if you want brands to work like this."}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, 'why our bottles are small', 1, '[{"heading":"Goal:","text":"answer why your bottles are small by showing what''s really inside the big ones."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"People keep asking me why our bottles are so small. Honestly? Because I''m not selling you water."},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"Big bottles are one of the oldest tricks in hair care.\nThey look like a better deal, and that''s the whole point."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"What''s actually filling most big bottles: water, cheap fillers and a tiny bit of what works.\nWhy brands do it: a bigger bottle feels like more value and costs them almost nothing."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"What''s in your bottle instead, and why it''s this size.\nHow long one bottle actually lasts compared to a big one.\nWhat people really pay for with the big ones: packaging and marketing."},{"heading":"PAYOFF","text":"A bigger bottle doesn''t mean more product. It usually means more filler."},{"heading":"CTA","text":"Check the first ingredient on your shampoo and tell me what it is."}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, 'my dad built every house like he''d live in it', 1, '[{"heading":"Goal:","text":"show where your moral code comes from."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"If my dad built houses the way most brands make shampoo, every one of them would''ve fallen apart."},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"Everything about how I run Noun comes from watching him.\nOne rule in particular."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"Growing up in Clifton, New Jersey, the only boy with four sisters.\nYour dad working 13 to 14 hour days building homes."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"His rule: build every house like it''s your own, your reputation is on the line.\nHe wanted you to get the education he never had.\nYou took his rule into Noun: make every product like your own family uses it.\nMost brands do the opposite: build it cheap, sell it fast, move on to the next launch."},{"heading":"PAYOFF","text":"What you want your customers to say about you."}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, 'this shampoo looks natural. read the back', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"Watch the reference"},{"heading":"Goal:","text":"take a shampoo that looks clean and natural and show what''s actually in the ingredient list."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"Okay, this is the perfect example of how hair care brands trick you. Look at this bottle."},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"At first glance you''d think this is a healthy shampoo.\nIt has all the right buzzwords and the green packaging."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"The words on the front of the bottle and the colors that make it feel pure."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"The ingredient list from the back.\nWhich ingredients don''t match what the front promises, and why.\nWhat a clean formula actually looks like."},{"heading":"PAYOFF","text":"The front of the bottle is marketing. The back is what you put on your scalp."}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, 'founder content turned into a car show', 1, '[{"heading":"Goal:","text":"separate yourself from flashy founder content and set the tone for your page."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"Just so you know, you''re not gonna see me flexing a Bugatti on this page."},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"Founder content turned into a car show.\nThis page will be different."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"What founder content looks like now: Bugattis, desks, Shopify dashboard screenshots, then selling a course."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"Why it''s empty: people faking being founders, no moral code behind what they sell.\nWho you are: you find solutions to problems, 8 years in this industry.\nWhat this page will be: how the brand gets built, honestly."},{"heading":"PAYOFF","text":"It''s not always about the money."},{"heading":"CTA","text":"Follow to see how a brand actually gets built."}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, 'this viral hair product probably won''t grow your hair', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"Watch the reference"},{"heading":"Goal:","text":"pick a viral hair product people buy for hair growth and break down why it probably won''t do what they expect."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"I mean this disrespectfully, but [viral product] is probably not going to grow your hair."},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"I started losing my hair at 17, so I know what it''s like to wait for something to work.\nIf you''ve been using it religiously and waiting for your hairline to fill in, we need to talk."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"The before and afters go crazy.\nWhat the product actually says it does on the label, compared to what people think it does."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"The hero ingredient and what it actually does.\nHow much of it is in there and whether that''s enough to work.\nWhat someone with thinning hair should look for instead."}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, 'customers who''ve been with us since 2018', 1, '[{"heading":"Goal:","text":"prove the brand through customer loyalty, not revenue screenshots."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"Funny thing is, some of my customers have no idea who I am. And they''ve been buying from us since 2018."},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"They don''t come back for me, they come back for the product.\nThat matters more to me than any revenue screenshot."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"Companies you''ve watched hit $20 million and fail the next year because they chased marketing.\nBrands that buy every first order with affiliates and ads, then never see that customer again."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"Subscribers since 2018 and 2019 who come back for the product, not for the founder.\nWhat actually keeps a brand alive: the relationship between the customer and the product."},{"heading":"PAYOFF","text":"Why you''d rather have loyal customers than fast revenue."},{"heading":"CTA","text":"If you''ve been with us a long time, tell me in the comments when you started."}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, '$100 billion a year on hair care. most of it doesn''t work', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"Watch the reference"},{"heading":"Goal:","text":"show people how big the hair care industry is and how much of that money goes to products that don''t work."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"Okay, this number should honestly make you uncomfortable. People spend over 100 billion dollars a year on hair care."},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"And a lot of it is going to products that were never built to work.\nI''ve watched brands make $20 million and disappear the next year."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"Most products are a logo on a white-label formula.\nActive ingredients go in at a fraction of the dose so they can be printed on the label."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"Brands spend on affiliates and marketing instead of the formula.\nA lot of products fix the look of your hair for a day, not your scalp long term.\nWhat you do differently: the dose on the label is the dose in the bottle."}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, 'my first order came from a stranger in maryland', 1, '[{"heading":"Goal:","text":"share the moment you realized the brand could actually work."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"My first customer wasn''t an influencer I paid. Most hair brands can''t say that anymore."},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"I was 18, making everything in my parents'' basement.\nAnd that one order changed how I saw everything."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"Before the website, only friends were buying from you.\nAt 18 you didn''t know if anyone else would pay."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"February 2018: first Shopify order from someone in Maryland who didn''t know you.\nIf you can sell one bottle, you can sell two.\nOne of the early Shopify stores, top 1% for a while.\nLast year you sent him free product to say thanks."},{"heading":"PAYOFF","text":"What that first order meant to you."}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, 'real or fraud: hair care trends rated by a founder', 1, '[{"heading":"Reference:","text":"Watch the reference"},{"heading":"Goal:","text":"rate popular hair care products and trends one by one. Say \"real\" or \"fraud\" and give one reason from your experience."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"Let''s go through the viral hair trends everyone''s buying right now. Real or fraud?"},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"TikTok sells a new hair fix every week, and most people can''t tell which ones work."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"Rosemary oil for hair loss\nMicrofiber towels\nSilk or satin bonnets\nHot oil treatments\nHair growth shampoos\nSulfate-free shampoo\nScalp massagers\nWashing your hair every day"}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, 'i''d pay $2,000 for one ingredient', 1, '[{"heading":"Goal:","text":"show what you''re willing to pay so the product does what the label says."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"There''s one ingredient in our formula that costs me $2,000. And I''m still not taking it out."},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"Most brands would cut it.\nOur suppliers say they''re not used to working with someone like us."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"How the industry cuts costs on the ingredients that actually do the work.\nBrands that swap the expensive ingredient for a cheaper one and keep the same label."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"The ingredient that costs $2,000 and goes in at 10%, because it''s on the label.\nPartners and suppliers work with you because you''re honest.\nIf someone gives you $30 for a product, it has to be the most valuable product they can buy for that."},{"heading":"PAYOFF","text":"The moral code is part of the brand DNA."},{"heading":"CTA","text":"Follow for more on what goes into our products."}]'::jsonb),
  ('founder', 1, 'how my faith runs my business', 1, '[{"heading":"Goal:","text":"share the values behind how you run Noun, as much as you''re comfortable with."},{"heading":"HOOK","text":"I grew up with one rule about money: you don''t feed your family with dirty money."},{"heading":"RETAIN","text":"I grew up with this rule.\nIt decides how I run Noun."},{"heading":"BUILD-UP","text":"What dirty money means to you.\nHow much of this industry makes exactly that kind of money: selling products they know don''t work."},{"heading":"REWARD","text":"How your faith gives you a moral code for business and how to treat people.\nHard decisions: you leave them in God''s hands.\nGiving back once you make money."},{"heading":"PAYOFF","text":"Honest intention shows up in the business."},{"heading":"CTA","text":"Follow for more on how I build Noun."}]'::jsonb)
),
weeks_in as (
  -- a week number that two live weeks of one space share is skipped, so no script lands in the wrong week
  select w.id, w.space_id, w.starts_on, s.slug as space_slug, n.week_no, count(*) over (partition by s.id, n.week_no) as same_no
    from public.weeks w
    join public.spaces s on s.id = w.space_id and s.deleted_at is null
    cross join lateral (
      select coalesce(w.number, nullif(substring(w.name from '(?i)^\s*week\s*(\d{1,6})'), '')::int) as week_no
    ) n
   where w.deleted_at is null
),
cards_in as (
  select c.id, wi.space_slug, wi.week_no, lower(regexp_replace(btrim(c.title), '\s+', ' ', 'g')) as title,
         row_number() over (partition by c.week_id, lower(regexp_replace(btrim(c.title), '\s+', ' ', 'g')) order by c.sort_order, c.id) as ord
    from public.cards c
    join weeks_in wi on wi.id = c.week_id and wi.same_no = 1
   where c.deleted_at is null
     -- the card write rule re-checks these on every update; a card that would fail it is left alone, so the file never stops
     and c.space_id = wi.space_id
     and (c.planned_on is null or c.planned_on between wi.starts_on and wi.starts_on + 6)
)
update public.cards c
   set script_sections = src.sections
  from src
  join cards_in ci
    on ci.space_slug = src.space_slug and ci.week_no = src.week_no and ci.title = src.title and ci.ord = src.ord
 where c.id = ci.id
   and c.script_sections = '[]'::jsonb;
